window.CULTIVATION_CHAPTERS=(window.CULTIVATION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2601,"title":"Chapter 2601: Gaia’s Heaven","paragraphs":["\"Let me get this straight...\"","After a moment of silence, Mei Feng spoke with a dumbfounded look on her face.","\"The reason you want to go outside the city alone is so that you can clean up the Void Specters? Do you really expect me to believe that? I cannot see its purpose or how it benefits you.\"","\"Well, to put things plainly, I get stronger through defeating these Void Specters,\" Yuan revealed the truth to her without revealing too many details.","Mei Feng raised an eyebrow at his statement and replied, \"This is the first time I’ve heard such a thing. We’ve been cleaning Void Specters for generations, but nobody has ever gotten stronger from doing so. There’s a reason why they’re considered trash, you know?\"","\"One man’s trash is another’s treasure,\" Yuan responded with a smile on his face. \"Also, in case you forgot, I am not from this world, so things work differently for me.\"","\"...\"","Mei Feng rubbed her eyes and sighed, \"Regardless, I cannot allow you to leave the city alone, especially when you are still a mere Corporal. I have already given you too many exemptions. As much as I want to support you, I am a General, and I cannot give you too much favoritism. If you want to go outside alone, then keep on doing missions, build up your reputation, and increase your rank.\"","\"How long does it usually take to be promoted to Sergeant?\" Yuan asked.","\"There’s no set amount of time,\" she replied. \"Most soldiers never advance beyond Corporal, since Sergeants are considered elite. To become one, you’ll need to accumulate enough achievements and merit by completing missions. But if you want an example, then the quickest anyone has ever been promoted to the rank of Sergeant from Corporal is three years.\"","\"Three years, huh?\" Yuan mumbled, relieved that it wasn’t too ridiculously long.","\"Then how do I go about joining cleanup missions without coming to you? I don’t want to bother you too often, after all.\"","\"Just go to the mission hall. You can ask about missions and even request them there.\"","\"Alright. Thanks.\"","\"From now on, unless you really need my assistance, refrain from coming here. I can’t have a Corporal coming to me for every little issue,\" she said a moment later.","\"I understand.\"","Yuan left shortly after.","\"Well? What did the General say? Can you go outside by yourself?\" Sergeant Bing asked.","\"No. She said it’s too early—that I should do more missions and increase my rank before she reconsiders it.\"","\"That’s to be expected,\" said Sergeant Quang. \"Not only did you just join the military, but you’re just a Corporal. Hell, not even Sergeants are allowed to leave the city alone.\"","\"Where is the mission hall?\" Yuan then asked.","\"We’ll take you there.\"","Some time later, Yuan arrived at the mission hall.","\"There are a lot of people here,\" Yuan remarked after entering the building to see thousands of soldiers present.","\"If a soldier isn’t resting or training, they will be here to look for missions.\"","\"How does this place work?\" Yuan asked.","\"You see those capsules over there?\" Sergeant Bing pointed at the rows of machines at the end of the room where most of the soldiers in this place were gathered, most of them seemingly waiting for their turn.","\"Once you enter the capsule, you can see all of the missions that are available to you, or request to join others’ missions.\"","\"What sort of missions are typically available?\"","\"That depends on your rank, but as a Corporal, you should have a good number of them unlocked.\"","\"Alright.\"","Yuan went to queue up for the machine shortly after.","While he waited, Yuan looked around and noticed that the majority of soldiers present were ranked between Private First Class and Corporal.","\"Hey, isn’t that the guy who fought a Captain during the recent recruitment?\"","\"You’re right! And look at his insignia! He’s already a Corporal!\"","It didn’t take long before some of the soldiers there noticed and recognized Yuan.","\"That’s the guy who broke all of the previous records? He doesn’t look that capable.\"","Eventually, a few of them approached Yuan and asked him, \"Which family are you from?\"","\"I don’t have one,\" Yuan calmly replied.","\"What? Surely, you must be joking.\"","\"What makes you think that?\" Yuan asked.","\"There’s no way you could’ve broken all of those records without the help of your family!\"","Yuan shrugged. \"Then I don’t know what else to tell you.\"","\"He obviously wants to keep it a secret, just like the Ironwoman.\"","\"Right? I bet he comes from the same background as that woman.\"","\"What if he’s that woman’s brother?\"","\"Is that true? Are you the Ironwoman’s brother?\"","\"No...\"","Since he had nothing to do in line, Yuan decided to chat with these soldiers, even though most of them were just questioning his background.","Eventually, it was his turn to use the machine.","Once inside, a notification appeared.","<Welcome to the Mission Board, Corporal Yuan>","\"Let me see what mission is available to me.\"","<Checking the user’s credentials>","<You are allowed to accept missions up to the rank of Sergeant>","<Listing all available missions in 3...2...1...>","A moment later, a list of missions appeared before Yuan.","\"There are a lot fewer missions than I anticipated...\" Yuan mumbled after seeing only about thirty or so missions available.","[Mission: Gather Unknown Ore in the Orange Zone]","\"Unknown Ore? What is that?\"","He checked the mission details.","[Mission Details: Enter the Orange Zone and gather Unknown Ores]","[Rank Requirement: Corporal]","[Squad Requirement: 4]","However, there was no information on the Unknown Ores.","With no other choice, he decided to ask the others later and proceeded to check the other missions.","[Mission: Gather Unknown Crystal in the Red Zone]","[Rank Requirement: Sergeant]","[Squad Requirement: 6]","\"Unknown Crystal?\"","There were several other missions that required him to venture outside to gather items that he had no information on. Other than that, the rest of the missions were miscellaneous things, such as acting as a guard for individuals within the city.","\"Huh?\"","Yuan’s eyes widened with surprise when he noticed a certain mission.","[Mission: Escort individual to Spirit City]","[Rank Requirement: Sergeant]","[Squad Requirement: 4]","\"Spirit... City? There are other cities in this world?\"","This was the first time Yuan had heard of such a thing. In fact, he’d thought this was the only city in the world.","After taking a moment to digest this new information, Yuan went to look for the cleanup mission.","Although there were other missions that allowed him to venture outside the city, his main purpose was to kill Void Specters.","However, he couldn’t see the cleanup mission on the list of available missions.","\"Where are the cleanup missions?\" he asked.","<Cleanup missions are automatically assigned to soldiers>","\"Then how do I join one?\"","<You may request to join a squad with that mission>","\"Then send a request for me.\"","<What time frame?>","\"The sooner the better.\"","<Request has been sent>","<Request has been approved>","\"That was quick.\"","Yuan remarked, as the request was basically instantly approved.","[Mission Details: Cleanup Void Specters up to the Orange Zone. Meet at the Southern Gate at 0600 in 12 hours]","\"Tomorrow, huh? That’s great.\"","Yuan exited the machine shortly after.","\"When’s your next mission?\" Sergeant Bing asked when Yuan returned to them.","\"Tomorrow.\"","\"That fast, huh?\"","As they made their way back to the residential area, Yuan asked, \"What are Unknown Ores and Unknown Crystals?\"","\"They are important resources that can only be found in the Orange Zone and beyond. There are multiple uses for them, such as crafting weapons and Gaia Stones.\"","\"Is that so...\" Yuan mumbled, wondering if they were anything like Spirit Stones or treasures in his world.","\"Even if you aren’t on a mission to gather them, you should pick them up if you come across them, as you can exchange them for merits and money,\" Sergeant Quang said.","\"What do they look like?\"","\"You’ll know when you see one. You won’t miss them, either.\" Sergeant Bing replied. \"They stick out like a sore thumb against the barren landscape with their glistening appearance.\"","\"Unknown Ore or Unknown Crystal?\"","\"Both. Unknown Ores are much more common, though.\"","\"I’ll keep that in mind.\" Yuan nodded.","\"Also, am I right in assuming there are other cities besides this one? I saw a mission to escort someone to Spirit City. Is that a separate city, or just a place within this one?\"","Sergeant Bing and Sergeant Quang looked at him with one eyebrow raised, looking confused by his question.","\"You mean... you didn’t know there were other cities out there?\" Sergeant Bing eventually spoke.","\"...No,\" Yuan answered truthfully.","\"Well, do I have news for you.\"","Sergeant Quang chuckled. \"There are eight other cities besides this one, so there are nine cities in total.\"","Sergeant Bing added, \"Our city is called Gaia’s Heaven. We are also the largest city out there.\"","\"I’ll be damned...\" Yuan muttered in a somewhat dazed tone."]},{"number":2602,"title":"Chapter 2602: Third Mission","paragraphs":["\"How does one get to the other cities?\" Yuan asked after taking a moment to digest the new information.","\"There is a portal that can teleport between all of the cities. However, there is only one such portal, and it is heavily regulated by the military. Unless you’re from an influential or wealthy family, it’s nearly impossible to use it due to how much energy it consumes,\" Sergeant Quang explained.","\"In other words, if you want to travel to another city, you’ll need to go there on foot... or drive there, which requires you to go through the Black Zone,\" Sergeant Bing continued. \"But honestly, I don’t see a point in traveling to another city, especially given how dangerous it can be. We already have everything one can ask for in this city, too.\"","\"Are you trying to travel to another city?\" Sergeant Quang asked out of curiosity.","Yuan quickly shook his head.","\"No, I was just unaware of their existence until just now. I have no reason or intention of going to another city for now.\"","\"For now, huh?\"","\"Well, it’s not like I can predict the future.\"","Yuan continued, asking, \"What is in the other cities, anyway? How do they differ from this one?\"","\"I’ve never been to another city, so I cannot tell you.\"","\"Have you never encountered someone from a different city?\"","\"Nope. As mentioned earlier, only those incredibly influential and wealthy would travel between cities.\"","\"What about missions? I saw one earlier that involved escorting someone to Spirit City.\"","Sergeant Bing shook her head. \"Just because a mission is available doesn’t mean you qualify for it. Those missions offer the most merit, but they also have the strictest rules and highest requirements. Everyone must undergo a rigorous screening process before they’re even allowed to partake in it, and tens of thousands of soldiers apply each time.\"","\"The most merits, huh? So I should apply for these missions if I want to improve my rank the quickest,\" Yuan mumbled.","\"In theory, yes. However, whether you’ll be accepted or not is an entirely different story. Moreover, they don’t just look at your capabilities. Even if you’re more than qualified to take the mission, the subject of the mission has the final say, so if they don’t like you, they can still disqualify you.\"","\"What a pain in the ass.\"","\"That’s why I don’t even bother applying for those missions,\" Sergeant Bing sighed. \"Still, if you want to advance beyond Sergeant, taking part in them is almost a necessity. They give you the chance to build connections with influential and powerful people who may be able to help with your promotion.\"","\"I’ll keep that in mind.\"","Once they reached the residential area, Yuan asked them before heading into his living quarters, \"You’re not coming with me tomorrow, right?\"","Sergeant Quang replied, \"After seeing what you’re capable of during the last mission, I no longer have a reason to be concerned.\"","\"It was quite entertaining, and I wouldn’t mind accompanying you again, but I am a bit behind my training schedule,\" Sergeant Bing said.","\"Alright. Then I won’t wait for you guys tomorrow. See you later.\"","\"Stay safe.\"","The next day, Yuan showed up to the rendezvous at the Southern Gate in the morning at 0600. Of course, he brought along his minigun.","The other soldiers stared at Yuan with bewildered expressions, almost as if they couldn’t believe what they were seeing.","\"A Corporal...?\"","\"With a minigun...?\"","\"Are you pranking us?\"","Yuan replied with a calm smile, \"I can assure you that I am not messing around. In fact, I will even do all of the cleaning alone, so you just need to follow me and try to keep up.\"","\"What are you even talking about...?\"","\"Squad leader, he’s clearly fucking with us. Let’s just leave him behind and go.\"","\"Unfortunately, his name is on the list, and we cannot leave without him. It’s also too late to remove him,\" sighed the squad leader.","\"Whether I am messing with you or not will be clear once we leave the city walls,\" Yuan said.","\"Whatever... Just don’t get in our way.\"","They teleported to the top of the city walls shortly afterward.","The moment they jumped down the city walls and landed on the ground, Yuan started flying forward.","\"Try to keep up!\" he said to them.","\"T-This guy! He’s running off on his own!\"","\"Just forget about him. We’re already outside the city, anyway.\"","\"Even if you say that... I don’t want to make a report because we let him go and die off on his own.\"","\"...Fuck.\"","With no other choice, the soldiers quickly chased after Yuan.","\"Fuck! How fast is this guy moving?!\"","Even after chasing for hours, they still couldn’t catch up to Yuan, almost as if he’d vanished entirely.","\"What if he’s already dead?\"","\"Wait! I see him!\"","They caught up to Yuan because he’d come to a stop, arriving just in time to watch him gun down the Void Specters before him with his minigun. However, since there were just a few of them, none of the soldiers were impressed.","If anything, they were annoyed at him for running ahead.","\"H-Hey! He’s running off again!\"","Before any of them could even approach Yuan, he sped off immediately after defeating the Void Specters.","\"Don’t tell me he actually plans on dealing with all of the Void Specters by himself?!\"","\"Did you not see that big ass minigun he was carrying? There’s no way he’ll last longer than a day if he fights alone!\"","\"Not just that, but he’s only at the Fifth Ascension. I doubt he’ll last for even half a day.\"","\"Damn it... Where did such a reckless idiot come from? I knew something was weird when someone willingly joined us for our cleanup mission!\"","However, an entire day passed, and Yuan continued eliminating the Void Specters on his own without any trouble or slowing down.","\"What is going on?! How is he still going?! He should’ve exhausted himself long ago!\"","The soldiers following behind were left baffled by Yuan’s abnormal performance."]},{"number":2603,"title":"Chapter 2603: Cleaning Maniac","paragraphs":["Two days have passed since Yuan left the city and started cleaning up the Void Specters alone. The soldiers on the same mission and following behind had expected him to exhaust himself by the end of the first day. Yet, he showed no sign of slowing down even after two whole days.","\"This doesn’t make any sense! How is he still going after two days without rest?!\"","\"I haven’t seen him take even a sip of stamina potion, either.\"","\"Who’d be stupid enough to use potions for this sort of mission, anyway? Those things are incredibly expensive.\"","\"If he continues cleaning at this rate, we’ll be done by tomorrow, and these missions usually take at least a week.\"","Unbeknownst to these soldiers, Yuan had no intention of stopping the mission until they verbally asked him to stop. This meant that he continued cleaning past the Green Zone and into the Orange Zone, something most, if not all, soldiers refrain from doing.","After all, the mission only asked them to clean the Green Zone, and going above and beyond yielded no bonus merit. Unless there was something to gain, most would not even consider it.","\"Hey... Aren’t we past the Green Zone already?\"","Eventually, one of the soldiers realized this and asked aloud.","\"You’re right! Then why isn’t he stopping?\"","\"Maybe he doesn’t know?\"","\"Damn it!\"","\"Hey, Corporal! Stop! We’ve already gone past the Green Zone! There’s no need to keep on going because the mission is already complete!\" The squad leader shouted at Yuan, who was just preparing to speed off again.","Yuan stopped and turned to face them.","\"I am aware, but I want to keep on cleaning,\" he said calmly.","\"What? Why?\"","\"Just because,\" he shrugged.","\"Are you insane? There’s literally no point. We’re heading back,\" said one of the soldiers.","\"Alright.\" Yuan didn’t even try to argue.","Since completing missions faster meant earning merit more quickly, Yuan had no objections to returning to the city, as it still moved him closer to his goals. Of course, that didn’t mean he wouldn’t try to extend the mission again during future assignments.","\"Hey, how are you not tired after shooting that thing for days without rest? Even I can’t last longer than a few hours, and there’s no way you have more Limitless than me.\"","\"You won’t be able to replicate it even if I told you,\" Yuan replied.","\"And what makes you so sure?\"","\"I just am,\" he said, refusing to elaborate further.","After returning to the military base, Yuan immediately went back to the mission hall to grab another cleanup mission, repeating the process again and again.","In the blink of an eye, an entire month passed. During that time, Yuan participated in every cleanup mission he could, completing seven in total. He even managed to convince one of his squads to let him spend several days clearing Void Specters in the Orange Zone.","His highly unusual behavior quickly drew attention, and it wasn’t long before his name spread throughout the military, earning him the nickname \"Cleaning Maniac.\"","\"Have you heard? Some Corporal with a minigun has been going around volunteering for every cleanup mission he could.\"","\"Someone is actually willingly doing those missions? Why?\"","\"Who knows? But from what I’ve heard, he does all of the cleaning alone while the rest of his squad just quietly follows behind.\"","\"What? That sounds amazing! Where was he during my cleanup mission two months ago?\"","\"Apparently, he joined the military only a month ago.\"","\"Huh? And he’s already a Corporal?\"","\"Because he’s also the prodigy who broke every record during the last recruitment.\"","\"That’s the same person? What the hell is someone like him doing wasting his time on such pointless missions? If he wants to earn merit, there are plenty of other missions that offer far more!\"","\"You can never tell what a genius is thinking—especially one of his caliber.\"","It wasn’t just the ordinary soldiers who were baffled by Yuan’s actions, as even General Gu and the officers on his side were greatly puzzled by it.","\"What the hell is going on? Why is he doing this?\"","\"What if it’s actually General Mei’s orders?\"","\"That makes even less sense! Why would General Mei recruit someone like that just to keep sending him on cleanup missions? What a waste of his potential!\"","\"Regardless of his reason for doing it, isn’t this a good opportunity to get rid of him before he becomes too troublesome?\" Someone suddenly said.","\"You want to get rid of him while he is outside the city, where there is no surveillance?\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"It’s not like there is zero surveillance. Have you forgotten about Gaia’s System? It can tell if a soldier has purposefully killed another soldier.\"","\"We can just use a scapegoat.\"","As the officers openly discussed killing Yuan, General Gu remained silent, listening without interruption.","Eventually, he spoke. \"There’s no need for a scapegoat. According to those who’ve gone on missions with him, he always asks to venture farther than necessary—even into the Orange Zone. We can simply take advantage of that and let him go as far as he wants. The further he goes, the higher the chance an accident will occur. There is virtually no risk for our soldiers either since he also willingly does the cleanup alone.\"","\"The only problem is that we have to wait for him to be assigned to one of our squads,\" one of the officers said. \"That could take months—or even years if we’re unlucky—and there’s no telling how long he’ll keep up this charade.\"","\"I can handle that,\" another replied. \"I’ll be responsible for assigning cleanup missions next month. Still, to avoid making it too obvious, we’ll need to wait at least two months.\"","\"Then we’ll leave it in your hands, Captain Huang.\"","Meanwhile, Yuan continued taking on cleanup missions, completely unaware that he had already become the target of a conspiracy. Of course, even if he knew, he wouldn’t care. If anything, he’d probably welcome it."]},{"number":2604,"title":"Chapter 2604: Unknown Ore","paragraphs":["\"General Mei, are you making Corporal Yuan partake in the cleanup missions nonstop?\" one of her officers asked during a meeting.","\"What sort of question is that? Why would you think that?\" she asked with a puzzled face.","\"That’s just what the others have been saying.\"","\"I’ve also been hearing it,\" another replied. \"They claimed that you’re trying to assert dominance over the new recruit by forcing him to do these missions over and over again.\"","\"How stupid.\" Mei Feng sneered in disdain at such outrageous claims. \"Why would I even need to assert any dominance? It’s not like he’s being disobedient.\"","\"So it’s true that he’s willingly doing these cleanup missions himself? Why? While I am happy to see a soldier finally eager to do something that everyone else finds a chore, it’s a little concerning how eager he is...\"","\"Right? It’s literally all he does. Mission after mission. Without rest. It’s like he’s possessed or something.\"","\"General, shouldn’t we assign him something more fitting for someone called the upcoming Ironman?\" someone suddenly suggested.","\"Why?\"","\"I mean... we’ll become a laughingstock if someone so talented keeps on doing these cleanup missions...\"","\"Let them laugh. In case you forgot, Corporal Yuan joined just a little over a month ago. Do you remember what you were doing during your first year, let alone the first few months? Give him some time to adapt and familiarize himself with his new surroundings, and if he wants to spend all of his time doing cleanup missions, let him. It’s not like he’s harming anyone.\"","\"I agree with General Mei. We should give him some time... at least until those who joined at the same time as him finish their training.\"","\"So a year, huh? Fair enough.\"","Meanwhile, Yuan began his second month of cleanup missions.","As his name and reputation continued to spread, more and more soldiers were willing to let Yuan spend some time in the Orange Zone cleaning up Void Specters, which extended his time outside the city but at the cost of completing missions more slowly.","Time continued to pass swiftly, and in the blink of an eye, it was the start of Yuan’s third month in the military.","However, instead of going on a new cleanup mission after completing his last, Yuan went to the training area to see how much closer he got to defeating the enemy on the 46th floor.","\"Foolish mortal...\"","After several intense rounds later, Yuan sighed in defeat.","\"I knew it wasn’t much, but I didn’t think two months of absorbing the Void Specters’ Eternal Essence would only help me last a few seconds longer...\"","At this rate, he’d need to keep on doing cleanup missions for decades to have any noticeable results.","\"This won’t do. I will need to head further into the Red Zone, if not even deeper. However, I doubt they’ll agree to let me venture so far away from the city so soon...\"","He considered doing the gathering missions that would allow him to enter the Red Zones, but upon asking Sergeant Bing about it, he learned that attacking Void Specters during such missions was highly frowned upon since it was unnecessarily risky for everyone involved.","\"Guess I’ll give it another month and ask Mei Feng if I can go outside alone again. My reputation has risen quite significantly, and pretty much everyone is aware that I can handle the cleanup missions alone without issue.\"","With that in mind, Yuan started doing cleanup missions again.","\"So, just to be clear, we won’t be doing anything but following you, right?\" asked the squad leader.","\"That is indeed correct,\" Yuan confirmed.","\"I’ve heard a lot about you, Corporal Yuan. If you don’t mind me asking, is there a reason you prefer cleaning alone? I don’t want to feel like we’re taking advantage of you.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"Don’t worry, I am doing this of my own accord, and the reason I prefer doing it alone is simply that it’s much more efficient and faster.\"","Although the soldiers didn’t agree with Yuan’s statement, none of them complained because Yuan was going to do all of the work alone. After all, how could a single person clean more efficiently than a whole group of people?","Eventually, they reached the Orange Zone.","\"You mind if we spend a few days in the Orange Zone? I want to continue cleaning.\"","\"Only if you tell us why you’re so obsessed with cleaning.\"","\"Sure. It’s nothing crazy,\" Yuan said before giving them the same explanation he’d told everyone else. \"Cleaning Void Specters is soothing for me. It’s kind of like therapy.\"","\"Like therapy?\" The soldiers raised their eyebrows, looking puzzled by his unexpected response.","Despite their curiosity, none of them dared to question Yuan further, as they did not want to be disrespectful.","However, inside their minds, they wondered if Yuan’s parents were soldiers who died to Void Specters, hence his hatred and obsession to clean them.","\"A-Alright... If you want to enter the Orange Zone, go ahead...\"","\"Thanks.\"","A few days into cleaning in the Orange Zone, just as they were prepared to return to the city, Yuan noticed something that stopped him in his tracks.","\"Hm?\"","Not far away, something glinted in the distance.","\"Is that what I think it is?\" Yuan muttered as he walked toward it.","A few moments later, he bent down and picked up the object—a fist-sized, glistening stone.","\"Oh? You found an Unknown Ore? How lucky.\"","\"So this is an Unknown Ore, huh? This is my first time seeing one,\" he said.","\"They’re usually much further into the Orange Zone, so it’s pretty rare to find them in this area.\"","Yuan examined the Unknown Ore as they made their way back to the city.","’This thing... it contains Eternal Essence!’ Yuan’s eyes widened slightly after realizing this.","’And it’s not a small amount!’","The Unknown Ore in his hand contained enough Eternal Essence to rival that of a thousand Void Specters—roughly the number he usually wipes out during a single cleanup mission."]},{"number":2605,"title":"Chapter 2605: Unknown Ore(2)","paragraphs":["When they returned to the military base, one of the soldiers asked Yuan, \"Corporal, how long do you think you’ll continue doing these missions? I know you’re new to the military, but surely you won’t be doing this for the rest of your career, right?\"","Yuan chuckled, \"Of course not. I will stop doing these missions when I feel like I have done enough, which might be sooner than I originally anticipated.\"","\"Is that so? In any case, good luck, and thanks for doing the mission for us.\"","\"It’s been my pleasure.\"","After going their separate ways, Yuan made his way back to the residential area instead of the mission hall.","When he arrived, he saw Sergeant Quang coming out of his room.","\"Oh? I was about to head to the mission hall to find you,\" Sergeant Quang remarked.","Although Sergeant Quang and Sergeant Bing were still acting as Yuan’s bodyguard on base, they were no longer as strict and constantly following him around like watchdogs. Moreover, rather than both of them following Yuan simultaneously, they took turns, which was suggested by Yuan himself, allowing them to have more time to themselves.","\"Look what I found.\" Yuan retrieved the Unknown Ore he had discovered during the mission and showed it to Sergeant Quang.","\"How far into the Orange Zone did you go to find that?\"","Instead of celebrating Yuan’s find, Sergeant Quang looked concerned. The presence of an Unknown Ore suggested Yuan had ventured deep into the Orange Zone.","\"Not far at all. In fact, I ventured less than I usually do. According to the soldiers with me, I was just incredibly lucky.\"","\"In that case, they’re right. Unknown Ore is rarely found near the outskirts of the Orange Zone because we patrol those areas so frequently.\"","\"How do they even come into existence?\" Yuan suddenly asked.","\"Honestly, I don’t know, but most people just consider it nature’s gift.\"","\"I see...\"","\"Anyway, since you have an Unknown Ore, I guess you’ll want to turn it in for merit and money? I’ll bring you to the distribution center.\"","\"Actually, before we do that, I have a few questions. Do they do anything special to the Unknown Ore when you turn it in? For example, will they examine it?\"","Sergeant Quang raised an eyebrow at Yuan’s strange question and pondered for a moment before responding, \"Not that I know of. What is there to examine, anyway? Do you think people hand in fake Unknown Ores or something? These ores are impossible to fake—not that anyone would be stupid enough to do something like that in the first place since it’s a serious crime.\"","Yuan fell silent for a moment.","Then, without a word, silently absorbed all of the Eternal Essence in the Unknown Ore.","After absorbing all of its Eternal Essence, Yuan examined the Unknown Ore for any changes.","\"There’s no change!\" Yuan’s eyes widened.","To his surprise, the Unknown Ore showed no discernible change in its appearance even after losing all of its Eternal Essence.","He looked at Sergeant Quang and showed him the Unknown Ore again.","\"Notice anything different?\" he asked.","\"No...?\" Sergeant Quang answered, sounding uncertain, as he wondered if Yuan was asking him some kind of trick question.","\"Take a closer look.\" Yuan insisted, even handing the entire Unknown Ore to him.","After taking a good moment to examine the Unknown Ore, Sergeant Quang looked at Yuan and asked, \"Are you messing with me or something? Are you going to tell me that this isn’t an Unknown Ore but something else entirely?\"","\"Yes, I was just messing with you.\" Yuan chuckled as he retrieved the Unknown Ore. \"But it’s really an Unknown Ore.\"","\"...\"","\"Anyway, can you take me to the distribution center now?\"","\"Sure...\" Sergeant Quang sensed that something was off about Yuan, but he couldn’t quite put his finger on it.","Some time later, they arrived at the distribution center, and Yuan went to hand over the Unknown Ore despite having already absorbed all of its Eternal Essence.","’Even if they realize something is wrong with it, I can just say that I found it in that condition, and they have no prove that I’d done anything to it...’ Yuan chuckled inwardly.","Despite his questionable actions, Yuan didn’t mind all that much. It was only a single Unknown Ore, and while he still wasn’t certain whether this was a real world or merely an illusion, he leaned toward it being the latter, so he figured he might as well do a few unethical things.","\"One Unknown Ore, correct? Please place your hand on the machine, so I can credit you for your merits.\"","The worker accepted the Unknown Ore after a mere glance at it and gestured toward the machine before Yuan.","<You have received some merits>","<You have received 1,000 Gaia Credits>","After receiving the reward, Yuan calmly walked away, acting completely innocent with nothing to hide.","’So the money is distributed and used through the system too, huh?’ Yuan thought to himself after realizing that this was his first contact with this world’s currency.","’And since they seem to have no clue that I’d already absorbed the energy inside the Unknown Ore... I might as well stop doing cleanup missions and start going on the ones that focus on gathering them!’","However, just to be sure they didn’t notice the Unknown Ore’s drained Eternal Essence and couldn’t track him for it, Yuan continued doing cleanup missions for another two weeks.","\"Did you hear? The Cleaning Maniac has finally stopped doing cleanup missions!\"","\"No. Where did you hear that?\"","\"From my buddies who are scheduled for a gathering mission for Unknown Ores. He said that Corporal Yuan is on his team.\"","\"Oh, really? Did that weirdo finally get bored of Void Specters, or did he just realize there are better missions out there?\"","The news spread quickly, eventually reaching the ears of General Gu and General Mei. One was delighted by the news, while the other was furious."]},{"number":2606,"title":"Chapter 2606: Underwhelming Performance","paragraphs":["\"Corporal Yuan has finally accepted a mission that isn’t a cleanup mission? The universe must have heard my wishes!\" One of Mei Feng’s officers exclaimed, her voice filled with joy.","\"Though it’s not much better, being only a mission to gather Unknown Ores in the Orange Zone.\"","\"So what if it’s only slightly better? This proves that he can accept missions besides cleanup missions, which is a big step forward!\"","\"You’re treating him like a toddler who’d just learned to take his first steps,\" Mei Feng remarked while shaking her head.","She continued, \"I knew he’d eventually start taking other missions, but this is quicker than I anticipated...\"","Someone then said, \"It may not seem like it, but many people are eager to see what he’ll accomplish, and they’ve been disappointed so far. Compared to the Ironwoman, who took on all kinds of dangerous missions shortly after joining, they find his performance underwhelming. Given his unprecedented talent, they expected him to follow in her footsteps.\"","\"Can you really compare the two, though? I don’t know why Corporal Yuan decided to join the military, but I doubt he has the same goal as the Ironwoman.\"","\"Corporal Yuan has a completely different demeanor, too,\" Mei Feng said. \"Unlike that woman, he’s carefree... almost a little too carefree.\"","\"Enough about Corporal Yuan. Any news from General Gu’s side?\" Someone suddenly asked.","Mei Feng replied, \"I gave him a pretty stern warning, and he hasn’t tried to do anything so far. However, we can never be too cautious. Keep an eye on them to make sure they don’t try anything on Corporal Yuan.\"","\"Yes, General!\"","Meanwhile, on the other side, General Gu started fuming after learning about Yuan’s sudden change of activities, especially when they were so close to their plan.","\"That stinking brat barely managed to dodge a bullet!\"","\"Please calm yourself, General Gu. There’s a good chance that little bastard is only trying out something new and will return to doing cleanup missions soon.\" One of the officers tried to reassure him.","Another then spoke, \"Even if he doesn’t, there are still plenty of ways to get him to join our squad for their cleanup mission.\"","\"However, we should proceed cautiously and put our plans on hold for now,\" said Captain Huang, the officer responsible for assigning cleanup missions. \"General Mei’s people have been watching us like hawks. If we do anything suspicious, they’ll seize the opportunity to ruin us.\"","General Gu nodded and said, \"I’ll leave everything to you and await good news.\"","\"Yes, General!\"","Several days later, Yuan showed up at the mission’s meeting spot, and instead of meeting at the gates, they met in front of the mission hall.","\"Wow! It’s really him! The Cleaning Maniac!\"","One of the soldiers exclaimed with excitement, almost as if they were meeting their idol.","\"There’s... a lot of people...\" Yuan muttered, a little taken aback by how many soldiers were present.","\"Is everyone here partaking in the mission?\" he asked, as there were twenty-three soldiers, excluding him.","\"That’s right. This is your first time doing this sort of mission, correct? This number of gatherers is pretty common. In fact, there are usually more.\"","\"What about the reward distribution? Do we all share, or are we only credited for what we find?\"","\"Of course, we share. This is a team effort and a mission, so we all receive a share of the total Unknown Ores.\"","\"I see...\"","\"Alright, now that everyone’s here, we’ll split into four squads. Squad 1 will head south, Squad 2 north, Squad 3 west, and Squad 4 east.\"","After some management, Yuan ended up in Squad 3 with five other soldiers.","\"We will meet here in two weeks. Until then, good luck with your gathering, and stay safe.\"","While the others went in their respective direction, Yuan’s squad made their way to the western gates.","Once outside the city walls, they began rushing to the Orange Zone, ignoring all of the Void Specters they encountered.","\"It must feel awkward not to clean the Void Specters, Corporal Yuan,\" someone in the squad remarked as they flew past the Void Specters.","\"Not really,\" he said with a smile.","\"Wait... Corporal Yuan, you just joined the military, right? And you were exempted from boot camp.\"","\"That’s right.\"","The soldiers in the squad suddenly stopped moving and looked at him with concerned expressions.","\"What is the problem?\" he asked.","\"If you just joined and didn’t go to boot camp... that means you didn’t have the chance to learn Void Control yet, which would make this mission much more difficult and dangerous for you.\"","\"Ah, that? Then you don’t have to worry, because I can use it.\"","\"Huh?\"","The soldiers’ eyes widened with surprise.","A new soldier begins training in Void Control during their first week of boot camp, but only the most gifted geniuses can use it by the time they graduate. As for everyone else, it usually takes another three to five years of training before they can wield it proficiently.","So how was Yuan, who had skipped boot camp and thrown himself into nonstop cleanup missions almost immediately after joining the military, already capable of using Void Control?","\"There’s no way you could’ve learned Void Control with such limited time...\"","In order to get rid of their doubt, Yuan used Void Control directly in front of them, teleporting left and right with ease.","\"My word! He can actually use it!\"","\"When did you learn to use it? Surely, you didn’t learn it before joining the military, right?\"","Yuan chuckled. \"No, I learned it during the downtime between missions. It only took me a few days to grasp it.\"","\"A few days...?\"","The soldiers’ eyes widened at the outrageous claim, their mouths hanging open in disbelief.","Not only were they awestruck by such an achievement, but they also felt insulted, as though their own years of effort meant nothing in the face of such overwhelming talent.","\"What are you all waiting for? If we linger any longer, we’ll lose to the others,\" Yuan said as he started moving again.","\"This is not a competition...\"","They shook their heads inwardly before following him."]},{"number":2607,"title":"Chapter 2607: Void Hunter","paragraphs":["After ignoring every Void Specter they encountered, Yuan’s group reached the Orange Zone in just a day. Since Unknown Ores were rarely found near its outskirts, they continued venturing deeper.","Before long, Yuan had gone farther into the Orange Zone than he ever had during any of his cleanup missions.","\"Alright, let’s begin our search here,\" the squad leader said.","\"Wait. Since this is Corporal Yuan’s first mission of this kind, shouldn’t we explain how it works first?\"","\"Oh, right.\" The squad leader turned to Yuan. \"It’s quite simple. We’ll form a line with some distance between each person, then advance together. If anyone spots an Unknown Ore, they let the others know so we can stop and wait for them to retrieve it.\"","\"...\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow after hearing the explanation, unable to ignore how inefficient the method seemed. However, he also understood the need for order. If everyone searched independently, it would be easy for someone to get lost.","Thus, Yuan decided to try their method first before suggesting an alternative.","Soon, they formed an orderly line, leaving several hundred miles between each person, and advanced deeper into the Orange Zone, gradually drawing closer to the Red Zone.","Shortly after they began moving, Yuan asked, \"Wouldn’t this method be more efficient with more people? Why did we split the group into several squads and send them in different directions?\"","\"Huh? You don’t know about ’that’?\" The soldiers turned to look at him with surprised faces.","\"What is ’that’?\"","\"We call it the Void Hunter. It’s an abnormal and mysterious being that appears when too many people are gathered in one place to hunt them.\"","\"It’s so powerful and dangerous that meeting it is essentially a death sentence. Because of this, we tend to keep our numbers as small as possible.\"","\"Is it anything like the Void Specters?\" Yuan asked.","\"Yes, but it takes the form of a human being.\"","\"And how strong is it... roughly?\"","\"So strong that nobody has been able to defeat it. I heard that even the strongest cultivator in history, Tian Yuchen, was completely helpless against it.\"","\"That strong?\" Yuan’s eyes widened at this information, as Tian Yuchen was able to climb all the way to the 50th floor in Endless Assault. This meant that the Void Hunter was likely several times stronger than his bottleneck on the 46th floor.","However, he couldn’t fathom why such a being even exists. What was its purpose? Why does it only appear when many people gather in one place?","About two hours later, Yuan sensed an Unknown Ore not far away in the distance, but it was located ahead of another soldier.","Rather than announcing his finding, Yuan waited to see how long it’d take before they noticed.","Some time later, the soldier finally noticed the Unknown Ore and said, \"Found one!\"","The others immediately came to a halt and waited for the soldier to retrieve the Unknown Ore using Void Control, as the place was crawling with Void Specters.","’As expected... since they cannot sense Eternal Essence, they won’t be able to detect the Unknown Ores from afar and can only rely on their sight...’ Yuan thought to himself.","This meant that Yuan had an immense advantage when it came to finding Unknown Ores.","As they ventured deeper into the Orange Zone, they began encountering Unknown Ores more frequently.","However, they could have found far more, as Yuan sensed numerous Unknown Ores buried beneath the ground. Unfortunately, he couldn’t reveal their locations without raising questions about how he knew they were there.","Over the next several days, Yuan considered how he could collect the Unknown Ores buried underground without arousing suspicion.","An idea soon came to him, and he decided to put it to the test.","\"I think I see something,\" Yuan called out.","When the others stopped to wait for him, Yuan used Void Manipulation to travel beyond their line of sight. Taking advantage of the opportunity, he quickly dug up several Unknown Ores.","However, in order not to go overboard, he did not dig up every Unknown Ore he sensed.","\"Huh? You found three in one go?!\"","The soldiers were shocked when Yuan returned with three Unknown Ores in his grasp.","Although it wasn’t unheard of to find more than one Unknown Ore at once, it was incredibly rare. As for three Unknown Ores... it had only happened two times so far.","\"Damn! To find three Unknown Ores in one go during his first gathering mission! What a lucky dog!\"","\"How lucky are we talking about?\" Yuan asked.","\"As far as I know, it has only happened twice before, and the last time it happened was seventy years ago.\"","\"Oh, I am only talking about the Orange Zone,\" he quickly added. \"It’s common to find more in the Red Zone and beyond.\"","\"Is that so? I should try going on those missions next then.\"","\"It’s not that simple,\" one of them replied. \"Even though they may be available on your mission list, you will need to pass a test before you’re allowed to partake in missions within the Red Zone. There’s a reason why many of us are doing this mission instead.\"","\"What sort of test?\"","\"Your Void Control. Since the Void Specters become aggressive in the Red Zone, you will be required to use Void Control frequently.\"","\"I see...\"","\"If you’re going to try, don’t bother. You may have learned Void Control in a few days, but the tests are a different kind of beast. Most people qualify only after decades of training. Even with your heaven-sent talents, you’ll likely still need at least a few years.\"","\"I’ll keep that in mind. Here are the Unknown Ores,\" said Yuan as he handed the Unknown Ores to the squad leader, who was in charge of accounting for them.","Of course, he didn’t forget to absorb all of the Eternal Essence from them before doing so.","Time continued to pass, and in the blink of an eye, it was time for them to return to the city."]},{"number":2608,"title":"Chapter 2608: Learning Void Control","paragraphs":["\"Welcome back, everyone.\"","The soldiers greeted one another as the four squads returned from their gathering mission.","After a quick headcount confirmed that everyone had returned safely, the four squads pooled their loot.","\"Three hundred and twenty-seven Unknown Ores, huh? Looks like we got lucky, especially the third squad, who contributed over a hundred ores.\"","\"You can thank Corporal Yuan for that, as he’d gathered more than half of our total alone.\"","\"Regardless, everyone did a good job. Hope to see you all in the next one again.\"","The group was disbanded soon after.","Although Yuan could’ve absorbed all of the Unknown Ores of their Eternal Essence, he decided against it, as he did not want to be too greedy. Above all, he wanted to be cautious.","After leaving, Yuan went to look for Sergeant Quang.","\"I want to partake in missions within the Red Zone, but I heard that one must take some kind of test.\"","\"That’s correct. Your Void Control will be evaluated by a group of examiners to see if you qualify to enter the Red Zone.\"","\"Where do I go to take the test?\" Yuan then asked.","\"You can—\" Sergeant Quang suddenly paused, his eyebrows raising as he realized something. \"You’re trying to take the test? Now? That implies you already know Void Control, but as far as I am aware, you did not have the time or opportunity to learn such a technique,\" he said.","Besides Wu Wang and Shi Fa, neither Sergeant Bing nor Sergeant Quang were aware that Yuan could use Void Control.","\"I just want to know for future reference—for when I learn Void Control,\" Yuan said, concealing the fact that he had already mastered it, let alone knew it.","\"Then you’re looking quite far into the future. Void Control isn’t something you can learn in a day—or even a month. Most people need years just to grasp it, let alone reach a level that would allow them to traverse the Red Zone. Even for a genius like you, it would likely take several years.\"","\"Then I’d better start learning now, huh?\" Yuan said with a calm smile. \"I still have a training session with an elite soldier as a reward for my performance during recruitment. Could I ask them to teach me Void Control?\"","Sergeant Quang nodded.","\"You can. Are you going to ask me to teach you?\" he then asked.","However, to his surprise, Yuan shook his head and said, \"No, I already have someone in mind.\"","\"Who?\"","\"Sergeant Wu.\"","\"Seriously? Instead of Wu Wang, I’d recommend Shi Fa. He’s a much better teacher—not that I’m trying to badmouth Wu Wang. Hell, since you can technically ask anyone to train you, you might as well choose an actual instructor. They’re trained to teach, after all.\"","However, Yuan shook his head and refused.","\"I have my reasons for choosing him.\"","\"If that’s what you really want...\"","\"I’ll let Wu Wang know,\" Sergeant Quang said a moment later.","\"Thanks.\"","Yuan returned to his living quarters to rest afterward.","Although the idea might have seemed sudden, he had already planned to pretend to learn Void Control from either Wu Wang or Shi Fa. Revealing that he already knew it would raise too many suspicions, and he knew he couldn’t fool everyone as easily as he had the soldiers before.","A few days later, Yuan received merit and money from the gathering mission, and on the same day, Wu Wang appeared at his doorstep with a frown on his face.","\"Is it true that you requested for me to train you?\" he questioned the moment Yuan opened the door. \"Please tell me that’s not true and that bastard Quang Qing is just messing with me.\"","A wide smile tugged at Yuan’s lips as he responded, \"No, it’s true. I want you to teach me Void Control.\"","\"Are you fucking with me?! You want me to teach you Void Control?! If anything, I should be asking to be your student!\" Wu Wang exclaimed in disbelief.","After all, he was fully aware of how profound Yuan’s Void Control was—that it was far superior to his own.","\"Lower your voice. Are you trying to let the entire residential area hear you?\" Yuan sighed, shaking his head.","\"Calm down. I’m not seriously asking you to teach me. Aside from you, Shi Fa, and a few others who aren’t a concern, no one knows I can use Void Control. If I suddenly use it, people would grow suspicious, so I need to pretend that I learned it from you.\"","\"Don’t worry, I won’t take up much of your time. Only a few days. Hell, I won’t mind training you, either.\"","\"You? Train me?\" Wu Wang stared at Yuan with one of his eyebrows raised.","\"Are we still talking about Void Control?\" he inquired.","\"If you think Void Control is the only advantage I have over you, you’re sorely mistaken,\" Yuan replied with an arrogant smile.","Wu Wang fell silent for a moment, visibly irritated by his claim.","\"In that case, I’d love to see what else you think you’re better than me at!\"","\"Does that mean you accept my request?\"","\"Yes. Even if you didn’t provoke me, I would’ve agreed, since I will get merit for training you.\"","\"Is that so? Then let’s go.\"","Yuan and Wu Wang made their way to a private training room.","Once they were inside, alone, they began sparring.","Before the match, Wu Wang had been certain there was no way he would lose to Yuan in a fair fight. Yet only a few minutes later, he found himself sprawled on the ground, having failed to touch even a single hair on Yuan’s body.","\"???\"","Wu Wang stared at the ceiling with a bewildered expression on his face, looking like he was having trouble comprehending what had just happened.","\"Want to go again?\" Yuan asked.","Wu Wang immediately sprang back to his feet, and their second round began.","The two continued sparring for several rounds without pause.","In the end, Wu Wang lost every match—each defeat more crushing than the last.","\"So, how about it? Still going to refuse my guidance?\" Yuan asked with a cheeky smile as he looked down at Wu Wang, who lay sprawled on the ground.","Wu Wang gritted his teeth in frustration, but instead of giving in to his anger, he swallowed both his pride and his resentment before asking Yuan for guidance.","Thus, Yuan started training Wu Wang.","Six days later, Sergeant Quang and Sergeant Bing showed up at their training room together to check on Yuan’s progress.","\"It’s much harder than you expected, isn’t it?\" Sergeant Quang asked Yuan with a faint smile, his expression practically saying, ’I told you so’.","Before Yuan could even respond, Sergeant Bing chuckled and said, \"Even with your talents, there is no way you can learn Void Control so quickly!\"","\"Um... actually, he’s already learned it.\"","Rather than Yuan, it was Wu Wang who spoke.","\"What did you just say?\"","Sergeant Quang and Sergeant Bing both stiffened, their eyes widening in shock and disbelief.","\"I said he’s already learned Void Control,\" Wu Wang repeated in an awkward voice, feeling a little guilty about fooling his comrades.","\"Surely you’re just messing with us,\" Sergeant Bing eventually responded. \"There’s no way someone can learn Void Control in just a few—\"","Before she could even finish her sentence, Yuan used Void Manipulation, teleporting directly in front of her.","\"You were saying?\" he said, a smile tugging at his lips.","\"Heavens!\"","Sergeant Bing was so surprised that she fell backward, hitting the hard ground with her buttocks.","\"That was... Void Control?!\" Sergeant Quang exclaimed, looking like he’d just seen a ghost.","\"You actually managed to learn Voice Control in just six days?! Just what kind of monster are you?!\"","\"I am just good at learning things,\" Yuan calmly replied. \"Really, really good.\"","\"Even so, there should be a limit to such nonsense!\"","Yuan silently shrugged.","\"Just what kind of training did you do?\" Sergeant Bing suddenly asked as she stood back up, one hand rubbing on her buttocks.","\"Just normal training,\" Yuan replied.","\"And how did you train, exactly?\"","\"Normally.\"","\"...\"","Sergeant Bing gave up on trying to receive a proper answer from Yuan and turned to look at Wu Wang, who quickly said, \"He isn’t lying. He just sat there and watched me use Void Control over and over again. Then, after a few days, he was able to use Void Control.\"","\"He learned it just by watching? That’s beyond ridiculous?\" Sergeant Bing shook her head.","\"I don’t know what else to tell you,\" Wu Wang shook his head.","\"Regardless...\" Sergeant Quang started speaking, \"Even if you managed to learn Void Control in just a few days, you’ll likely need at least several months of training before you become proficient enough for the test.\"","\"Perhaps, but I want to take the test and see just how difficult it is,\" Yuan responded. \"If I fail, I can just retake the test in the future.\""]},{"number":2609,"title":"Chapter 2609: Red Zone Exam","paragraphs":["\"Before I apply for the test, I would like to know the level of Void Control required to pass it,\" Yuan said.","\"Does it really matter? You either pass or don’t,\" Sergeant Quang remarked.","\"It does to me.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Sergeant Quang sighed out loud before speaking, \"Watch. This is the level you must reach to pass the test.\"","The next moment, Sergeant Quang used Void Control, teleporting left and right in a steady rhythm. Each teleport covered exactly one hundred meters—not a single meter more or less.","\"You’ll be required to do more than just teleport left and right,\" Sergeant Quang said afterward.","\"There will be obstacle courses,\" Sergeant Bing elaborated.","\"I see...\"","Yuan nodded, committing Sergeant Quang’s demonstration to memory. He wanted a proper benchmark so he wouldn’t go overboard during the test and completely obliterate it.","After all, he needed to make it as believable as possible. Learning Void Control so quickly was already outrageous enough. If he displayed a level of mastery that would normally take eras to achieve immediately after learning it, it would undoubtedly raise a lot of eyebrows.","Yuan turned to Wu Wang and spoke with a smile, \"Thanks for the training. I will do my best not to disappoint you.\"","\"S-Sure...\" Wu Wang nodded with a stiff expression, looking a bit embarrassed.","\"Now... where do I go to take the test?\" Yuan asked.","\"You can do it by attempting to accept a Red Zone mission,\" Sergeant Bing explained. \"If you don’t meet the qualifications, you’ll be prompted to take the test. Once you accept, you’ll be scheduled for the next available session.\"","\"The mission hall, it is.\"","Yuan immediately made his way to the mission hall.","While he entered the queue to wait for his turn, soldiers would come up to him and ask, \"What mission will you be accepting this time, Corporal Yuan? Another cleanup mission?\"","\"Haven’t you heard? He’s doing gathering missions now.\"","\"Perhaps he’ll do something different this time.\"","Yuan replied, \"It’s a secret.\"","Once it was his turn to use the machine, Yuan immediately picked the mission that required him to gather Unknown Ores in the Red Zone.","<Checking soldier’s qualifications>","<You currently lack the permit to enter the Red Zone>","<Would you like to schedule the Red Zone Exam for the permit?>","<You have been accepted to partake in the next Red Zone Exam, scheduled to begin in 77 hours and 32 minutes>","When Yuan returned, Sergeant Quang asked, \"When is the test?\"","\"In 77 hours.\"","\"What are you going to do until then? Keep on practicing your Void Control?\"","He nodded.","\"But I intend on doing it alone. Since I already learned it, I can practice by myself,\" he then said.","\"Are you sure? I don’t mind training you for a few days,\" Sergeant Quang said.","Yuan smiled and said, \"Just your thoughts are enough.\"","\"If you insist.\"","Once Yuan returned to his living quarters, he said, \"I’ll be training in my room, so you don’t need to escort me anywhere until the day of the exam.\"","\"Training inside your room?\"","They looked at him with raised eyebrows. Although they all lived alone, none of their homes were spacious enough to practice Void Control.","Of course, Yuan had no intention of actually practicing Void Control.","\"See ya in 77 hours.\"","Before they could question him, Yuan hastily retreated into his living quarters and closed the door, leaving them speechless.","\"The more time I spend with him, the more mysterious he feels,\" Sergeant Bing remarked with a dazed expression.","\"Now that I think about it, he never goes anywhere in between missions, always remaining inside his home,\" Sergeant Quang remarked.","\"He did go to the training area... once,\" said Sergeant Bing.","They left shortly afterward, still wondering what Yuan did with his spare time.","Meanwhile, back in his room, Yuan sat in the lotus position with his eyes closed, cultivating using the Limitless Cultivation Technique.","One of the main reasons Yuan could use Limitless continuously without exhausting himself, unlike everyone else, was the Limitless Cultivation Technique, which he cultivated whenever he had the opportunity.","The deeper Yuan’s understanding of the technique grew, the more he realized just how powerful it was, especially when paired with his Perfect Heavenly Refinement physique.","’Although it appears simple at first glance and is relatively easy to learn, the deeper I study it, the more profound and difficult it becomes!’","An excited smile tugged at Yuan’s lips. It had been a long time since he had encountered something that truly challenged him.","Time passed swiftly, and 77 hours later, Yuan left his living quarters and followed Sergeant Bing to the exam area.","An hour before Yuan showed up at the exam site, several individuals suddenly appeared, startling the examiners there.","\"G-General Mei?! And Officers?!\"","General Mei and some of her officers had shown up unannounced.","\"Don’t mind us. We’re here to spectate today’s examination. That’s all,\" said Mei Feng.","\"O-Of course! Please, let me show you to the spectator’s room!\"","Since it was a simple exam held several times a month, it rarely drew spectators, especially those of higher rank. As for someone of General Mei Feng’s standing, this was the first time a person of her rank had ever attended, hence why the examiners were bewildered by her presence.","Once Mei Feng and her associates left for the spectator room, the remaining examiners began openly wondering why she had come.","\"It must be one of the examinees! That’s the only reason to come here! Check the list again! Find out who she’s here to see!\"","\"I-I think I found him! Corporal Yuan! That’s the super rookie who aced the last recruitment and broke all of its previous records!\"","\"Huh? The last recruitment was only a few months ago, and he’s already a Corporal?\"","\"I’m more interested in why he’s already taking this exam. Does he even know what he’s walking into? There’s no way his Void Control is anywhere near the level needed for this exam.\"","\"Perhaps he’s just taking it to see how much work he needs to reach such a level.\"","\"I guess we’ll see in an hour...\""]},{"number":2610,"title":"Chapter 2610: Void Control Evaluation","paragraphs":["\"I can’t believe Corporal Yuan is already taking the Red Zone Exam right after his first gathering mission,\" one of the officers with Mei Feng remarked after taking a seat in the spectator’s room.","\"And to think we thought he was taking it too slow not long ago,\" someone else remarked.","Another then spoke up, asking, \"Aren’t you all curious? Since when did he learn Void Control? As far as I am aware, he skipped boot camp and has been on missions since joining, so he doesn’t have any time to learn it—at least, he shouldn’t.\"","\"Now that you mentioned it...\"","They all turned to look at Mei Feng, who calmly replied, \"He used his 20,000-meter reward a few days ago, requesting Sergeant Wu to train him, so I can only assume that he learned Void Control in that time.\"","\"Huh? A few days ago? There’s no way anyone can learn Void Control that quickly, let alone reach the level required for this exam.\"","\"We’ll never know what that guy is thinking.\"","Some time later, the participants for the Red Zone Exam started showing up at the test site, and in the blink of an eye, hundreds of people gathered.","\"This is my seventh time taking this test. I have a good feeling about today!\"","\"According to my analysis, the difficulty of the Red Zone Exam varies, with some sessions being much easier than others. If my calculations are correct, today’s exam should be the easiest one this year!\"","The soldiers chatted among themselves as they waited for the exam to begin, unaware that, because of a certain high-ranking officer, they had walked into the most difficult exam ever recorded because the examiners did not want it to look too easy.","\"Good luck,\" Sergeant Bing said to Yuan before going to the spectator’s room—one that was different from the private room used by Mei Feng and the other officers.","\"Welcome, everyone. Before we begin the evaluation, we will give you a quick run-through of how it works.\"","\"There will be three tests in total. For the first, you’ll need to catch balls using Void Control. You don’t have to catch all of them—only eighty out of a hundred. For the second test, you must avoid attacks for ten minutes using nothing but Void Control. The final test will assess your precision. Ten people will go at a time.\"","Soon, the examiners began calling the participants onto the testing ground.","\"One more thing, in case this is your first time taking the exam. Aside from moving your arms and body to catch the balls, all physical movement is strictly prohibited. You may only reposition yourself using Void Control, even if you need to move only a few inches.\"","Once the exam began, a machine positioned at the opposite end of the field started firing glowing green balls at nearly the speed of sound, launching one every three seconds.","Before each ball was fired, a red laser appeared, indicating the general direction it would travel.","Although the test started relatively easily, the firing rate increased after the first twenty balls, with one ball launched every two seconds instead of three. After forty balls, the remaining sixty were fired at one-second intervals.","\"W-What’s going on?! Why is the test so difficult?! It was supposed to be easy today!\" exclaimed the soldier who had done the analysis.","\"How can you tell?\" someone asked.","\"Normally, it doesn’t switch to two-second intervals until after fifty balls, and the one-second interval doesn’t start until eighty! This time, it switched to two-second intervals after only twenty balls, then to one-second intervals after forty! This is the hardest exam ever recorded!\"","\"That’s crazy... No wonder why half of them dropped out already...\"","By the end of the first test, only three of the ten participants managed to catch at least eighty balls, moving on to the second test.","At the end of the first test, the participants were given five minutes to rest while seven more soldiers entered the testing ground to begin theirs.","\"For those of you taking the second test, your objective is to avoid all damage for ten minutes. Even a single graze will result in immediate disqualification. After all, against a Void Specter, even the slightest touch means death, so there is absolutely no room for error.\"","When the second test began for the first three participants, the machines that had previously fired balls began shooting bullets instead, each one aimed directly at them. As before, red lasers indicated where the bullets would travel, appearing first as thick lines that gradually narrowed as the machines prepared to fire.","Each laser represented a single bullet. During the first minute, only one laser appeared every three seconds. At the start of the second minute, two appeared at once, and by the third minute, that number had increased to three.","As the number of bullets increased, the participants had less room to dodge and fewer chances to rest. Since the shots were fired one after another rather than simultaneously, even when three lasers appeared every three seconds, they still had to use Void Control once every second.","At the start of the fourth minute, the number of bullets had suddenly doubled, going from three bullets to six.","Although the speed at which they were fired didn’t increase, they shot two bullets at once.","Upon reaching the fifth minute, the number of bullets doubled again.","The same happened after the sixth minute, and the number of bullets increased to twenty-four.","After the seventh minute, the number of bullets didn’t merely double—it tripled, now firing seventy-two bullets every three seconds. Moreover, the rate at which it shot them also increased, now shooting twelve bullets at a half-second interval.","This meant the participants could no longer teleport wherever they pleased. Instead, they had to anticipate the bullets’ trajectories and identify a safe location to teleport to before the next volley arrived.","By the eighth minute, the participants had to deal with two hundred and sixteen bullets.","During the final minute, however, the exact number no longer mattered, as the machines fired without pause, unleashing a continuous barrage like machine guns.","Ultimately, none of the three participants managed to last all ten minutes and were disqualified in the final minute."]},{"number":2611,"title":"Chapter 2611: Void Control Evaluation(2)","paragraphs":["\"Hey, analyst, is the second test harder or easier than usual?\" one of the participants asked at the end.","The analyst, who had been anxiously biting his nails, stopped to respond, \"Harder. Much harder. Just like the first test, this is the first time it’s this difficult! Just what in heaven’s name is happening today?!\"","\"Maybe they decided to modify the difficulty, so this will be the new norm.\"","\"That’s outrageous! It was already hard enough to pass the exam! There’s no reason to make it even harder!\"","\"Actually, I think I know why this exam is harder than usual...\" someone suddenly said before turning to look at a certain individual among the participants.","The others followed his gaze to a handsome man with silky black hair tied neatly into a single ponytail.","\"Who is that?\" one of them asked in a puzzled voice.","\"T-That’s Corporal Yuan, the Cleaning Maniac!\"","\"Cleaning Maniac? What kind of nickname is that? And why would they make the exam harder just because of him?\"","\"He’s called the Cleaning Maniac because he’s famous for willingly joining others’ cleanup missions ever since he joined the military, even insisting on doing all of the cleaning alone.\"","\"That’s impressive in its own right, but that still doesn’t explain—\"","\"Let me finish!\" The soldier who was explaining interrupted before continuing, \"Not only was he handpicked by General Mei, he even broke all of the records during his recruitment! They’re calling him the upcoming Ironman who could rival the Ironwoman!\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow as the soldier recounted his background to everyone while staring at him as though he were some rare treasure on display in a museum.","\"I appreciate the introduction, but there’s no reason to increase the difficulty of the exam solely because of my presence. If anything, they should be lowering it, as I had only learned Void Control a few days ago.\"","\"The hell? Why are you here if you’ve only learned Void Control a few days ago? Most of us here have trained for over a decade!\"","\"I guess most of you here have also broken records during your recruitment, huh?\" Yuan responded in a sarcastic tone, which immediately ticked off the soldier.","However, the soldier realized he had nothing to argue against Yuan’s words, so he quickly fell silent, his face still slightly flushed.","A moment later, Yuan said, \"I don’t know why they decided to increase the difficulty of this exam, but it has nothing to do with me.\"","\"...\"","Despite his words, Yuan couldn’t help but wonder whether General Gu had arranged it as another attempt to make things difficult for him.","After more than fifty soldiers had attempted and failed the exam, someone finally advanced to the final test, where the precision of their Void Control would be assessed.","On the participant’s testing ground, two red circles materialized a mile apart, each barely large enough to fit a pair of feet.","\"For the final test, you must use Void Control to teleport between the two circles one hundred consecutive times, with no more than a quarter of a second between each teleport. To pass, you must achieve an accuracy rate of at least ninety percent.\"","Although the test appeared easy at first glance, the participant was already exhausted from constantly using Void Control throughout the previous two tests. That fatigue greatly diminished both their precision and consistency, making the final test far more difficult than it seemed.","\"N-Ninty percent?! That’s the requirement for the Purple Zone!\" The analyst cried out loud in disbelief. \"It’s always been eighty percent for Red Zones!\"","\"It’s doomed. Nobody will pass this month’s exam.\"","\"We might as well just leave now...\" someone muttered out loud. \"We can always retake the test at a later date, anyway.\"","And surprisingly, a few soldiers actually took that advice and left, quitting the test without even attempting it.","The examiners did not stop these soldiers, merely shaking their heads in disappointment.","As for the officers in the private spectator’s room, they couldn’t care less about the other soldiers, as they were solely there to watch Yuan. Moreover, they knew that this month’s exam was cranked up to an unprecedented degree.","\"Should we really let them continue the exam at this level of difficulty? To be honest, it seems excessive,\" one of the officers voiced their concern.","Mei Feng calmly responded, \"As long as this doesn’t become the new standard, let it continue. It’s good to shake things up once in a while. This experience may even benefit them.\"","Some time later, the participant who reached the final test received his result.","<Accuracy: 80.13%>","\"...\"","The soldier fell to his knees in shock. Had the examiners not raised the passing threshold to ninety percent, he would have barely passed the exam.","\"Failed. Please exit the testing grounds.\"","As if to rub salt into the wound, the examiner coldly announced his failure.","Unwilling to accept the result, the soldier turned toward the examiners and shouted angrily, \"Why the hell did you suddenly raise the passing score to ninety percent when it has always been eighty percent?! And without any sort of announcement, either! This is unacceptable!\"","As though they had anticipated such backlash, the examiners calmly replied, \"The world is evolving, so we soldiers must evolve alongside it.\"","\"What kind of explanation is that?! That’s complete nonsense!\"","Sure enough, such an excuse was pure bullshit. However, the examiners refused to elaborate.","\"Please leave the testing grounds. There are still soldiers who need to take the test. If you’re not satisfied with the results, you may take the examination again in the future... once you improve a little more.\"","\"Fuck! This is bullshit!\" The soldier cursed out loud as he stomped away.","However, before the soldier left the testing grounds, Yuan could feel the man’s gaze fixed on him, as though he blamed Yuan for everything that had happened.","Yuan pretended not to notice, as there was no way for him to prove his innocence."]},{"number":2612,"title":"Chapter 2612: Void Control Evaluation(3)","paragraphs":["After waiting around an hour, Yuan’s ears twitched when he heard his name being called.","\"Corporal Yuan! Lane number nine!\"","Yuan was slightly surprised to hear his name, as he thought he would be called last again, but there were still plenty of people after him.","He calmly walked to his lane while wondering how he should deal with the exam.","’The exam unexpectedly became even more difficult than anticipated... should I just fail on purpose and try again on the next one? They have a test every month, anyway...’","However, after some contemplation, he decided that it wasn’t worth waiting another month, and that he might as well get this thing over with today.","When Mei Feng and the officers noticed Yuan entering the testing grounds, they subconsciously sat up with straightened backs.","\"What kind of performance will you show us today?\" Mei Feng mumbled in a low voice, a subtle smile on her face.","Once Yuan stepped into lane number nine, the test began shortly afterward.","The moment Yuan began using Void Control, the spectators collectively sucked in a breath of cold air. Seeing someone wield it after only a few days of training was simply too astonishing.","Even Mei Feng had harbored some doubts. However, once Yuan demonstrated the technique—even with movements that appeared somewhat amateurish—everyone was left speechless.","\"I can’t believe it... He’s really using Void Control. It’s still somewhat unrefined, but that’s only natural considering he learned it just a few days ago.\"","At first, Yuan deliberately made it seem as though he was struggling to catch the balls, which was actually the most difficult part of the exam. However, as the test continued, his Void Control gradually became more refined, giving the impression that he was improving with every use.","\"How is he improving so quickly that we can see it with our own eyes?! That kind of talent should be illegal!\" One of the participants exclaimed in disbelief.","Soon, Yuan reached his 50th ball, catching all of them. However, after that point, he started to miss a few of them, especially towards the end.","In the end, he’d only managed to catch eighty-one balls in total, which was just slightly passing.","\"My word! He’s actually passed the first test!\"","\"Even if he fails the second test, nobody would blame him.\"","\"What if he also passes the second test?\"","\"Unfortunately, I don’t think he has any energy to continue. If you hadn’t noticed, he slowed down quite a bit toward the end.\"","After his first test, Yuan was given five minutes to rest, but it was over in the blink of an eye, and his second test began.","’I won’t be able to barely pass this test as I did with the first test...’ Yuan thought to himself as he dodged the first bullet.","Five minutes later—","\"Hey, who was it that claimed he won’t have enough energy to continue? He’s doing just fine.\"","\"He was given some time to rest, after all. But I’m sure he’ll drop within the next two minutes.\"","Two minutes later, Yuan continued dodging the bullets with the same consistency.","\"It’s been two minutes...\"","\"O-One more minute! He will definitely fall within the next minute!\"","Yet, two more minutes passed, and after lasting ten minutes, Yuan passed the second test.","\"What?! How is that possible?! He was clearly out of breath after the first test! Even if he was given five minutes to rest, that isn’t nearly enough time to recover that much! That makes no sense!\"","\"Your first mistake was to use common sense against a genius like that...\"","Although every participant was given five minutes of rest after the first test, there was no rest after the second, so Yuan had to immediately start the third test.","\"As amazing as his performance was for someone who’d learned Void Control just a few days ago, this is where he fails,\" said the analyst. \"Even if he has the stamina to keep going, his precision is another subject. I have been watching him closely, and I noticed that his precision has been all over the place. I would be surprised if his accuracy is above 30 percent.\"","\"That low?\"","\"I guess we’ll see...\"","The moment the third test started, Yuan started using Void Control to teleport between the two circles.","\"H-Hey....\"","\"That’s ridiculous!\"","Only seconds after Yuan began, everyone realized he was performing exceptionally well—better than anyone who had taken the exam before him.","The spectators watched with wide eyes as Yuan teleported with astonishing precision, displaying a level of mastery that far surpassed anything he had shown up to that point.","One hundred teleports later—","<Accuracy: 90.05%>","\"What?!\"","Many exclaimed simultaneously, unwilling to believe their eyes.","\"P-Pass...\" The examiners swallowed nervously before announcing the result, their voices filled with disbelief.","The spectator room was eerily silent, as everyone needed a moment to process what they had just witnessed.","\"His precision during the first and second tests was nowhere near this level... Was he deliberately hiding his abilities, or did he truly improve that much in such a short time?\" one of the officers muttered thoughtfully.","\"He has no reason to conceal his skills. Considering he learned Void Control in only a few days, it’s more likely that he simply improved that quickly,\" someone replied.","Meanwhile, on the training grounds—","\"Corporal Yuan, you’ve already finished the test. You can leave now.\"","However, Yuan turned to face the examiners and uttered words that nobody there could’ve anticipated even in a billion years.","\"Is it possible for me to retake the test?\" he asked with a calm expression.","\"Excuse me?\"","Everyone present stared at him with widened eyes.","\"W-Why?\" one of the examiners snapped out of his daze and asked.","\"Because I am not satisfied with my results,\" Yuan responded in a serious tone.","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, another examiner spoke. \"S-Since you passed, you may request a retake. However, you’ll have to forfeit your current result, and whatever score you receive on your second attempt will become final—even if you fail. You won’t be allowed to retake the exam again. Are you fine with that?\"","Yuan silently nodded, leaving them speechless."]},{"number":2613,"title":"Chapter 2613: Retaking the Exam","paragraphs":["\"Is he crazy?! He barely passed the exam, which is already a miracle itself, but he wants to retake it?! Does he really think he can obtain a higher score?!\" The officers were in disbelief at Yuan’s arrogance.","\"I don’t understand why he even wants a higher score... It’s not a competition, and he gains nothing from it.\"","\"This must be some kind of illness for geniuses like him. They are never satisfied.\"","Mei Feng then spoke, \"If he wants to do it again, let him. If he fails, then he can only blame himself.\"","Meanwhile, Yuan asked the examiners after having his request accepted, \"Do I have to retake the test immediately? I’d like to get an hour of rest.\"","\"You can retake it at any time as long as the exams are still going,\" replied an examiner.","\"Alright.\"","Yuan left the testing grounds and began resting by the wall.","\"That guy’s truly crazy.\"","\"Bastard is just trying to show off. I hope he fails the second exam.\"","The exam continued, but not a single soldier passed after Yuan.","Even after failing, however, none of them left the building. Instead, they chose to remain behind and watch Yuan retake the exam.","An hour later, Yuan got off the floor and approached the examiners.","\"I am ready to retake the exam.\"","\"O-Okay. We’ll send you in once there’s an available lane.\"","\"Thank you.\"","A few minutes later, Yuan returned to the testing grounds and coincidentally stepped into lane number nine once more.","When the exam began, his performance during the first test was noticeably better than before—so much so that the difference was incomparable.","\"What the hell?! It’s like I am watching a different person!\"","The officers nearly got off their seats after seeing how much Yuan had improved.","During his first attempt, Yuan had purposefully started missing after the 50th ball. This time, however, he was determined to catch every single one.","Some time later—","\"He actually caught all hundred balls!\"","\"What the hell is going on?! Even if his mastery of Void Control had drastically increased, he shouldn’t have the stamina to keep going! An hour of rest is nowhere near enough time to fully recover, either!\"","Five minutes later, Yuan began his second test.","Since he had passed it flawlessly during his first attempt, the spectators assumed there was nothing left for him to improve. However, rather than dodging preemptively like most participants, Yuan waited until the very last instant—just before each bullet struck—to teleport away, displaying both his extraordinary reaction speed and absolute confidence.","Ten minutes later, Yuan moved onto the third test.","<Accuracy: 99.96%>","Yuan looked at the results and silently nodded, satisfied with them.","\"N-Ninety-nine point ninety-six percent?! That’s practically a perfect score!\"","\"Heavens!\"","The officers could no longer contain their excitement and stood from their seats, their eyes glued to Yuan’s miraculous results.","\"To improve this much in such a short time! What terrifying talents! It’s practically otherworldly!\"","Meanwhile, the examiners were so awestruck that they fell into a daze and forgot to announce the result.","The other soldiers could only stare at Yuan as if they had seen a ghost, their eyes widened and jaws hanging open in complete disbelief.","Although Yuan could have simply accepted the result of his first attempt, he wanted everyone present to witness firsthand how quickly he could improve. That way, even if he suddenly accomplished something outrageous in the future, no one would question it.","In other words, he wanted to drill one thought into their minds—that nothing was beyond his capabilities.","\"I can leave, right?\" Yuan asked the examiners, snapping them out of their daze.","\"Y-Yes...\"","\"Do I get some sort of certificate to verify that I have passed this exam?\" Yuan asked as he walked off the testing grounds.","\"No, we’ll update your information after the exam today, and you’ll be able to partake in Red Zone missions by tomorrow.\"","\"Sounds good.\"","Yuan began making his way to the exit but was promptly stopped by a familiar voice.","\"Wait a second, Corporal Yuan.\"","Yuan turned around to follow the sound of the voice.","\"General Mei?\" he muttered in a surprised tone.","\"General Mei?!\" The other soldiers hastily raised their arms to salute her after taking a moment to comprehend the situation.","\"Follow me to my office. I’d like to have a word with you,\" she said to him.","\"I understand.\"","Once Yuan followed Mei Feng to her office, she immediately asked him, \"Tell me the truth. Did you already know Void Control before joining the military?\"","\"What makes you think that?\"","Instead of directly answering her question, Yuan asked one of his own, a playful smile on his face.","Mei Feng sighed aloud before speaking, \"Your expression confirms my suspicion. Where did you learn it? From your original world?\"","Yuan nodded and answered truthfully, \"That’s correct, but in my world, it’s called Void Manipulation.\"","Mei Feng rubbed her eyes and sighed again.","\"What was the purpose of your performance today?\"","\"Well, it’d be odd for someone who just joined the military to know Void Control without doing proper training, right?\"","\"I mean, why’d you retake the test when your first one would’ve sufficed?\"","\"To put things simply... to raise my reputation.\"","\"Even though pretty much everyone is already aware of your existence?\"","\"Not that sort of reputation. I want to reach a level where nobody will question anything that I do.\"","\"That sounds like something someone with ulterior motives would say—a villain, so to speak.\"","Yuan chuckled at her words.","\"What are you worried about?\"","Mei Feng fell silent for a moment before responding, \"To be perfectly honest, I suspected you might be a spy from another city. However, no spy would willingly draw this much attention to themselves.\"","\"...\"","\"No response? You could at least try to deny it.\"","\"What would be the point of that? You already implied that you don’t think I am a spy.\" Yuan shrugged.","\"You’re really a handful...\" Mei Feng sighed for the third time."]},{"number":2614,"title":"Chapter 2614: Abnormalities","paragraphs":["\"Anything else?\" Yuan asked a moment later.","After a brief moment of silence. Mei Feng spoke, \"Now that you’ve acquired the authorization to enter the Red Zone, are you going there for your next mission?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"What kind?\"","\"Gathering Unknown Ores, as there are no other options for a mere corporal like me.\"","\"A mere corporal?\" Mei Feng raised an eyebrow at his remark. \"If you somehow didn’t figure it out already, you’re already allowed access to missions typically assigned to Sergeants, such as the one we just mentioned.\"","\"I was aware,\" Yuan admitted. \"But when do I get access to missions within the Purple Zone?\"","\"Let’s slow down a little and take one step at a time. You’ve just passed the exam for the Red Zone, after all.\"","\"I wouldn’t call that a test... at least not from my perspective. Hell, it barely qualifies as a warm-up. When it comes to Void Manipulation—or Void Control, as you call it—I wouldn’t be surprised if no one in this world can wield it better than I do,\" Yuan said.","Despite his seemingly arrogant declaration, there wasn’t the slightest trace of arrogance in his eyes.","\"Even if your Void Control is unmatched in this world, there are things beyond the Red Zone—dangerous entities that defy comprehension, especially for someone who came from another world,\" Mei Feng said, shaking her head.","\"There’s no need to be impatient. You’re already progressing several times faster than other geniuses. If you continue at this pace, you’ll definitely be able to enter the Purple Zone within a few years.\"","\"A few years, huh?\" Yuan mumbled.","He wouldn’t be this impatient if he had concrete evidence that this world was merely an illusion or a dream. The same applied if he knew whether time here flowed faster or slower than in the Nine Heavens, as it did in the Demonic Realm.","Of course, he was still leaning toward this world being an illusion of sorts, hence why he wasn’t too panicked.","’I have seen and experienced plenty of realistic illusions throughout my lives, and this one... although it is the most realistic one I’ve experienced so far, my gut tells me this world is fake...’","Despite those thoughts, Yuan still couldn’t completely dismiss the minuscule possibility that this world was real.","\"By the way, how’s your daughter? Is she doing okay in boot camp?\" Yuan suddenly asked about Mei Xiaoyun.","\"What makes you think that I would be keeping an eye on her?\" Mei Feng asked with a slight frown.","\"You don’t have to pretend to hate her since I am not your daughter,\" Yuan shook his head. \"There’s a reason you asked me to bring her into the military, after all.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Mei Feng sighed, \"She’s doing fine. A few had tried to recruit her, but they were all immediately shut down by her.\"","\"Oh? Does that mean she’s already decided to join one of your divisions?\" Yuan smiled.","\"Who knows?\" Mei Feng suddenly spun her chair around so Yuan couldn’t see her face.","\"If there’s nothing else, I am going to prepare for my mission in the Red Zone,\" Yuan then said.","\"Go.\"","After leaving Mei Feng’s office, Yuan returned home to rest for the day since the examiners said it would take at least a day for his status to be updated.","The following day, Yuan was escorted to the mission hall by Sergeant Quang.","\"I heard about the exam from Sergeant Bing. You’re one crazy bastard,\" he said with a bittersweet smile on his face.","\"It’s because I had an amazing teacher,\" Yuan laughed out loud.","\"Yeah... sure...\"","Of course, Sergeant Quang didn’t believe for a moment that Wu Wang possessed such teaching ability. Instead, he suspected that Yuan had already learned Void Control before joining the military and was merely putting on an act.","However, since Yuan had been personally recruited by General Mei, Sergeant Quang chose not to question him, deciding it would only create unnecessary trouble.","[Mission Details: Enter the Red Zone and gather Unknown Ores]","[Rank Requirement: Sergeant]","[Squad Requirement: 6]","[Mission Details: Enter the Red Zone and gather Unknown Crystals]","[Rank Requirement: Sergeant]","[Squad Requirement: 6]","However, when Yuan saw the missions available, his eyes stopped at the second mission.","’Unknown Crystals... If I recall correctly, Unknown Crystals are much rarer than Unknown Ores, so logically, they should contain even more Eternal Essence!’","Although Yuan had planned on searching for Unknown Ores, he changed his mind and decided to look for Unknown Crystals instead.","Moreover, there was a good chance that they would pick up any Unknown Ores along the way—at least it was a logical assumption.","<Checking soldier’s qualifications>","<Red Zone Permit has been confirmed>","<Request has been sent>","<Request has been approved>","Just like usual, his request was accepted almost instantly after it was sent.","[Mission Details: Gather Unknown Crystals in the Red Zone. Meet at the Eastern Gate at 0700 in 42 hours]","After accepting the mission, Yuan went home to cultivate.","Meanwhile, in a facility somewhere within the military base—","\"Senior! We’ve detected abnormalities with some of the Unknown Ores.\" A young woman called out to her supervisor while holding an Unknown Ore in her grasp.","\"What sort of abnormalities?\" The senior inquired for more information.","\"Well, we noticed that we were receiving less Limitless than usual during extraction, and after a thorough examination, we discovered that some of the Unknown Ores had already been extracted of their energy.\"","\"Are you sure someone didn’t accidentally mix the old ones in with the new batch? It happens from time to time.\"","\"No, we’re certain that wasn’t the case. These Unknown Ores had only just been delivered. Moreover, they retained their glowing appearance despite containing no energy, whereas the ones we extract always darken and turn into ordinary rocks.\"","The senior frowned upon hearing this and fixed her gaze on the Unknown Ore in the young woman’s hand.","\"Is that...?\"","\"Yes. This is one of them,\" the young woman replied as she handed it to the senior."]},{"number":2615,"title":"Chapter 2615: Red Zone","paragraphs":["The senior examined the glistening Unknown Ore in her hands. Had her junior not pointed out the anomaly, she would never have realized that it contained no energy.","\"How many Unknown Ores are like this?\" she asked after a moment of silence.","\"Sixty-one... so far.\"","\"That many?\" The senior’s eyes widened at the number.","Since this was the first time they had encountered such an issue, she had expected only a handful of ores to be affected. However, the actual number far exceeded her expectations.","\"Do we know where these ores came from?\" she asked a few seconds later.","\"We know they were collected by the military, but that’s about it. We only record the basic details, so we don’t keep track of their exact origins.\"","\"Well, starting now, that’s exactly what we’re going to do. We need to trace their origins and rule out any possibility of foul play.\"","\"Foul play...?\" The junior looked surprised. \"You think someone is responsible for this? It should be impossible for anyone outside this facility to extract Limitless from Unknown Ores.\"","\"As I said, we need to rule out every possibility, even those that seem impossible. I also find it difficult to believe that anyone outside this facility can extract Limitless from Unknown Ores. However, if someone truly has discovered a way, we must find them as soon as possible. It would be catastrophic if the other cities learned of their existence and got their hands on them.\"","\"Yes, Senior!\"","\"Also, I shouldn’t have to say this, but this information doesn’t leave this facility.\"","\"What about the Generals?\"","\"No... at least, not right now. We’ll do so once we gather more information and evidence.\"","\"I understand.\"","Two days later, Yuan arrived at the Eastern Gate for his mission.","Before he arrived, Yuan expected to see a large group of soldiers just like his previous gathering mission. However, he was surprised to find only five other soldiers present.","\"Is this everyone?\" Yuan asked.","\"No, there should be one more.\"","\"Why are there so few participants? Is it because there aren’t many soldiers permitted to enter the Red Zone?\" Yuan asked. \"As you can probably tell, this is my first time joining this kind of mission.\"","\"Your first time, huh? Well, it has nothing to do with a shortage of qualified soldiers. Plenty of them are permitted to enter the Red Zone. However, we aren’t searching for Unknown Ores—we’re looking for Unknown Crystals. They’re rarely found outside the tunnels, and the limited space inside means we can only bring seven or eight people at most.\"","\"Tunnels...?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow at this new information.","\"Is this your first time entering the Red Zone, too?\"","He nodded.","\"No wonder. Tunnels only exist in the Red Zone and beyond. As its name suggests, it’s a tunnel that goes underground.\"","\"Are there Void Specters inside these tunnels?\"","\"Of course. And unlike gathering Unknown Ores, we cannot ignore them, so we’ll have to get rid of them in order to reach the Unknown Crystals.\"","’Cleaning Void Specters while gathering resources at the same time? This mission offers the best of both worlds!’ Yuan exclaimed inwardly, already feeling impatient to go out there and start absorbing more Eternal Essence.","A few minutes later, the seventh member of the squad showed up.","\"Oh?\" Yuan muttered in a somewhat surprised voice after seeing Shi Fa’s face.","\"Why do you look so surprised? Don’t you take a look at who’s in your squad before the mission?\" Shi Fa asked as he approached the group.","\"No,\" Yuan said as he shook his head. \"I don’t really care who is in the squad, either.\"","\"Is that so? I won’t get into the details here, but you really should start looking,\" Shi Fa said. \"You want to make sure there aren’t any bad apples in your squad, after all.\"","Some time later, once they confirmed everyone was present, Shi Fa said, \"The system has appointed me as the squad leader. If there are any objections, speak up.\"","\"...\"","When no one voiced any objections, Shi Fa nodded and said, \"Alright. Then let’s go.\"","They teleported to the city walls shortly after, before traversing straight toward the Red Zone, ignoring every Void Specter they encountered along the way.","Of course, they also picked up every Unknown Ore they discovered.","\"So this is the Red Zone, huh?\" Yuan muttered as he entered it for the first time.","Beyond the barren landscape, a thin veil of crimson mist blanketed the sky, casting the entire region in an ominous red hue.","\"If you’re wondering about the red particles, you don’t have to worry. It’s not harmful,\" Shi Fa said to Yuan just in case he was concerned.","\"What is it?\" Yuan asked.","\"We don’t know, but we’re fairly certain it doesn’t affect us, as nobody has ever gotten sick from entering the Red Zone.\"","\"I see...\"","However, Yuan quietly examined the red mist with his divine sense.","’T-This is—!’","His eyes widened when he recognized it.","’This is Chaotic Essence!\"","At least that was his first impression.","’No, something isn’t right...’","He quickly realized something was different.","\"Now that we’re in the Red Zone, stay alert, especially you, Corporal Yuan, considering this is your first time here. The Void Specters behave differently in the Red Zone, and they are much more aggressive. However, if one attacks you, do not fight back and keep moving forward.\"","\"I understand.\"","As they continued forward, Yuan kept half of his attention focused on the crimson mist and the other half on the Void Specters.","’This is definitely Chaotic Essence, but it feels incomplete—like it had just formed. Could this be what Chaotic Essence is like before it develops its chaotic attribute and becomes the energy I’m familiar with?’ he speculated.","As Yuan spent more time examining the mist, he became more confident in his own theory.","He tried absorbing some of the red mist, but it had no effect on his Chaotic Essence. However, he could feel his energy being restored.","’It’s not strong enough to benefit me even in the slightest...’ he sighed inwardly, and he started to wonder if it was any different in the Purple Zone."]},{"number":2616,"title":"Chapter 2616: Red Zone(2)","paragraphs":["An hour after entering the Red Zone, one of the Void Specters suddenly attacked a soldier, forming an arm that shot forward like a spear.","Fortunately, the soldier remained alert and evaded it using Void Control.","However, the nearby Void Specters also started attacking, forcing everyone to use Void Control to teleport to safety, ignoring the Unknown Ores scattered nearby.","\"Are we just going to wander aimlessly and hope we find one of these tunnels?\" Yuan asked after several hours.","\"No.\"","Shi Fa responded by showing Yuan the small device he had been carrying ever since they entered the Red Zone.","\"Areas containing Unknown Crystals cause subtle changes in the surrounding atmosphere. This device can detect those fluctuations and guide us toward their source.\"","\"I’ve been wondering what that device was...\" Yuan muttered.","\"The only drawback of this device is its limited detection range,\" Shi Fa continued. \"So, to answer your earlier question, yes—we’re essentially wandering around until it detects something.\"","Several more hours passed, yet they still hadn’t found a tunnel. None of the soldiers in the squad spoke, each remaining fully focused on their surroundings and personal safety.","The atmosphere was a stark contrast to the Orange Zone, where everyone acted far more relaxed and casual.","As for Yuan, he’d stopped studying the red mist to look for the tunnels with his own methods.","’If Unknown Crystals are anything like Unknown Ores and contain Eternal Essence, I should be able to detect them. The only problem is...’","Unknown Ores were abundant throughout the Red Zone, with most of them buried underground. Their sheer number interfered with Yuan’s senses, making it difficult for him to distinguish any potential Unknown Crystals among them—or so he thought.","’What a tremendous amount of Eternal Essence! I can sense it all the way from here even though it’s so far away!’ Yuan cried inwardly when it suddenly entered his detection range.","However, there was a slight issue.","Rather than heading toward the source of the Eternal Essence, his squad was heading in another direction.","With no other choice, Yuan said to Shi Fa, who was the squad leader, \"Hey, this is going to sound weird, but my gut is telling me to head that way.\"","Yuan pointed in the direction of the energy.","Shi Fa followed his gesture and aimed the device that way, but it showed no reaction whatsoever.","When Shi Fa turned to look at him again, Yuan quickly spoke, \"My instincts are never wrong. Just trust me on this one.\"","\"Alright.\"","Knowing just how abnormal an existence Yuan was, Shi Fa didn’t doubt him for a moment and immediately instructed the squad to head in the direction he had indicated.","One... two... three...","Five more hours passed without the slightest reaction from Shi Fa’s device. Just as he began to doubt Yuan’s instincts, however, the device suddenly vibrated, and a red arrow appeared on its screen, pointing in the very direction they were already heading.","\"A-A tunnel! There’s a tunnel up ahead!\" Shi Fa announced to the others, his voice sounding a little shaken.","He turned to look at Yuan, who remained silent, but there was a smile hanging on his lips that said ’I told you so’.","Another hour later, they finally arrived at their destination—a cave-like burrow that descended deep underground.","\"I can’t believe we found one so quickly,\" said one of the soldiers.","\"Right? It’s normal to go weeks without finding one.\"","\"This is likely the fastest tunnel discovery in recent times.\"","\"And we have Corporal Yuan to thank for that,\" Shi Fa said.","\"What did it feel like when your instincts kicked in? You know, for future reference,\" one of the soldiers asked.","\"You know that strange feeling you sometimes get when you’re alone and suddenly feel like someone is watching you from afar? It felt something like that,\" Yuan replied, making up a random explanation on the spot.","\"I don’t get it... But I’ll keep it in mind.\"","\"Are we all ready?\" Shi Fa asked them a few moments later.","Everyone nodded.","\"Good. Then let’s—\"","Shi Fa suddenly stopped talking before looking at Yuan.","\"Once we go inside, just clear any Void Specter that is in our path.\"","\"Just my specialty,\" Yuan replied with a smile.","\"Then let’s go.\"","Shi Fa entered the burrow first, followed closely by Yuan and the others.","Once inside, the narrow passage widened considerably. What had initially been barely large enough for a single person to squeeze through soon became spacious enough for all seven members of the squad to walk side by side with room to spare.","However, it was incredibly dark inside. The light from the entrance only illuminated the first few meters, while everything beyond was swallowed by pitch-black darkness.","Of course, such darkness posed no obstacle to cultivators like them, whose vision in the dark was just as clear as it was under broad daylight.","It didn’t take long for them to encounter Void Specters. After only a few minutes of traversing the tunnel, they came across a group clustered together like a pile of trash, completely blocking the path.","\"I got it,\" Yuan said as he pointed his minigun at them.","\"H-Hey... be careful with that thing. We don’t want the tunnel to collapse—\"","One of the soldiers tried to warn Yuan, but he had already opened fire.","The others instinctively stepped back and prepared to flee. To their surprise, however, every bullet struck the Void Specters with perfect precision before vanishing upon impact, preventing them from piercing through and hitting the tunnel walls.","\"Hm? What were you saying?\" Yuan asked the soldier after clearing the tunnel.","\"N-Nothing...\"","Shi Fa chuckled and said, \"They don’t call him the Cleaning Maniac without reason. Anyway, let’s continue.\"","As they continued deeper into the tunnel, Shi Fa said to Yuan, \"I know you like to clean alone, but the Void Specters are much tougher in here than outside. When you start feeling tired, let us know.\"","Yuan nodded.","\"I know.\""]},{"number":2617,"title":"Chapter 2617: End of the Tunnel","paragraphs":["As Yuan and his squad ventured deeper into the tunnel, it gradually widened, and the number of Void Specters they encountered steadily increased.","While the others moved cautiously, Yuan could barely stop himself from rushing forward. The Void Specters within the Red Zone offered several times more Eternal Essence than those in the Orange Zone, not to mention their abundance.","’This place is a treasure trove, and I haven’t even encountered any Unknown Crystals yet!’ Yuan smiled inwardly.","After spending nearly three hours inside the tunnel, they finally discovered an Unknown Crystal. However, it was embedded deep within the wall.","\"So, is there a special process for extracting it, or can I simply yank it out?\" Yuan asked as the squad gathered around the crystal.","\"Stop! Don’t touch it!\" Shi Fa hastily said, even though Yuan wasn’t even reaching for it.","He quickly explained, \"Unlike Unknown Ores, Unknown Crystals contain so much energy that it’s dangerous to touch with your bare hands.\"","\"What’s the worse that can happen?\" Yuan asked out of curiosity.","\"You explode like a balloon.\" Shi Fa responded with a dead seriously expression.","\"I see.\"","Shi Fa retrieved a pair of gloves that had been reinforced with a powerful defensive formation and said, \"You can harvest it with this.\"","After wearing the gloves, Yuan grabbed the crystal and yanked it out of the wall like harvesting a radish.","The Unknown Crystal was double-terminated and roughly the length of an adult’s forearm, but most importantly, it contained an immense amount of Eternal Essence.","’This is about a million years’ worth of Eternal Essence!’ Yuan thought to himself as he quickly absorbed about fifty percent of it to see if it had any changes in its appearance.","After confirming that its appearance remained unchanged, just like the Unknown Ores, Yuan quickly absorbed another thirty percent of its energy.","Although he could have drained it completely, he chose to leave some behind. Unknown Crystals were far rarer and contained much more energy than Unknown Ores, so he would have felt far guiltier than absorbing a few Unknown Ores.","After storing the Unknown Crystal, they continued delving deeper into the tunnel, repeating the process of cleaning Void Specters and harvesting Unknown Crystals.","Four days later...","\"Hey, are you really not exhausted?\" One of the soldiers suddenly questioned Yuan, as he’d been cleaning thousands of Void Specters alone by this point.","\"No.\"","Yuan clearly answered.","\"How the hell is that even possible?\"","\"I’m starting to understand how he broke all of the Ironwoman’s records.\" Another remarked.","A few more days went by.","\"Seriously... there’s no way you’re not tired by now.\"","\"But I feel fine.\"","\"...\"","Another week passed in the blink of an eye.","\"This tunnel is much deeper than typical.\"","\"That just means there’ll be more reward in the end.\"","\"What is the end of a tunnel typically like?\" Yuan asked.","\"It’s usually where the majority of the Unknown Crystals are hidden, but it’s protected by a powerful Void Specter. It’s not something you can deal with alone, either.\"","\"I see. So like a guardian.\"","Several more hours later, Yuan suddenly announced, \"I can see the end.\"","\"Huh? Really?\"","However, even with their divine senses stretched to their limits, none of the others could perceive the end of the tunnel.","Despite their superior cultivation, their soul strength was incomparably weaker than Yuan’s, preventing their divine senses from reaching nearly as far.","Eventually, the others also came within range of the tunnel’s end, though it took another two hours of travel.","There, they found a pitch-black opening that plunged straight down into the depths.","\"There’s a good chance we’ll be attacked the moment we arrive at the bottom, so remain alert and be ready to use Void Control,\" Shi Fa said.","\"Are we ready?\"","Once everyone was ready, Shi Fa moved first, leaping into the hole and vanishing into the darkness below.","Yuan and the others immediately followed.","After falling for several minutes, Yuan spotted a faint light beneath them. It rapidly grew brighter, signaling that they were nearing the bottom.","Soon, they were engulfed by the light and emerged into a massive enclosed cavern. Dozens of Unknown Crystals were embedded throughout the walls, their glow illuminating the entire chamber.","However, at the center of the cavern loomed an enormous Void Specter several times larger than any they had encountered before, its massive form resembling a small mountain.","Just as Shi Fa had predicted, the Void Specter detected their presence almost immediately and launched a barrage of hundreds of tentacles from its massive body.","\"Scatter!\" Shi Fa shouted.","While everyone else focused on evading the tentacles, Yuan calmly aimed his minigun at the Void Specter.","\"Focus on defending yourself! Your bullets will likely be ineffective—\"","Before Shi Fa could finish speaking, immense Limitless surged from Yuan’s body as the minigun unleashed a relentless storm of bullets, firing tens of thousands every second at the Void Specter below.","The others assumed Yuan was panicking and expected him to exhaust his energy within moments. To their astonishment, however, he continued firing without pause for several minutes, completely overwhelming the Void Specter and riddling it with countless holes until its body ceased to exist.","\"W-What just happened...?\"","After confirming that the threat had been eliminated, the soldiers turned to Yuan with stupefied expressions, as though they had just witnessed the impossible.","As for Yuan, he completely ignored their stares and focused on absorbing the Eternal Essence left behind by the Void Specter. There was so much of it that, for once, he had to sit down and cultivate properly to absorb all of it.","The others didn’t question it since they figured that he’d exhausted himself and needed to rest.","\"L-Let’s stop standing around and harvest the Unknown Crystals before the tunnel collapses,\" Shi Fa spoke after snapping out of his daze a moment later.","Shi Fa’s voice snapped the others out of their daze, and they quickly started harvesting the Unknown Crystals while Yuan continued his cultivation."]},{"number":2618,"title":"Chapter 2618: Ironwoman","paragraphs":["\"I know we all just watched it happen right before our very eyes, but I still cannot believe that he’d managed to defeat a Void Guardian all by himself...\" one of the soldiers remarked as he harvested the Unknown Crystals.","\"I know exactly how you feel. It was such a surreal experience, especially considering that it normally takes a whole squad several hours to defeat one.\"","\"It was pretty amazing, but it’s not unprecedented. The Ironwoman defeated a Void Guardian by herself last year, too.\"","\"Can you really compare the two of them? The Ironwoman has been in the military for many years now, while Corporal Yuan just joined!\"","\"Right? Don’t downplay Corporal Yuan’s achievement! Not even the Ironwoman was defeating Void Guardians by herself as a new soldier!\"","\"By the way, what do you think he’s doing? I’ve never seen anyone sit in such a strange position before,\" one of the soldiers suddenly asked, referring to Yuan’s lotus position.","\"Isn’t he just resting?\"","\"Is he? It feels like he’s doing something more than that.\"","A few minutes later, Yuan opened his eyes and drew a deep breath.","’What a remarkable harvest. To think such an easy target would provide me with more than a billion years’ worth of Eternal Essence,’ he thought as he turned toward the others, who were collecting the last few Unknown Crystals.","Once every Unknown Crystal in the cavern had been collected, the squad gathered around Yuan.","\"Let’s leave as soon as possible. The tunnel usually collapses about a week after its guardian is defeated,\" Shi Fa said.","\"Sure. Let me carry some of those Unknown Crystals as well,\" Yuan offered.","However, Shi Fa shook his head. \"You’ve already done more than enough. Take it easy from here on and leave the chores to us.\"","\"Just let me carry them for a little—until we reach outside. If I stay idle for too long, my hands start to itch,\" Yuan insisted.","\"Fine...\"","Shi Fa sighed as he handed Yuan about thirty Unknown Crystals.","As they climbed the tunnel and traveled back to the surface, Yuan absorbed some of the Eternal Essence from the Unknown Crystals.","Since he’d already absorbed plenty from the Void Guardian, Yuan decided not to absorb too much, only between twenty-five and sixty percent from each crystal, ensuring there was no obvious pattern.","Once they left the tunnel and returned to the surface, they immediately started making their way back to the city.","Upon returning to the city, Shi Fa collected all of the Unknown Crystals and said, \"Thanks for the hard work, everyone, especially you, Corporal Yuan.\"","\"This mission ended much faster than it normally would, and it’s thanks to Corporal Yuan.\"","\"Not only was it fast, but it was relatively relaxing.\"","\"If you ever want to do another mission, you can contact me.\"","\"Me too!\"","\"You want to lower the chances of encountering a shitbag, after all.\"","\"A shitbag?\" Yuan repeated with a questioning expression.","\"To keep things simple, they are soldiers you don’t want to go on missions with because they will make things more difficult for everyone.\"","\"I’ll keep that in mind, but if you want to do another mission with me, I don’t mind.\"","\"Oh? When?\"","\"Right now.\"","\"...\"","\"Hahaha! Yeah, right.\" The soldiers laughed, assuming Yuan was merely joking.","\"Good one, Corporal Yuan. But seriously, contact us the next time you want to take another mission.\"","The soldiers departed shortly afterward.","\"See you next time.\" Shi Fa said, being the last to leave.","Unbeknownst to them, however, Yuan hadn’t been joking. The moment they all left, he headed straight to the mission hall to accept another assignment.","<Request has been sent>","<Request has been approved>","[Mission Details: Gather Unknown Crystals in the Red Zone. Meet at the Northern Gate at 0800 in 13 hours]","The following day, Yuan left the city with his new squad and began his mission.","\"Hm? He’s already gone on another mission?\" Mei Feng stared at the report before her with a dumbfounded expression. She had never encountered anyone so motivated—or so obsessed with taking missions.","\"If he continues at this pace, he’ll likely be promoted to Sergeant within a year...\" She paused briefly before adding, \"No, considering he has already completed a Red Zone mission, no one would question me even if I promoted him right now.\"","Suddenly, another voice rang out. \"Keeping such close tabs on him... You really like this guy, don’t you?\"","\"Are you jealous? I did the same thing with you when you first joined,\" Mei Feng replied calmly, turning toward the woman lounging lazily on the couch in her office.","\"...\"","\"Since you’re here, tell me what you think about him,\" Mei Feng said after a moment of silence. \"I know you’re also interested in him, ’Ironwoman’.\"","\"I don’t know what you want me to say, but I think he’s someone with a lot of secrets,\" said the Ironwoman.","\"Care to elaborate?\"","\"Remember his fight with Captain Gu during the recruitment?\"","\"Of course. You saved him.\"","\"Who? Corporal Yuan?\" The Ironwoman chuckled. \"That man didn’t need any saving. If I saved anything that day, it would be Captain Gu’s reputation.\"","\"What...?\" Mei Feng muttered, her expression filled with bewilderment.","\"That man was more than capable of defeating Captain Gu, yet he deliberately chose to lose. It’s not something you’d expect from someone who appears so carefree and unrestrained.\"","\"Where’d you find someone like that, anyway?\"","\"I didn’t.\" Mei Feng shook her head before revealing the truth. \"It was my daughter who found him.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"Then...\"","\"Don’t bother trying.\" Mei Feng suddenly interrupted. \"I won’t reveal any more information about him, even if it’s you... No... especially because it’s you.\"","\"What are you worried about? That I might try and steal him from you?\" The Ironwoman chuckled.","\"No, not you. Your family.\"","\"...\"","The Ironwoman fell silent for a moment before speaking again, \"Then you have even less of a reason to worry, as I haven’t spoken to them since coming to this city.\"","\"Anyway, enough about me. Although I don’t know Corporal Yuan well enough to say for certain, he doesn’t strike me as the type of person who would betray others.\"","\"I already know that,\" Mei Feng said.","\"Then why even ask me?\"","\"I wanted to see if you had any thoughts about adding him to your squad.\"","\"My squad?\" The Ironwoman mumbled with her eyebrows raised."]},{"number":2619,"title":"Chapter 2619: Ten Minutes Head Start","paragraphs":["\"You want to add Corporal Yuan to my squad? Did I hear you correctly?\" The Ironwoman asked with a surprised look on her face.","\"I’m just asking since you have full authority over your squad members. He has more than enough talent. Hell, if we’re being honest, he’s even more talented than you.\"","Ironwoman shook her head and said, \"This isn’t about talent alone. I admit that he is more talented than me—and everyone in my squad. However, his achievements are too lacking, and all he has on his record are some cleanup missions and two gathering missions. My squad specializes in extreme missions that most soldiers don’t even know exist.\"","\"I am well aware of that, but give him some time. It hasn’t even been half a year since he joined. And although he started out slow, he’s been picking things up lately. I wouldn’t be surprised if he starts doing missions in the Purple Zone within five years.\"","\"When and if he gets to that point, I’ll consider it. But right now, he doesn’t qualify.\"","A few days have passed since Yuan started his second mission in the Red Zone, and just as before, he led his squad to a tunnel using his instincts as an excuse.","\"We really found a tunnel... I will never doubt you again, Corporal Yuan!\" said the squad leader, who refused to listen to Yuan in the beginning and needed some convincing.","\"Then, as promised, we’ll clear the tunnel my way,\" Yuan said, as he’d made a bet with the squad leader on whether or not he’d find a tunnel.","\"Of course. You’ll enter alone, and we’ll follow you after ten minutes.\"","\"Good. Make sure to harvest any Unknown Crystals you see,\" Yuan reminded them before entering the tunnel alone.","Half a minute after Yuan disappeared into the tunnel, one of the soldiers asked, \"Should we really let him go inside alone?\"","\"That’s what he wants.\"","\"What if he dies? That would look terrible for the rest of us, regardless of whether it was his request or not.\"","\"I heard that General Mei had personally recruited him. If he dies...\"","\"Relax. It’s only ten minutes. What the hell could he possibly do alone in such a short time?\" said the squad leader.","Ten minutes later, the squad of six soldiers entered the tunnel.","\"Looks like he cleaned up some of the Void Specters,\" one of the soldiers remarked when they traveled for half an hour without seeing a single Void Specter.","An hour later...","\"I don’t think we’ll catch up to him if we keep moving at this pace. Let’s pick up the speed,\" the squad leader suggested, and the others readily agreed.","The squad immediately started running forward, though they remained vigilant as they advanced.","However, even after several hours of nonstop running—with only occasional stops to harvest nearby Unknown Ores—the soldiers still failed to catch up to Yuan.","\"How much farther ahead is he?! And how the hell is he clearing the Void Specters while still maintaining such a lead?!\"","The soldiers could hardly believe it.","\"Doesn’t he wield a minigun? How does he even have enough energy to deal with so many Void Specters alone?\"","\"He’s quite famous for that, actually.\"","Three more days passed without them encountering a single Void Specter or catching even a glimpse of Yuan. By this point, their initial shock had transformed into awe, accompanied by a faint sense of fear toward his unfathomable capabilities.","\"I can see the end of the tunnel!\" The squad leader announced.","\"He’s not here, either! Don’t tell me that he went to face the Void Guardian alone?!\"","The soldiers were expecting Yuan to wait for them at the end of the tunnel before facing the Void Guardian together.","\"I underestimated his arrogance and recklessness! Let’s hurry and hope he isn’t dead already!\"","The soldiers quickly steeled themselves before leaping into the hole and descending toward the chamber where the Void Guardian awaited.","When they finally emerged into the chamber, they expected to find Yuan locked in a fierce battle with the Void Guardian—or the creature alone after having already killed him.","What none of them expected, however, was to see Yuan standing there by himself, with the Void Guardian nowhere in sight.","\"W-What’s going on? Where’s the Void Guardian?\" The soldiers surveyed the chamber with dumbfounded expressions.","\"Don’t tell me there was no Void Guardian...\" one of the soldiers muttered.","\"A tunnel without a Void Guardian? That’s never happened before.\"","\"What happened, Corporal Yuan? Was the place already empty when you arrived?\" the squad leader asked, turning to Yuan—the only person who could explain what had occurred.","\"The Void Guardian? There was one, but I defeated it right before you all arrived,\" he responded in a calm voice, acting like what he’d done was nothing out of the ordinary.","\"YOU WHAT?!\"","The soldiers exclaimed simultaneously, their eyes popping out of their sockets in shock.","\"Y-You defeated a Void Guardian... all by yourself?\" the squad leader muttered in a daze.","As difficult as it was to believe Yuan, there was no other plausible explanation. A Void Guardian had never been absent while the chamber still contained Unknown Crystals, especially when it remained filled with them, as if nobody had touched them.","Eventually, the soldiers snapped out of their daze and harvested the Unknown Crystals while Yuan rested.","\"We’re done.\"","The squad gathered by Yuan some time later.","\"Alright. Let’s leave.\"","Yuan did not need to absorb the Eternal Essence since he’d already done so long before they arrived at the scene.","After they returned to the military base, Yuan asked them, \"Since we’re already here, want to go on another mission?\"","The soldiers could only stare at him in silence, looking like they’d just heard something absurd.","\"Even if you’re being serious... I am mentally exhausted and need to rest.\"","\"Me too.\"","The soldiers politely declined Yuan’s offer before going their separate ways.","Yuan didn’t mind and calmly made his way to the mission hall again."]},{"number":2620,"title":"Chapter 2620: Growing In Reputation","paragraphs":["Unlike Yuan’s first squad, the soldiers from his second mission made no attempt to keep quiet about his capabilities.","As soon as they saw their friends, they began spreading word of everything that had happened, revealing that Yuan had practically cleared an entire tunnel by himself—including its Void Guardian.","Of course, few people believed such an outrageous rumor. In their eyes, no matter how talented Yuan was, he had only recently joined the military and had spent most of his time completing cleanup missions. There was simply no way someone so inexperienced could already clear an entire tunnel and defeat its Void Guardian all by himself.","\"Come on, man. You’d have to be insane to believe such a fairytale. Even the Ironwoman had only managed to defeat a Void Guardian by herself a year ago, and she’d been in the military for over a decade!\"","\"I know very well what Corporal Yuan is capable of, considering I’ve accompanied him on a cleanup mission before. As much credit as I’m willing to give him, there’s no way he has already reached a level where he can defeat a Void Guardian by himself.\"","\"Who the hell is spreading these rumors? If a mere Corporal can defeat a Void Guardian by himself, I can defeat the Void Hunter by myself!\"","However, even though the majority of soldiers did not believe the rumors, a few did.","\"Where’s Corporal Yuan?\" Sergeant Bing asked Sergeant Quang.","\"I haven’t heard from him since his first mission in the Red Zone.\"","\"Don’t tell me that he already went on another mission?\"","\"It’s very likely...\"","A little over a week later, Yuan returned from his third mission. Once again, his squad members eagerly spread word of his achievements among their friends.","\"What’s with that disappointed look?\" one of the soldiers asked after noticing his friend’s reaction to the story.","\"Do you have any idea how many times I’ve heard that rumor? It’s been spreading for over a week now! At this point, there’s probably nobody who hasn’t heard it already, so you can stop exaggerating,\" the soldier’s friend said, explaining his frustration.","\"What are you talking about?\"","Having been away on a mission the entire time, the soldier had no idea about the rumor, nor the fact that Yuan joined their mission literally right after his last one.","\"How could it have been circulating for a week when we literally just returned from the mission?\"","\"Huh? What do you mean?\"","The soldier then explained that he had just completed a mission with Yuan and that everything he had said had happened during that very mission—not the one everyone had been talking about for the past week.","\"What?! Are you serious?!\"","\"You don’t believe me? You can ask the others!\"","Thus, the rumor began spreading once more. This time, with a second squad corroborating the story, it became far more credible.","Shortly afterward, a third squad came forward and revealed that they had actually been the first to witness Yuan defeat a Void Guardian by himself.","\"G-General! Have you heard of the rumors about Corporal Yuan yet?\"","An officer asked General Mei over the phone.","\"You’re the sixth person to call me about this today,\" Mei Feng sighed.","\"Do you think it’s true?\"","\"Well, I’d certainly rather believe it than assume more than twenty soldiers conspired to lie and exaggerate Corporal Yuan’s achievements.\"","\"What if it’s one of General Gu’s schemes?\" the officer asked.","\"And what would he possibly gain from such a scheme? Making the other soldiers jealous of Yuan—or provoking them into targeting him? Also, half of the soldiers spreading the rumors are from my division.\"","\"Are you going to do something about this?\" the officer suddenly asked. \"You should already be aware of how many officers are trying to recruit him into their squad. The only reason they haven’t approached him yet is because of your influence. However, if his reputation continues to grow at this rate, they may decide to disregard you and try to recruit him themselves.\"","\"So what?\" Mei Feng replied calmly. \"It’s not like I have a squad for him to join. Whatever Corporal Yuan chooses to do as a soldier is no longer my concern—as long as he doesn’t side with General Gu, not that I can imagine him ever doing so.\"","Meanwhile, several officers sat inside General Gu’s office, each wearing a solemn, contemplative expression.","\"If these rumors are true—that Corporal Yuan can already defeat a Void Guardian by himself—our initial plan to lure him into the Red Zone wouldn’t work on him,\" one of them eventually sighed aloud.","\"Then we adjust the plan! If the Red Zone won’t do, we’ll take him out in the Purple Zone! And if that doesn’t work out, there’s still the Black Zone!\" General Gu shouted as he angrily slammed his desk.","\"While you’re all wasting your time here, that bastard is improving at an unfathomable pace! At this rate, he’ll become so powerful that even we cannot touch him!\"","\"W-We can act swiftly, but that would be extremely risky—\"","\"I don’t give a fuck anymore! We need to stop him from growing, or he’ll become another thorn in my path like that Ironwoman!\"","After a moment of silence, one of the officers said, \"I understand. I’ll expedite the plans and get rid of him as soon as possible.\"","While Yuan’s reputation within the military continued to soar, he himself had gone on another mission, starting his fourth.","\"Is it true? That you can clear a tunnel and defeat the Void Guardian by yourself?\"","The soldiers in his squad asked him before they departed the city.","Yuan calmly nodded.","\"So you can just sit back and let me do all of the work,\" he said with a smile.","\"...\"","The soldiers exchanged dumbfounded gazes with each other.","Suddenly, one of them asked, \"If you don’t mind me asking... why do you insist on doing all of the work by yourself? Even if you’re capable, it doesn’t make sense to push yourself this hard.\"","\"It’s quite simple, actually.\" Yuan faced the soldiers and responded with a serious expression, \"Because it’s much safer and faster if I do it alone.\""]},{"number":2621,"title":"Chapter 2621: Corporal Yuan","paragraphs":["\"Safer? How is it safer?\" one of the soldiers couldn’t help but ask.","\"I have heard from others that deaths are not uncommon when fighting the Void Guardian,\" Yuan said. \"Since I can defeat them alone, why risk others’ lives?\"","\"But wouldn’t that just put your own life at risk?\"","Although the soldiers were grateful that Yuan cared enough about their safety to endanger himself, the thought of him doing so still didn’t sit right with them.","Yuan chuckled and said, \"My life is not at risk. I can fight a dozen of them alone if I wanted to, let alone a single one.\"","The soldiers’ jaw dropped to the ground at his arrogant claims, but they decided not to comment on it.","They left the city shortly afterward and began their mission.","Meanwhile, inside the facility that extracted Unknown Ores and Unknown Crystals for energy, a group of individuals gathered to discuss a certain issue.","\"So, the anomaly isn’t limited to Unknown Ores, and even some of the newer Unknown Crystals have been found to be missing some of their energy,\" one of them muttered in a troubled tone as a small mountain of Unknown Cores and Unknown Crystals lay piled on the table before them.","\"Are the Unknown Crystals truly missing energy? What if they’re simply of lower quality? Not every Unknown Crystal contains the same amount of energy, after all,\" someone asked.","\"Did you even read the report before coming here? They aren’t missing just a small amount of energy. Most have lost at least twenty-five percent, while some are missing more than half of what they would normally contain! The discrepancy is far too great to dismiss as a difference in quality!\"","\"Are these all the affected ores and crystals?\"","\"They are... so far. The amount may seem insignificant for now, but if we fail to identify the cause and the anomaly continues to spread, we could be facing a catastrophe in the near future.\"","\"Have we learned anything about this anomaly yet? Could it simply be a natural phenomenon? If that’s the case, I’m not sure there’s anything we can do about it.\"","\"Not yet. However, we have discovered a coincidence—or a connection.\"","One of the individuals snapped her fingers, causing a screen to materialize before the group. Displayed on the projection was the profile of a certain individual.","\"Corporal Yuan?\" another individual read aloud, a puzzled look crossing his face.","\"After discovering the anomaly, we began tracing the origins of the affected resources. According to the records, every one of them was collected by soldiers during missions, and Corporal Yuan was the only one who had participated in all of said missions.\"","\"That is certainly suspicious.\"","\"Wait until you hear more about this Corporal Yuan...\"","The screen flickered, revealing more detailed information about him.","As the individuals examined the new information, their expressions gradually shifted from curiosity to disbelief.","\"As you can see for yourself, there’s practically no information about him, except that he’d joined the military a few months ago and broke multiple records during his recruitment.\"","\"No records before joining the military? It’s like... he materialized out of thin air...\"","\"Look at those data! There’s no way someone this talented could be a nobody! I’m willing to bet that someone erased his data to keep his identity a secret.\"","\"Haven’t we seen something like this before?\"","\"You mean the Ironwoman? She’s a different story. Her information wasn’t erased, but sealed. There’s a big difference. Also, nobody has the authority to completely erase an individual’s background from the system.\"","\"I beg to differ.\" Someone said. \"There is one person who can do that—the one who made the system.\"","\"...\"","The room suddenly fell silent.","\"Are you suggesting that Gaia is responsible for erasing Corporal Yuan’s information? Why would they do something like that?\"","\"You already know that no one but Gaia could answer that question.\"","\"So, are we supposed to assume that Corporal Yuan is somehow connected to Gaia now?\"","\"What? Of course not. There’s no evidence that—\"","\"There is, though. Corporal Yuan’s lackluster record that looks like it’d been deliberately cleaned.\"","\"That’s just an assumption.\"","\"It’s also an assumption that he has anything to do with the anomaly. We can’t go around accusing someone like that, especially if they’re connected with General Mei.\"","\"Speaking of General Mei, looks like she recruited him... just like she recruited the Ironwoman.\"","\"Must be a coincidence. That woman attracts the strangest but also the most talented people, after all.\"","\"In the end, it all points to Gaia.\"","\"Then how should we proceed with this new information?\"","\"...\"","\"If Gaia is truly already involved, then there’s nothing for us to do.\"","\"Haa...\" The most senior there sighed while rubbing her eyes. \"In any case, since we still lack concrete evidence that Corporal Yuan is connected with the anomaly, we will continue monitoring the situation and Corporal Yuan closely.\"","The meeting ended shortly after with no real progress.","\"Corporal Yuan, huh? Just who are you... and where did you come from?\"","A week later, Yuan returned from his fourth mission.","\"My lord, Corporal Yuan! You’re even more capable than the rumors give you credit!\"","The soldiers in his squad praised him as they returned to the military base.","\"If you ever want to go on another mission, don’t hesitate to find me!\"","\"Sure.\"","Yuan didn’t bother trying to ask them to go on another mission this time.","The squad disbanded shortly afterward.","Instead of heading straight to the mission hall to accept another assignment as one would expect, Yuan made his way to the training hall.","Of course, he wanted to see how much closer he’d gotten to defeating the entity on the 46th floor.","A few hours and many attempts later, Yuan emerged from the training hall.","’Although I am still nowhere near defeating it, I can at least see clear progress. If I continue defeating Void Guardians and absorbing energy from Unknown Crystals, it won’t be long before I have enough Eternal Essence to conquer it!’ Yuan thought to himself as he made his way toward the mission hall."]},{"number":2622,"title":"Chapter 2622: A New Mission","paragraphs":["When Yuan arrived at the mission hall, he immediately noticed that nearly everyone inside was glaring at him.","Of course, there was no malice behind their stares. They were simply curious and a little awestruck to finally see Corporal Yuan, who had been a hot topic lately.","\"Is that him?\"","\"Yep. That’s the Cleaning Maniac.\"","\"This might sound strange, but he looks... out of place. Like he doesn’t belong here.\"","\"I know what you mean. He’s practically a monster walking among humans.\"","\"No, I mean something about him feels otherworldly.\"","The soldiers chatted among themselves without pause, yet for some reason, not a single one dared to approach Yuan.","Eventually, just as Yuan was about to reach the machines to accept a mission, several soldiers finally gathered the courage to approach him.","However, before they could reach him, another group suddenly cut them off.","\"Hey, watch where you’re—\" The soldier who had been shoved aside was about to curse, but the words died in his throat the moment he saw their faces and recognized who they were.","Then, without a word, they backed away and silently watched as this group of soldiers approached Yuan.","\"Are you Corporal Yuan?\"","The group consisted of five individuals, and the one who addressed him was a tall, broad-shouldered man.","Yuan turned toward them. \"Who’s asking?\"","The man frowned. \"Is that any way to speak to your superior?\"","Yuan glanced at the insignia on the man’s chest. Two black bars. It was the same rank that Captain Gu had.","However, before Yuan could respond, another soldier from the group stepped forward with a friendly smile.","\"There’s no need to be so tense. I’m Captain Chen, and this large, stern-looking fellow is Captain Dung. You don’t need to be overly formal with us, either.\"","\"In that case... what do you want from me?\"","\"We have a proposition for you, but it’s not something we can talk about here. Can we go somewhere more quiet?\"","\"Can it wait until I grab my mission?\" Yuan asked.","Captain Chen chuckled and said, \"You won’t even care about your mission once you hear what we have in store for you.\"","\"Is that so?\"","After pondering for a moment, Yuan nodded.","\"Sure, let’s go.\"","Captain Chen wasn’t expecting Yuan to agree so readily, but he remained calm and said, \"Follow us.\"","Once Yuan left with the group, the soldiers began mumbling to each other.","\"Wasn’t that...?\"","\"Yes...\"","\"I wonder what sort of business they have with Corporal Yuan.\"","\"They’re probably going to confirm the rumors.\"","\"You mean whether he can really defeat a Void Guardian by himself or not?\"","Meanwhile, after leaving the mission hall, Yuan followed Captain Chen and the other four soldiers to a private room.","\"Before I reveal our offer to you, I must ask you something. I heard that you’ve been doing missions nonstop. Is there a reason you’re working so hard?\" Captain Chen asked Yuan.","\"To receive fast promotions, of course.\"","\"Is it really so simple?\"","\"Why else would I be doing so many missions? Isn’t it the goal of every soldier to raise their ranks?\" Yuan shrugged.","\"Fair enough, as I was once just like you.\" Captain Chen gave a hearty laugh. \"Anyway, let’s get to the point.\"","\"Corporal Yuan, how would you like to join us on a mission?\"","\"I’m listening,\" Yuan responded, looking like his interest was piqued.","\"It’s a gathering mission, similar to the ones you’ve been doing, but on a much larger scale, and it will take place in the Purple Zone. If you want to receive fast promotions, then you can only go above and beyond.\"","\"The Purple Zone, huh? That does sound interesting... However, don’t I need to pass an exam before I can accept missions there, as I did for the Red Zone?\" Yuan asked.","\"Normally, yes. However, with the approval and supervision of at least three captains, you can receive special permission to enter the Purple Zone, and as you can see, there are five of us here.\"","Yuan pondered for a moment before asking, \"May I ask why you’re inviting a mere corporal like me to join your mission? If you’re short on members, surely there are plenty of more qualified soldiers available.\"","\"To be honest, we’ve heard a lot of stories about you, and we’d like to see for ourselves if they’re true. More importantly, we want to find out where your limits truly lie. If you’re worried about the danger, don’t be. We’ll make sure nothing happens to you.\"","Yuan closed his eyes and seemed to be pondering again.","Worried that Yuan might refuse, Captain Chen suddenly added, \"If you complete the mission, we’ll recommend you for a meritorious promotion.\"","\"I was waiting for you to say that.\" Yuan opened his eyes and said with a smile. \"When do we start?\"","\"We can leave for the mission right now.\"","\"Then what are we waiting for? Let’s get started!\" Yuan exclaimed excitedly, showing a level of impatience that might lead one to think it was his first mission.","\"Alright. Then let’s leave for the mission now.\"","Without any delay, they immediately made their way to the northern gate.","Upon reaching the gate, they headed straight for the teleporter, bypassing the soldiers stationed there.","This was a first for Yuan, as the guards normally checked the identity of everyone in the squad and their mission details before allowing them to use the teleporter.","However, the soldiers on duty did not say anything, merely giving them a glance before turning a blind eye to it.","Seeing this, Yuan confirmed his suspicions.","’Looks like they’ve finally decided to act,’ he smiled inwardly, as he’d been waiting for this opportunity.","Despite knowing full well that he was walking into a trap, Yuan stepped into it willingly—even gleefully. After all, this opportunity would allow him to enter the Purple Zone far sooner than he had anticipated.","Shortly after Yuan left the city, Mei Feng received word that several of General Gu’s soldiers had approached him inside the mission hall and taken him somewhere."]},{"number":2623,"title":"Chapter 2623: Scorpion Squad","paragraphs":["\"Say that again for me.\"","A deep frown formed on Mei Feng’s face when she heard the news.","\"T-There have been reports that several officers under General Gu approached Corporal Yuan in the mission hall and took him somewhere. We’re currently trying to locate them,\" one of Mei Feng’s officers reported after barging into her office.","After a moment of silence, Mei Feng turned her gaze toward Sergeant Bing and Sergeant Quang, who were also in the room, their heads lowered, as if trying to hide the shame on their faces.","\"Where were the two of you when that happened?\" Mei Feng asked them in a calm yet cold voice.","\"We have no excuses,\" Sergeant Quang said as he raised his head to look at Mei Feng with a resolute face, as if he accepted his fate.","Sergeant Bing spoke up a moment later. \"I’m not trying to make excuses, but Corporal Yuan always heads straight to the mission hall after returning from a mission. We never expected them to make a move in such a crowded, public place. Besides, we usually don’t even learn that he’s back until he’s already accepted and left for another mission.\"","Mei Feng rubbed her eyes and sighed. \"As much as I want to blame you, I can’t ignore my own complacency. I should have seen this coming, especially after his reputation began rising so rapidly.\"","She had already known that General Gu felt threatened by Yuan’s talent. Once Yuan’s reputation started soaring, she should have anticipated that General Gu would eventually make a move.","\"And for it to be the Scorpion Squad... It’s like they don’t even care about hiding their intentions...\" Mei Feng sighed again.","\"Did you say the Scorpion Squad?!\" Sergeant Bing exclaimed in shock.","The Scorpion Squad was infamous for its ruthlessness. Its members constantly disregarded regulations and were widely regarded as nothing more than a band of troublemakers.","However, because they were talented and came from influential backgrounds, none of them had experienced any real accountability, especially with General Gu protecting them.","Suddenly, someone knocked on the door and spoke loudly from outside, \"General! I have information on Corporal Yuan’s whereabouts!\"","\"Enter!\"","Once the soldier was inside, he revealed that some soldiers witnessed Corporal Yuan at the northern gate.","\"Some even claimed they saw Corporal Yuan using the teleporter!\"","Hearing this, Mei Feng immediately searched the system to determine whether Yuan had officially accepted a mission. As she had expected, however, no such record existed.","\"Bring the soldiers from the northern gate to me for questioning!\" Mei Feng commanded the soldier.","\"Yes!\"","\"They must have lured Corporal Yuan outside the city. However, I doubt they’d be foolish enough to kill him outright. They’ll most likely try to make his death look like an accident,\" said the other officer in the room.","Mei Feng turned to her and said, \"Discreetly dispatch several squads to search for Corporal Yuan. If my guess is correct, they’re likely headed to the Purple Zone.\"","Then, she stood up and started walking toward the door.","\"Where are you going?\"","\"A little chat with General Gu. You can bring the soldiers on duty to his office,\" she said before disappearing entirely.","\"I’d like to volunteer for the search,\" Sergeant Quang said to the officer.","\"Me too,\" said Sergeant Bing.","\"Even if you didn’t ask, I would’ve sent you so.\"","While Sergeant Quang and Bing prepared for their mission, Mei Feng went to General Gu’s office.","When the guards saw Mei Feng, they said nothing and silently stepped aside, allowing her to enter General Gu’s office.","However, unlike her previous visit, Mei Feng did not enter calmly. She kicked the door off its hinges, startling everyone inside.","\"G-General Mei?! What are you doing?!\"","\"Even if you’re a General, you can’t just barge in here like a bandit!\"","General Gu was not alone in the office, and several other officers were present.","\"What brings you here this time, General Mei?\" General Gu greeted her calmly, as though he had been expecting her arrival.","\"You know damn well why I am here,\" she responded as she walked into the room, ignoring the others. \"Where did you take Corporal Yuan?\"","\"You’re making it sound as though I had him kidnapped.\" General Gu raised an eyebrow, appearing genuinely puzzled by the accusation.","\"Numerous witnesses saw the Scorpion Squad take Corporal Yuan out on an unauthorized mission.\"","\"An unauthorized mission? How can you be certain they’re even on one? And even if they are, I fail to see why that warrants such concern—much less why you would assume I ordered them to abduct him. They may belong to my division, but they are also officers with the authority to bring soldiers on missions at their own discretion.\"","\"As we’re all likely aware, Corporal Yuan has become quite the topic of discussion lately. I wouldn’t be surprised if they took him to a tunnel to see for themselves whether he can truly defeat a Void Guardian alone. Besides, with five captains accompanying him, I highly doubt anything will happen.\"","Mei Feng sneered. \"If a group of notorious troublemakers secretly taking away a talent you failed to recruit—and nearly killed during the recruitment—isn’t enough to warrant my concern, then I don’t know what is.\"","General Gu shook his head and sighed. \"That is another serious accusation, General Mei. I understand that you’re still upset about what happened during the recruitment, but Captain Gu had no intention of killing him.\"","He continued, \"And while I admit that the Scorpion Squad has earned a certain degree of infamy, that alone does not justify treating them like criminals. Moreover, they have been making an effort to improve their behavior lately, and their increasingly positive reputation is proof that they genuinely wish to change for the better.\"","Suddenly, another officer in the room spoke up. \"General Gu is right, General Mei. At this point, you’re merely hurling baseless accusations. Unless you have solid evidence that supports your claim, please leave for now and allow us to finish our meeting that you’d so brazenly disturbed.\"","One might have assumed that everyone present supported General Gu, but in truth, many of the officers remained neutral and had taken neither side.","However, their presence there was not a coincidence."]},{"number":2624,"title":"Chapter 2624: Purple Zone","paragraphs":["\"I’ve heard your concerns, General Mei, and I will personally look into the matter. For now, I must ask that you leave us,\" General Gu said solemnly. \"Unless, of course, you intend to threaten me as you did before.\"","However, Mei Feng made no move to leave. Moments later, the guards stationed at the northern gate were escorted into the office.","\"What is it now?\" General Gu sighed.","\"These soldiers were on duty when the Scorpion Squad escorted Corporal Yuan out of the city. I would like to know why they ignored protocol and allowed them to leave without verifying their identities and mission details.\"","\"Well? What do you soldiers have to say for yourselves?\" General Gu turned to the guards.","The soldiers immediately lowered their heads.","\"W-We were in the wrong! We were slacking off and did not bother to verify their identities!\"","\"And... they were all officers with well-established reputations...\"","Rather than making excuses or attempting to lie, they openly admitted their negligence and accepted responsibility.","General Gu turned to Mei Feng and said, \"It’s not as though this is the first time soldiers have grown complacent and neglected their duties. It was simply an unfortunate coincidence that it happened under these circumstances.\"","He continued, \"I’ll personally see that they’re punished accordingly. Of course, if it would ease your concerns, I’m willing to let you decide their punishment yourself.\"","\"Don’t worry. I’ll make sure they receive the harshest punishment permitted, so others will think twice before making the same mistake,\" Mei Feng said before turning toward the destroyed doorway.","Just as she reached the exit, she stopped.","\"If anything happens to Corporal Yuan...\"","However, she left the threat unfinished and walked away.","Once Mei Feng’s presence could no longer be sensed, the officers in the room turned toward General Gu with perplexed expressions.","Although they agreed that Mei Feng lacked sufficient evidence to directly accuse him, they were also well aware of General Gu’s character. Deep down, many of them suspected that he had something to do with the Scorpion Squad secretly taking Yuan out of the city, especially considering that they were ’coincidentally’ present during Mei Feng’s appearance.","Eventually, one of them spoke up. \"I don’t know what kind of conflict the two of you are caught up in, but please leave us out of it from now on. You practically dragged us into it today.\"","None of them were fools. They understood perfectly well that General Gu had used their presence as both witnesses and a shield against General Mei.","General Gu offered no response, neither confirming nor denying their suspicions. Instead, he simply resumed the meeting as though nothing had happened.","Meanwhile, as Mei Feng walked away, she reflected on her own misstep.","’I was too rash today and walked straight into that man’s trap...’ she sighed inwardly. ’At least I confirmed that he had something to do with Yuan’s disappearance... Now I just need to find him before anything happens...\"","When Mei Feng returned to her office, she raised an eyebrow upon noticing a masked figure standing outside.","Unfazed by their presence, she asked, \"What do you want now?\"","\"I heard about the situation.\"","\"And?\"","\"I happen to have nothing to do now, so I could help with the search.\"","\"The Ironwoman willingly going on a search mission? Aren’t you worried that might affect your reputation?\" Mei Feng said. \"You’ve always refused to accept such missions, after all.\"","\"This is different. It’d be a pity for someone who is being called my future rival to die so soon.\"","\"Well, if you’re going to help, I have no reason to refuse.\"","Thus, the Ironwoman decided to join in on the search.","Meanwhile, Yuan and the Scorpion Squad arrived at Red Zone after a few days of traveling without rest.","As they approached the Purple Zone, Yuan noticed the crimson mist in the air gradually darkening, its color slowly shifting toward a light shade of purple.","That light purple darkened as they got closer to the Purple Zone.","’As expected, the further we go, the more closely this mist resembles Chaotic Essence...’ Yuan thought to himself after examining it.","However, it was still nowhere near the point where it’d strengthen his Chaotic Essence.","\"How are you feeling, Corporal Yuan?\" Sergeant Chen suddenly spoke to Yuan for the first time since they left the city. \"Feeling nervous... or scared yet?\"","\"Honestly, I am a little nervous,\" Yuan calmly lied.","\"With us with you, what is there to be worried about?\" Captain Chen laughed.","Some time later, they arrived at the Purple Zone, where the color of the mist was a deep violet.","\"Let’s go. We have already located a tunnel, so it won’t be long before we arrive at our destination,\" said Captain Chen.","Without any questions, Yuan followed them into the Purple Zone.","He glanced at the Void Specters that wandered below.","Even without fighting them, he could tell that they were incomparably stronger than the ones in the Red Zone, but this also meant they would have more Eternal Essence.","’Can’t wait to absorb their Eternal Essence.’ Yuan thought to himself as he smiled inwardly.","However, before they could even reach the tunnel, they had to survive the countless Void Specters that relentlessly attacked them.","As they traveled through the Purple Zone, Yuan and the others had to use Void Control almost constantly.","Although the Scorpion Squad had known from the start that getting rid of Yuan wouldn’t be simple, they had still hoped he would meet an early end.","But alas, to their disappointment, several days passed, and the group arrived at the tunnel safe and sound.","\"That wasn’t as bad as I was expecting,\" Yuan casually remarked after they cleaned up the Void Specters around the tunnel.","\"We are still in the outer areas of the Purple Zone, so it’s not too bad,\" said Captain Chen.","\"But things will get dangerous once we enter the tunnel, so make sure you stay alert.\"","\"I get to clear the tunnel by myself, right?\" Yuan then asked.","\"Of course. How else are we supposed to see what you’re really capable of?\" Captain Chen replied with a smile. \"But don’t worry. If things get too dangerous, we’ll step in.\""]},{"number":2625,"title":"Chapter 2625: Elite Void Specter","paragraphs":["Yuan entered the tunnel shortly afterward, with the Scorpion Squad following close behind.","At first glance, the tunnel looked no different from the ones he had explored before. However, the deeper they ventured, the more apparent the differences became. The passage gradually widened, and before long, it branched into two separate paths.","\"Which way do we go?\" Yuan asked Captain Chen. \"I’ve never seen tunnels branch like this before.\"","\"I’m not surprised. This only happens in the Purple Zone,\" Captain Chen replied.","\"As for which path to take... it doesn’t really matter. Well, it does, but they all eventually lead to the same destination. The only difference is what you’ll encounter along the way. Some paths have far more Void Specters than others, while some have tougher ones. Of course, if you’re unlucky, it could be both.\"","They hadn’t encountered a single Void Specter up to this point, but Yuan had a feeling that would change very soon.","Without giving much thought to it, Yuan picked the right path.","The Scorpion Squad didn’t say anything and quietly followed.","As expected, it didn’t take long before they encountered their first Void Specter.","However, even without engaging it, Yuan could tell at a glance that this Void Specter was vastly different from any he had encountered before, including those roaming the Purple Zone outside.","Not only did it emit a unique aura unlike the others, but its form was also far more humanoid.","’An Elite Void Specter!’","The members of the Scorpion Squad cried inwardly the moment they saw the Void Specter. There was only one, yet its mere presence sent chills down their spines.","Elite Void Specters were, as their name implied, the elite among Void Specters. Although they were not as powerful as Void Guardians, they were still exceedingly difficult to deal with in their own right due to their speed and high durability.","Under normal circumstances, encountering an Elite Void Specter—especially as their first encounter—would be considered incredibly unlucky.","However, given their current circumstances, the Scorpion Squad couldn’t help but rejoice at Yuan’s misfortune, seeing it as a stroke of good luck for themselves.","’To think we’d encounter an Elite Void Specter so soon! The heavens must also want to see this guy dead as much as we do!’ Captain Chen laughed inwardly.","\"Good luck, Corporal Yuan.\"","Captain Chen said, not even bothering to explain to Yuan what he was facing.","\"Hmm...\"","Rather than fighting it immediately, Yuan examined the Elite Void Specter from afar.","\"What’s wrong? Cold feet?\" Captain Dung asked when Yuan did not move after moments of stillness.","\"No, I was just thinking that my minigun won’t be effective on it,\" Yuan calmly remarked.","Despite his near-limitless reserves of energy, Yuan’s cultivation was still lacking, which meant there was only so much power he could draw from Limitless at once.","His minigun was devastating against large groups and could shred through them with ease, but only because the strength of his Limitless was sufficient to overwhelm them; hence why it took him several minutes of nonstop attacking to defeat the Void Guardian during his first gathering mission.","\"Then how are you going to fight it? With your fists?\" Captain Chen inquired with a puzzled face.","\"Nope.\"","Yuan raised his minigun toward the Elite Void Specter, raising the others’ eyebrows.","\"I thought you said it wasn’t going to be effective,\" Captain Chen remarked.","\"Correct, but that doesn’t mean it won’t work. I also want to test out its limits.\"","Yuan’s words left them speechless, as nobody would be foolish enough to test the capabilities of an Elite Void Specter if they knew about it. However, they kept quiet, and moments later, Yuan began firing a barrage of Limitless bullets at the Elite Void Specter.","\"Oh?\" Yuan muttered in surprise a few seconds later.","Although his bullets initially struck their target, the Elite Void Specter began evading them the moment it realized it was under attack.","Yuan immediately increased his output, but that only worked for several bullets before the Elite Void Specter adapted to it and began evading them perfectly again.","Soon, the Elite Void Specter was right in front of Yuan, and it swung its scythe-like arms at him.","’Die!’ Captain Chen prayed inwardly.","However, Yuan used Void Manipulation and avoided the attack with ease.","\"Looks like this weapon won’t work on you...\"","Without hesitation, Yuan dropped the minigun and proceeded to raise two fingers.","The members of Scorpion Squad were puzzled by his actions, wondering if he really intended on fighting the Elite Void Specter with his hands.","When the Elite Void Specter attacked again half a second later, Limitless suddenly surged from Yuan’s hands. However, instead of dispersing in every direction like an unrestrained aura, the energy condensed into a distinct shape—a sword.","Sha!","Before the members of the Scorpion Squad could even comprehend what they had witnessed, the Elite Void Specter abruptly froze in front of Yuan.","A split second later, dozens of cuts appeared across its body before it dispersed into the air like smoke.","\"W-What just happened?!\" Captain Chen exclaimed in shock, turning to the others for an explanation.","However, the others shook their heads, as none of them saw what Yuan did just now.","Meanwhile, Yuan quickly absorbed the Eternal Essence left behind by the Elite Void Specter.","’That was about a hundred million years’ worth of Eternal Essence! Although not as much as a Void Guardian, it’s still plenty!’ Yuan thought to himself.","A moment later, Yuan turned to the Scorpion Squad and said, \"Alright, let’s keep going.\"","They nodded in a dazed manner before quietly following him.","However, one of the members could not contain her curiosity and asked, \"Um... what did you do to that Void Specter just now?\"","\"What does it look like I did?\" Yuan replied with a question of his own.","\"I’m asking because I don’t know! Your movements were too fast just now, and I couldn’t see anything!\" she snapped, clearly irritated at having to admit that she had failed to follow his movements."]},{"number":2626,"title":"Chapter 2626: Elite Void Specter(2)","paragraphs":["\"I apologize in advance if this sounds rude, but it’s not something that you can learn through an explanation, so I’ll save my breath,\" Yuan said a moment later.","\"What?!\" The captain cried out loud, unable to believe her ears.","\"Surely, a brief explanation wouldn’t hurt,\" Captain Chen urged, as he was also interested in Yuan’s powers.","After all, since he was going to die, they might as well learn his secrets before then.","\"It’s a family secret,\" Yuan calmly replied.","Then, without waiting for them, immediately started heading deeper into the cave.","’This little bastard! I want to strangle him to death right now!’","’That would definitely make things a lot easier.’","’Calm down. You know he has to die an ’accidental’ death.’","The Scorpion Squad spoke to each other using voice transmission as they continued to follow Yuan.","’I know that, but can’t we make it look like an accident? Instead of waiting for him to make a mistake, one of us could \"accidentally\" bump into him during a fight,’ Captain Dung suggested.","’The system isn’t stupid. It can sense your killing intent, even if you try to disguise it as an accident,’ Captain Chen replied.","’If it can detect our killing intent that easily, then wouldn’t it still hold us responsible if he dies later, even if we never lay a hand on him?’","’Right? We’re technically luring him to his death right now.’","’The system isn’t that powerful.’","’What if we tie him up and move as far away as possible?’","Captain Chen sighed, ’Do you really think nobody has tried that before? If it was so simple, we wouldn’t be doing this right now!’","Soon, Yuan reached another fork in the tunnel, but this time, three separate paths stretched out before him.","However, rather than choosing one at random, Yuan extended his senses as far as possible, searching for whichever path carried the strongest aura.","Instead of avoiding danger, he deliberately sought out the most dangerous route. Not only would stronger Void Specters benefit his cultivation, but he also wanted to give the Scorpion Squad a taste of their own medicine.","Although the Scorpion Squad had done an excellent job concealing their killing intent, they slipped up during Yuan’s battle with the Elite Void Specter and allowed a trace of it to leak out.","Naturally, Yuan did not fail to notice it.","Moreover, even though Yuan was almost certain that they had been sent by General Gu to kill him, there remained a minuscule possibility that this wasn’t the case... until just now, that was.","’A-Another Elite Void Specter?! He’s encountered two Elite Void Specters in a row!’","The Scorpion Squad was baffled by Yuan’s misfortune.","But since they’ve already witnessed Yuan defeat one in the blink of an eye, they didn’t have any hope that he would fall to this one.","Sure enough, Yuan ended the fight in the blink of an eye, using the same technique he’d used before.","’Just what sort of technique is that?’ asked one of the captains, as they grasped a slight glimpse of it this time.","’I don’t know, but he’s condensed his Limitless on his hand...’","The soldiers secretly tried to replicate Yuan’s technique, and while they managed to condense their Limitless and even form a shape with it, it was nowhere near as refined or compressed as his. The difference was like comparing a solid steel blade to one made of jello.","Yuan noticed what they were doing and smiled inwardly, ’Not bad. If only they could use Supreme Sword Aura.’","Indeed, he had imbued his Supreme Sword Aura with Limitless, strengthening it multiple times over.","He also used the same technique to defeat the Void Guardians. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have been able to defeat them in time before the other soldiers caught up with him.","Some time later, Yuan cleared several more paths. Unfortunately, not every path had an Elite Void Specter, and besides the first two, he only encountered ordinary Void Specters. Though even the ordinary ones were more powerful than the ones outside the tunnel.","\"What do you think?\" Yuan suddenly turned around to face the Scorpion Squad.","\"What do you mean?\"","\"Are you satisfied with my capabilities so far?\"","\"Y-yes...\" Captain Chen nodded with a stiff smile.","\"Is that so? Well, I am just getting started, so try not to be too surprised later.\"","A day later, a cold smile crept across Yuan’s face when he sensed an impressive aura emanating from one of the paths. Since he was walking ahead of the Scorpion Squad, none of them noticed his expression.","Not long after choosing that route, Yuan encountered not one... not two... or three... but four Elite Void Specters!","\"T-This is—!\" The Scorpion Squad visibly flinched when they saw this.","\"Four of them, huh? As confident as I am in my abilities, I don’t think I can handle more than two at once, so I’ll leave the other two to you guys,\" Yuan said.","Captain Chen’s eyes widened at Yuan’s words, and he hastily said, \"You’re still thinking of fighting in this situation?! That’s insane! No! We will go back and take another path!\"","Even though this was the perfect opportunity to get rid of Yuan, there was no way they could deal with the aftermath. After all, once the Elite Void Specters killed Yuan, they would inevitably turn their attention to the Scorpion Squad next.","However, Yuan then said, \"Surely, you’re saying that just to mess with me. They’re not that difficult to fight, so there’s no way the five of you cannot handle two of them. Don’t worry, I’ll help out as soon as I defeat my targets.\"","\"Yo—\"","Captain Chen opened his mouth, but before he could even utter a complete word, Yuan rushed into the detection range of the Elite Void Specters, immediately drawing their attention.","\"This fucking suicidal maniac is going to drag us down with him!\" Captain Dung cursed out loud, his face flushed with anger as they immediately prepared for battle."]},{"number":2627,"title":"Chapter 2627: Elite Void Specter(3)","paragraphs":["Once the Elite Void Specters noticed their presence, one of them charged at Yuan while the other three made their way towards the Scorpion Squad behind him.","Even though Yuan said he’d take care of two of them, he completely ignored it and focused on the Elite Void Specter before him.","Of course, if he wanted to, Yuan could easily defeat the Elite Void Specter in a split second, but he purposefully took his time with it.","Meanwhile, the Scorpion Squad began to panic as they found themselves facing three Elite Void Specters at once.","With only five members, they were forced to split into three groups, with Captain Chen taking on one of the Elite Void Specters by himself while the remaining four paired up against the other two.","Although Captain Chen was the strongest member of the squad, even he knew that defeating an Elite Void Specter alone was beyond him. His only option was to stall for time until the others could come to his aid.","With all of his attention focused on surviving, he had no room to spare for Yuan, who was essentially pretending to struggle against his own Elite Void Specter.","A full minute later, Yuan defeated his Elite Void Specter and went to assist Captain Chen.","\"What took you so long?!\" Captain Chen shouted at Yuan, his forehead bulging with veins.","\"That Void Specter was much stronger than the previous ones I fought,\" Yuan calmly responded before defeating the one before him in less than a second, which only enraged Captain Chen even more when he saw this.","But before Captain Chen could even say anything, Yuan left to assist the others.","In the end, nobody died, but the Scorpion Squad definitely received a scare.","Once all of the Elite Void Specters were defeated, the Scorpion Squad surrounded Yuan and screamed at him.","\"WHAT THE HELL WAS THAT?! WERE YOU TRYING TO GET ALL OF US KILLED?!\" Captain Dung roared, the veins in his neck bulging with rage.","\"I told you we should’ve taken another path! Why did you ignore my order and rush in?! That could’ve ended badly for all of us!\"","Despite their anger, Yuan remained remarkably calm.","After a moment, he looked at them with genuine confusion and asked, \"I don’t understand. Why are you so upset? Sure, those Void Specters were stronger than expected, but why did you struggle so much against them? I thought all of you were strong enough to handle them yourselves.\"","\"That wasn’t any ordinary Void Specter, but an Elite Void Specter! They’re not something one can defeat alone!\"","\"Elite Void Specter? This is new information for me,\" Yuan said before questioning, \"If they were so dangerous, why’d you let me fight them alone?\"","\"They may be dangerous, but they’re still weaker than a Void Guardian. Since you’ve claimed that you can defeat a Void Guardian by yourself, we weren’t worried about you losing to a single Elite Void Specter. Even if you couldn’t defeat it, the rest of us could handle one together. What we can’t handle is several of them at once. What you did was incredibly reckless and foolish!\"","\"Is that so? I’ll keep that in mind,\" Yuan said with a nod. \"But you can’t expect me to know something if you never explain it beforehand. Also, if there’s something you can’t handle, you should tell me in advance. That way, I won’t recklessly put myself in another situation where you won’t be able to protect me if things go wrong.\"","Although Captain Chen wanted to punish Yuan for his actions, he had no real justification for doing so. After all, they had deliberately withheld information about the Elite Void Specters from him, giving Yuan the perfect excuse to claim that he simply hadn’t known any better.","\"Anyway, let’s continue.\" Yuan turned around and started venturing deeper into the tunnel.","’That bastard must’ve done that on purpose!’ Captain Dung suspected.","’Unless he knows our true objective, he has no reason to do such a thing,’ said Captain Chen.","’What if he knows?’ another officer asked.","’Even if he knows, there’s nothing he can really do about it. Not only does he lack proof, but it’s not like he can kill us, either.’","’The real question is... how the hell are we supposed to kill him and make it look like an accident now? He can defeat four Elite Void Specters by himself...’ someone asked.","’Damn it... I don’t understand how he’s doing it! How the hell is he defeating these Void Specters so easily when his cultivation is far lower than ours?! It makes no sense!’","’Right?! I’ve been watching him closely this entire time, and the amount of Limitless he uses isn’t anything extraordinary! He must possess some kind of technique that allows him to draw out the hidden power of Limitless, just like Tian Yuchen!’","’If that’s the case, we must acquire that technique before we kill him!’","’And how do you intend to do that when we’re not even sure we can kill him without touching him?!’","The Scorpion Squad argued with each other while Yuan continued to clear the tunnel alone.","Eventually, they arrived at the end of the tunnel.","\"What are you waiting for?\" Captain Dung asked when Yuan stood at the edge of the hole without moving for a long time.","\"Don’t tell me you’re getting cold feet because you can’t actually defeat a Void Guardian by yourself?\" Another member said in a somewhat mocking tone.","Yuan, who had been staring at the hole, turned around and spoke with a calm smile, \"As if.\"","Then, without another word, jumped into the hole.","Seeing this, the members of Scorpion Squad gave each other a quick glance before following Yuan down the hole.","A few minutes later, they arrived at the chamber with the Void Guardian.","However, their eyes widened with shock the very next moment.","\"T-Two... There are two Void Guardians?!\"","Captain Chen exclaimed in shock when he saw two massive silhouettes standing beside each other."]},{"number":2628,"title":"Chapter 2628: Double Void Guardians","paragraphs":["\"Why are there two Void Guardians here?! That shouldn’t be possible in the Purple Zone!\" Captain Chen cried out loud.","\"Who cares about that?! We need to get out of here before they attack!\" Captain Dung shouted as he immediately flew back up the hole.","The others did not hesitate and quickly followed after him, abandoning the chamber without a second thought.","Captain Chen gritted his teeth and prepared to retreat as well. Before leaving, however, he glanced back at Yuan, who was still falling and showed no intention of turning back.","’What a fool. It’s a shame we won’t be able to uncover his secrets before he dies, but at least our mission is finally complete,’ Captain Chen mocked inwardly before leaving the chamber.","Meanwhile, Yuan merely shook his head inwardly at the Scorpion Squad. He didn’t even bother looking back at them, keeping his attention fixed on the two Void Guardians before him instead.","An excited smile slowly appeared on Yuan’s face. In his eyes, two Void Guardians only meant double the reward!","Shortly after the Scorpion Squad began making their way back up the tunnel, an immensely powerful and unfathomable aura suddenly erupted from the chamber below, catching their attention.","\"W-What the hell is that energy?!\" Captain Dung exclaimed in shock.","\"Did that guy really stay behind to fight two Void Guardians at once?! Suicidal!\"","\"That works in our favor, anyway. There’s no way he’s getting out of this one alive.\"","Captain Chen said nothing and merely glanced back down the tunnel, an ominous feeling stirring in the pit of his stomach.","’Will that really be enough to kill him?’ he wondered inwardly.","The energy surging from the chamber continued to rise, eventually reaching a level that felt almost surreal.","Not only were the Void Guardians in the Purple Zone vastly stronger than those in the Red Zone, but there were also two of them. Even for someone like Yuan, this was not a situation he could resolve in the blink of an eye.","That being said, Yuan wasn’t exactly struggling, either. Although the Void Guardians were stronger, that merely meant they were faster and far more aggressive. With Yuan’s mastery of Void Manipulation, however, neither posed any real threat to him.","In other words, defeating them simply required a little more time than usual.","A few minutes later, just as the Scorpion Squad reached the top of the hole and returned to the tunnel, the energy suddenly stopped.","\"Hm? Did he finally die? That took longer than I expected.\"","\"Should we go back down and check?\"","\"And risk our lives? Don’t be stupid. There’s no way he could defeat two Void Guardians by himself. He’s definitely dead.\"","\"Chen? What are you thinking about, staring down that hole so intensely?\" Captain Dung suddenly asked after noticing his unusual behavior.","After another moment of silence, Captain Chen finally spoke.","\"Call me crazy, but I don’t think he’s dead.\"","\"Huh? That’s definitely crazy, all right. Did you hit your head on the way out or something?\" One of the members mocked him openly.","\"I’m going to take a look. You can stay here if you want.\"","Before the others could respond, Captain Chen jumped back down the hole.","\"C-Chen?!\"","Captain Chen could hear Captain Dung’s shocked voice echoing from above but ignored it and continued falling.","A few minutes later, Captain Chen returned to the chamber.","\"I-Impossible...\" he muttered in a daze when he realized that the two Void Guardians were nowhere to be seen.","His gaze instinctively shifted toward the center of the chamber, where Yuan sat quietly absorbing the Eternal Essence they had left behind.","If a Void Guardian from the Red Zone contained roughly a billion years’ worth of Eternal Essence, then each one in the Purple Zone possessed more than ten billion years’ worth.","Since Yuan had defeated two of them, he had gained over twenty billion years’ worth of Eternal Essence in a single battle.","Captain Chen silently stared at Yuan from a distance for a full minute before calling out to him.","\"C-Corporal Yuan...?\"","However, there was no response from Yuan.","\"Corporal Yuan!\" he called out again, this time in a much louder voice.","\"I heard you the first time,\" Yuan responded without moving.","\"What are you doing? What happened to the Void Guardians?\" Captain Chen asked.","\"I’m a little busy right now, so let’s talk later.\"","\"...\"","A few minutes later, Captain Chen turned around after sensing Captain Dung and the others entering the chamber behind him.","Sure enough, every single one of them wore a bewildered expression, as though they were struggling to comprehend the scene before them.","\"W-What is going on here...? Where are the Void Guardians?\" Captain Dung asked in a dazed voice.","\"He’s actually still alive...\" another member mumbled as she stared at Yuan, who was still cultivating in silence.","\"What is he doing?\" a third member asked.","\"I don’t know, but he’s been in that position since I arrived.\"","\"Is he sleeping?\"","\"Hey, wake up!\" Captain Dung suddenly yelled at Yuan.","When Yuan ignored him, Captain Dung began walking toward him with a deep frown.","Just as he reached Yuan and extended a hand toward his shoulder, Yuan suddenly turned and fixed him with a calm yet piercing gaze.","\"You’re still here? I thought you would’ve run all the way back to the tunnel entrance by now.\"","\"W-What did you just say...?\" Captain Dung muttered, his eyebrows twitching with anger. \"I dare you to say that again!\"","\"Why are you getting so angry? It’s true that you ran away the moment you saw two Void Guardians. Or are you going to deny it and call me a liar?\" Yuan said, shaking his head.","He then stood up to face Captain Dung and the others.","\"Why did you come back? To collect the Unknown Crystals or... to confirm my death?\"","\"?!\"","The members of the Scorpion Squad widened their eyes in shock at Yuan’s words.","\"W-What are you talking about, Corporal Yuan?\" Captain Chen spoke a moment later, trying his best to sound confused. \"There must be some kind of misunderstanding.\"","Yuan looked at him and sneered, \"You can drop the act. I know that you brought me out here with the intention of killing me.\""]},{"number":2629,"title":"Chapter 2629: Dropping the Act","paragraphs":["\"W-We brought you out here to kill you? That’s a serious accusation, Corporal Yuan!\" Captain Chen exclaimed, continuing to insist that it was nothing more than a misunderstanding. \"What reason could we possibly have to want you dead?! We only wanted to verify the rumors!\"","\"You may have no reason to kill me, but your boss, General Gu, definitely does,\" Yuan said with a smile. \"However, if you truly have no intention of killing me, then you’d have no problem with us returning to the city now, right?\"","\"...\"","Captain Chen fell silent for a moment before releasing a deep sigh.","\"Unfortunately, we cannot do that,\" he said with a serious expression, finally deciding to drop the act.","The members of the Scorpion Squad suddenly moved, surrounding Yuan from all sides.","\"Are you going to kill me now?\" Yuan asked calmly, even though he already knew they wouldn’t dare dirty their own hands. After all, if they could kill him directly without consequence, they would’ve done so long ago.","However, Captain Chen and the others remained silent.","’What should we do now that we’ve been exposed?’ one of the members asked through voice transmission.","’Do we just... kill him now?’","Although killing Yuan themselves seemed to be their only remaining option, none of them wanted to be the one to actually dirty their hands.","\"I will do it. I will kill this bastard with my own hands!\" Captain Dung suddenly said out loud.","\"I have a suggestion.\"","Captain Dung froze at Yuan’s words.","\"A suggestion, you say? Unless you’re offering to kill yourself, I don’t want to hear it,\" Captain Dung sneered with a look of disdain on his face.","Yuan smiled and said, \"That’s exactly what I was going to suggest.\"","\"Excuse me?\" Captain Chen raised his eyebrows in puzzlement.","\"Although I don’t know why you’re so hesitant to kill me yourselves, it wouldn’t matter even if you tried. After all, none of you are capable of killing me,\" Yuan said with a confident smile.","\"What did you just say?\" Captain Dung frowned.","\"We’ll give you credit for being able to defeat Elite Void Specters and Void Guardians on your own, but fighting other humans is an entirely different matter,\" one of the members said.","Yuan chuckled and said, \"In that case, let’s put that to the test.\"","Before any of them could even react to Yuan’s words, he suddenly used Void Manipulation, vanishing from his spot and appearing right behind Captain Chen.","\"Catch me if you can,\" Yuan said.","\"G-Get him! Don’t let him escape!\" Captain Chen hastily shouted as he lunged toward Yuan.","\"Don’t worry. I have no intention of leaving this tunnel,\" Yuan said as he teleported a few meters away.","The next moment, the members of the Scorpion Squad found themselves playing an absurd game of tag with him, and despite having five people, none of them could so much as touch his shadow.","\"Hahaha! Is this really the level of captains?! I was expecting much more!\"","\"Slow! Too slow!\"","\"Are you sure you even qualify to enter the Purple Zone? Your Void Control barely qualifies for the Red Zone!\"","Yuan continued taunting them relentlessly as they desperately tried—and repeatedly failed—to catch him.","One hour... two hours... five hours passed—","\"Enough! We get your point!\" Captain Chen finally came to a halt and shouted, his voice trembling with frustration.","The other members of Scorpion Squad also stopped trying to catch Yuan and started taking deep breaths from exhaustion.","Yuan then said, \"As I was saying... since none of you are capable of killing me, you might as well return to the city and give up trying to kill me.\"","\"Do you really think that’s an option for us?\" Captain Chen responded with a frown.","\"Well, what other options do you have? If I wanted to return to the city, there’s nothing any of you here could do about it. And if I wanted to kill you... it’d be easier than dealing with Void Specters.\"","\"Then—\"","\"With that being said...\" Yuan interrupted Captain Chen before he could respond. \"I don’t actually want to return to the city. At least not yet.\"","\"What the hell are you talking about?\"","A profound smile tugged at Yuan’s lips as he explained, \"I’ve been wanting to explore the Purple Zone alone—and even the Black Zone—for quite some time now. Unfortunately, with my low rank and status as a new soldier, that isn’t possible.\"","His smile deepened.","\"But thanks to you lot, I now have the perfect excuse to venture as far as I want, and I have no intention of wasting such a valuable opportunity.\"","Yuan approached Captain Chen and continued, \"Therefore, here is my real suggestion. Go back to the city and tell General Gu that you have succeeded in your mission and that I am dead.\"","\"You... are you crazy...?\" Captain Chen muttered with a dumbfounded expression.","\"You want us to lie to General Gu?! And what do you think will happen to us when you return alive?!\" one of the members exclaimed.","Yuan shrugged and nonchalantly replied, \"I fail to see how that is my problem. In fact, I couldn’t care less.\"","\"You—!\"","\"What other choice do you have?\" Yuan interrupted them again. \"You can either return without me and hope I somehow die on my own, or we can go back together, where you’ll have to explain to General Gu why you failed your mission—and answer to General Mei for trying to kill me.\"","\"!!!\"","The members of the Scorpion Squad swallowed nervously at Yuan’s words and fell silent as they weighed their options.","If they returned to the city with Yuan still alive, they would undoubtedly have to face the wrath of both General Gu and General Mei. However, if they followed Yuan’s suggestion and returned without him, they would at least retain a slim chance of survival.","Though it wasn’t as if they really had a choice in the first place, as they were incapable of killing Yuan.","\"Are you... really going to go deeper into the Purple Zone and even enter the Black Zone?\" Captain Chen asked out of curiosity.","\"That’s right.\" Yuan nodded with a genuine-looking expression on his face.","\"Why?\"","\"That’s none of your business.\"","\"...\"","Captain Chen closed his eyes and took a deep breath before turning to look at the other members.","\"We’re returning to the city,\" he announced in a defeated tone.","\"...\"","None of the members said anything and silently nodded.","Shortly afterward, the Scorpion Squad left the tunnel, leaving Yuan behind, who went on to absorb the Eternal Essence from the hundreds of Unknown Crystals still glistening along the walls.","\"Are we really going to return to the city and lie to General Gu? What if that bastard was lying and plans to return immediately as well?\" Captain Dung asked as they made their way back toward the surface.","\"Of course not,\" Captain Chen said. \"I want to confirm with my own eyes that he truly intends to venture deeper into the Purple Zone, and regardless of his actions, we’re going to ambush him.\"","\"How are we supposed to do that when we can’t even catch him?\"","\"That’s why I said we’ll ambush him! We don’t stand a chance in a direct confrontation, so our only option is to catch him off guard.\"","After leaving the tunnel, the Scorpion Squad hid their presence and waited for Yuan to come out.","Some time later, Yuan emerged from the tunnel.","However, instead of leaving immediately, he remained by the entrance and glanced from side to side, as though searching for someone nearby.","After looking around for a minute, Yuan started venturing in the direction that led him deeper into the Purple Zone.","’He’s really going deeper into the Purple Zone!’","’Should we keep following him?’ Captain Dung asked.","’Of course. For all we know, he could simply be putting on an act because he suspects we’re still watching him,’ Captain Chen replied.","Thus, the Scorpion Squad began secretly following Yuan, completely unaware that he had sensed their presence long before he even emerged from the tunnel.","Despite knowing they were there, Yuan had no intention of confronting them. In his eyes, the Scorpion Squad wasn’t worth his time or effort. Moreover, if they insisted on following him deeper into the Purple Zone, they would only be putting their own lives at risk.","’Now that I am alone...’","A wide grin slowly spread across Yuan’s face as his aura began to rise.","’What is he doing...?’","The members of the Scorpion Squad watched with puzzled expressions, unable to understand what Yuan was planning.","The next moment, his aura erupted violently. Limitless surged outward in every direction like a colossal tidal wave, sweeping across the barren landscape and instantly annihilating every Void Specter caught in its path.","\"?!?!?!\"","Captain Chen and the others stared with their mouths agape, their eyes filled with utter disbelief at what they had just witnessed.","However, Yuan wasn’t finished.","After clearing the area of Void Specters, he made a simple gesture with two fingers, pointing them toward the heavens. The next moment, hundreds of Unknown Ores shot into the air and gathered before him, as though invisible ghosts were collecting them on his behalf.","After gathering all of the Unknown Ores, including the ones inside the ground, Yuan took a moment to absorb all of their Eternal Essence before moving deeper into the Purple Zone, leaving the Unknown Ores behind.","’W-What was that just now?!’ Captain Chen exclaimed inwardly, having trouble comprehending what he’d just witnessed.","Unfortunately, they had no time to stand around and process what they had witnessed, as Yuan was already leaving them behind.","With no other choice, the Scorpion Squad hurried after him. Yet as they continued following Yuan, he repeated the same astonishing feat again and again—slaughtering countless Void Specters and gathering thousands of Unknown Ores in ways none of them had ever seen before."]},{"number":2630,"title":"Chapter 2630: Black Zone","paragraphs":["A hundred million years... a billion years... ten billion years... a hundred billion years...","Yuan’s Eternal Essence soared as he wreaked havoc across the Purple Zone, annihilating every Void Specter in his path while absorbing the energy contained within the thousands of Unknown Ores scattered throughout the land.","However, such rapid growth did not occur over the span of merely a few days. Even at Yuan’s pace, it still required several weeks of relentless effort.","Of course, the Scorpion Squad followed him the entire time.","’This guy... he’s not human!’ Captain Chen clenched his fists tightly, desperately trying to suppress the trembling in his body.","’Chen... It’s obvious now that he truly intends to enter the Black Zone,’ one of the members remarked. ’Maybe we should... head back to the base?’","’I agree with Mung. At this point, I don’t see any reason to keep following him. Hell, I don’t even think we’ll be able to ambush him!’","Captain Chen pondered for a moment before responding, ’We’ll keep following him until he enters the Black Zone.’","The others exchanged concerned looks.","’I know what all of you are thinking—and I feel the same way. I’m afraid of him too... but at the same time, I can’t help feeling curious. I want to see what other secrets he’s still hiding.’","Captain Chen turned to look at them and continued, ’It won’t be too long before we reach the Black Zone. Moreover, it’s clear that he isn’t aware of our presence.’","A few days later, Yuan slowed down when he noticed that the purple mist had darkened so much that it had turned black.","’Am I in the Black Zone?’ he wondered.","He examined the black mist a moment later.","’Oh?’","Although it was not by much, his Chaotic Essence had improved slightly after absorbing the mist!","Meanwhile, Captain Chen and the others finally stopped following Yuan.","’He’s really entering the Black Zone.’","’I’ve been watching him for the last several weeks, but I still cannot fathom his actions.’","’There’s no point thinking about it. Let’s go back and report his death.’","Thus, the Scorpion Squad turned around and began their journey back to the city.","As they traveled, they couldn’t help but feel that, all things considered, the situation had turned out far better than they had anticipated, especially after they’d been exposed. After all, Yuan could’ve returned to the city after learning of their schemes, but for some reason, he decided to enter the Black Zone on his own.","The Scorpion Squad had expected a smooth journey back to the city. However, a week later, while they were still traveling through the Purple Zone, they encountered something completely unexpected—or rather, someone.","’I-Isn’t that the Ironwoman?! To think we’d encounter her out here! How unlucky!’ Captain Chen cried inwardly after seeing her.","’Chen! What should we do?! Should we just ignore her?’ one of the members asked anxiously.","’No. Greet her normally, then leave as quickly as possible.’","The Scorpion Squad approached the Ironwoman and her squad, who had already come to a stop after noticing their presence and were now watching them closely.","Once they were close enough, Captain Chen and the others greeted them.","\"We greet the Ironwoman and the Stellar Squad!\"","The Ironwoman nodded in acknowledgment before asking, \"Are you returning from a mission?\"","\"Y-Yes, we are,\" Captain Chen replied, unable to hide his surprise at the question. The Ironwoman was well known for minding her own business, so he hadn’t expected her to show any interest in them.","The Ironwoman fell silent.","\"Then, if you’ll excuse us—\"","Just as Captain Chen and the others prepared to leave, the Ironwoman spoke again, \"Where do you think you’re going?\"","Captain Chen’s movements instantly froze at the sound of her cold tone.","\"Excuse me?\" he turned to look at her.","\"Is this all of you?\" she then asked.","\"Yes.\" Captain Chen nodded.","Despite his seemingly calm demeanor, Captain Chen’s back was already drenched in cold sweat. The Ironwoman hadn’t said much, but she had said enough for him to realize that her appearance—and their encounter—was no mere coincidence.","\"That’s funny.\"","\"Why would it be funny?\" Captain Chen frowned.","\"You see... before coming out here, I heard that your squad had secretly brought a new soldier out on a mission.\"","The Ironwoman scanned the members with a cold gaze before continuing, \"So, where is this soldier? Surely, you didn’t leave a mere corporal who’d just joined the military behind in the Purple Zone.\"","Captain Chen subconsciously clenched his fists.","’Fuck! To think they’d send the Ironwoman to search for Corporal Yuan!’ he cried inwardly, realizing that he’d underestimated how important Yuan was to General Mei.","However, Captain Chen quickly replied, \"There must be some kind of misunderstanding. We didn’t bring anyone who wasn’t supposed to be out here with us.\"","\"That’s right!\" Captain Dung added. \"What you heard was nothing more than a baseless rumor. Unless you personally saw us bringing this corporal out here, you shouldn’t be making such accusations!\"","The Ironwoman merely shrugged. \"The gate guards have already admitted what happened, and they’re willing to testify that they saw you use the teleporter with Corporal Yuan.\"","Captain Chen narrowed his eyes. \"For argument’s sake, even if we did bring Corporal Yuan out here, it wouldn’t be against the rules. As officers, we have every right and authority to take soldiers with us on missions.\"","\"You’re right. It isn’t against the rules,\" the Ironwoman replied. \"However, his safety would then be your responsibility. If he dies under your supervision, you’ll have to answer for your negligence and failure to protect him. And, of course, we’d also have to investigate whether his death was truly accidental.\"","\"Anyway, Scorpion Squad, you’re under arrest on suspicion of conspiring against a fellow soldier. Are you going to surrender peacefully, or do you want to make this difficult?\"","Captain Chen glanced at the others before slowly raising his hands in surrender. The rest of the Scorpion Squad followed suit without resistance.","Even if they chose to fight, they stood no chance against the Stellar Squad—much less the Ironwoman, who was more than capable of defeating all of them by herself.","\"Arrest them.\" The Ironwoman commanded, and her squad swiftly restricted their movements and cultivation with a golden chain.","\"Take them back to the city. I’ll stay out here for a little longer,\" said the Ironwoman.","\"Yes, squad leader.\"","Her squadmates had complete faith in her abilities and did not question her decision to remain behind and venture through the Purple Zone alone.","Once the Stellar Squad departed with the Scorpion Squad in custody, the Ironwoman turned toward the direction they had come from and flew off.","’The chances of Corporal Yuan still being alive are slim...’ The Ironwoman had realized this the moment she saw that he wasn’t with the Scorpion Squad.","Even so, an inexplicable feeling in her gut urged her to keep searching.","A few days later, the Ironwoman arrived at the border between the Purple Zone and the Black Zone.","\"...\"","She hovered silently in the air, a thoughtful expression on her face.","Throughout the past few days of travel, she had noticed a disturbing lack of Void Specters. No, it would be more accurate to say that they were completely absent.","’I’ve never seen the Purple Zone this quiet before... Just what the hell happened here?’","However, that wasn’t even the strangest part.","The Ironwoman lowered her gaze toward the ground, where thousands of Unknown Ores lay scattered openly across the barren landscape.","It was such a bizarre sight that she could only imagine seeing something like it in a dream.","The Ironwoman scratched her head, utterly bewildered by the situation before her.","Eventually, she decided to stop dwelling on it and entered the Black Zone, where the trail of Unknown Ores continued into the distance like bait deliberately laid out to lure unsuspecting prey.","Unsurprisingly, the Black Zone was no different. Not a single Void Specter could be sensed anywhere, as though some unknown force had swept through the region and completely eradicated them.","One day... three days... five days...","Time passed quickly, and after nearly an entire week of following the trail of Unknown Ores, the Ironwoman suddenly came to a halt when she sensed an immensely powerful presence in the distance.","The moment she detected it, she immediately increased her speed and rushed toward its source, which also happened to be where the trail ended.","\"T-That’s...\"","Her eyes widened beneath her mask, filled with shock and disbelief as she stared at the lone figure standing at the end of the trail.","\"C-Corporal Yuan?!\" she cried out in disbelief.","Hearing her voice, Yuan turned around to face her.","\"You are...\" He quickly recognized her.","\"What are you doing out here alone?! And what the hell is up with the Unknown Ores on the ground?!\" the Ironwoman asked as she slowly approached him, unable to suppress the faint wariness she felt toward his presence.","\"I...\"","Yuan hesitated, unsure how to respond."]},{"number":2631,"title":"Chapter 2631: Black Zone(2)","paragraphs":["’I wasn’t expecting anyone to find me so soon...’ Yuan sighed inwardly.","He had finally been given the freedom to roam outside the city alone and train to his heart’s content, and while he’d already gained a lot, he was nowhere near satisfied. Returning now would feel like wasting such a rare opportunity.","\"Corporal Yuan? Why are you remaining silent?\" The Ironwoman asked a moment later.","\"Ahem.\" Yuan cleared his throat and responded, \"I’m training right now.\"","\"Excuse me?\"","Ironwoman raised her eyebrows behind her mask, wearing a puzzled look on her face.","\"You’re... training?\" she muttered in a dumbfounded tone.","\"What about the Scorpion Squad? Weren’t you kidnapped by them? At least, that’s what half the military believes right now!\"","Yuan chuckled and said, \"I wouldn’t call it kidnapping since I willingly agreed to come out here with them.\"","\"So what you’re telling me is that the Scorpion Squad is innocent?\"","\"Well, that depends on what you’re charging them with. If it’s kidnapping, then yes, that would be inaccurate. But if you’re charging them with conspiracy to commit murder, then you’d have a case.\"","\"If they were really trying to kill you, why did they leave without you? We encountered them on the way here and have arrested them, you know?\" said the Ironwoman.","\"Whether they are capable of killing me or not is an entirely different story,\" Yuan responded with a calm smile. \"They tried to kill me, but they lack the capability, so they gave up.\"","The Ironwoman released a weak sigh before asking, \"What about the Unknown Ores on the ground? Where did they come from?\"","Yuan looked at the Unknown Ores scattered across the ground and replied with a poker face, \"I don’t know.\"","He couldn’t come up with a convincing excuse, so he decided it would be better to simply feign ignorance.","\"...\"","The Ironwoman stared at Yuan in silence. Although she could tell that he was withholding information from her, she ultimately decided not to press him for answers. After all, the most important thing was that he was still alive. Moreover, it was not her mission to question him.","\"Let’s return to the city now. You can explain everything to General Mei,\" she said a moment later.","However, just as she turned around and prepared to leave, Yuan spoke, \"Sorry, but I don’t want to return to the city.\"","\"What did you just say?\"","The Ironwoman’s movements froze for a second before she turned to look at him with a puzzled expression.","Yuan sighed and explained, \"If I wanted to return to the city, I would’ve done so already. But as I mentioned earlier, I am training. Do you have any idea how hard it is for a new soldier like me to come out alone? Now that I have the opportunity to do so, I don’t want to return until I am finished.\"","\"Do you have any idea how many people are waiting for your return? Many of them probably already think you’re dead.\"","\"That’s even better,\" Yuan chuckled. \"If they already think that I am dead, I might as well stay out here for a little longer. As for General Mei, you can tell her that I am still alive and doing well—that I will return as soon as I finish my training. I’m sure she’ll understand.\"","After another moment of silence, the Ironwoman shrugged. \"My mission was to find you, and since I’ve done exactly that, I’ve technically completed it. Whether you return with me or stay out here is none of my concern.\"","She paused briefly before continuing, \"That being said, I want to at least make sure you can take care of yourself in the Black Zone before I head back and get an earful from General Mei for leaving you out here alone.\"","\"Thanks,\" said Yuan.","Knowing the Ironwoman’s identity, Yuan already had a feeling that she wouldn’t force him to go back to the city, so he wasn’t too surprised by it.","Some time later, Yuan resumed his training, eliminating every Void Specter he encountered. However, now that he was no longer alone, he stopped gathering Unknown Ores.","He hadn’t minded letting the Scorpion Squad witness his unusual methods, since there was a good chance no one would believe anything they said anyway. The Ironwoman, however, was a different story. Even though Yuan trusted her, explaining everything would be far more trouble than it was worth.","’This guy... he’s defeating the Void Specters with ease!’ The Ironwoman quickly found herself stunned by Yuan’s unfathomable prowess.","The Void Specters within the Black Zone were on an entirely different level from those in the Purple Zone. Not only did they possess humanoid forms similar to Elite Void Specters, but their strength was comparable as well.","’I knew he was hiding his strength, but I could’ve never imagined it was to such a degree! A corporal dominating the Black Zone that even top officers are not able to do so? It’s no wonder that General Mei cares so much about him!’","The more the Ironwoman watched Yuan, the less she understood him—his very existence.","\"Where’d you learn to fight like that?\"","The Ironwoman could no longer hold her tongue and asked Yuan.","\"Would you believe me if I said that I learned it from another world?\" Yuan responded with a smile.","\"Another world, huh? Is that a metaphor for another city, or are you telling me that you came from beyond this sky—from another star?\"","\"What do you think?\"","\"I think you’re pulling my leg,\" she said.","Then, she asked, \"Anyway, I noticed that you’ve stopped digging up Unknown Ores. You don’t have to mind me and just keep doing what you’ve been doing, you know?\"","\"Are you going to question me about it?\"","\"Well, I am questioning you now precisely because you stopped. If you’re worried about revealing your secrets, I promise I won’t tell anyone.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan started gathering Unknown Ores and absorbing their Eternal Essence again.","The Ironwoman quietly picked up a few of the Unknown Ores Yuan had left behind and examined them closely, but she couldn’t find anything unusual about them.","This only left her more puzzled. From her perspective, Yuan was simply pulling the ores out from underground before tossing them aside like worthless trash—an utterly pointless action.","’Is he looking for a specific Unknown Ore or something?’ she wondered inwardly."]},{"number":2632,"title":"Chapter 2632: Black Zone(3)","paragraphs":["\"Are you looking for something specific?\" asked the Ironwoman.","\"I thought you weren’t going to question me,\" Yuan said with a smile.","\"Did I say that? I only remember saying that I won’t tell anyone about your secrets,\" she replied with a smile of her own, but it was concealed by her mask.","\"Is that so? Well, I’m not really looking for anything.\"","\"Then what’s the purpose behind your actions?\"","Yuan fell silent for a moment before answering, \"I... figured I’d make things easier for the soldiers who come out here on gathering missions. There are far too many for me to carry by myself, so I thought I’d bring them to the surface and make them easier to find.\"","It wasn’t the most convincing explanation, but Yuan had at least managed to come up with an excuse for his strange actions.","\"You don’t have a storage cube?\" the Ironwoman suddenly asked.","\"A storage cube? No.\"","\"They’re issued to every soldier after completing training. Since you skipped training, you should’ve received one already. Have you even visited the supply warehouse since you joined?\"","\"No...\"","\"Why am I not surprised?\" The Ironwoman shook her head before taking out a pebble-sized, cube-shaped object and holding it up for Yuan to see.","\"This is a storage cube,\" she explained before demonstrating how it worked.","The moment she injected Limitless into it, the cube glowed with an azure light and began drawing in all of the Unknown Ores scattered across the ground.","\"It can hold up to ten thousand Unknown Ores,\" she said after gathering all of the Unknown Ores on the ground.","Yuan raised an eyebrow at the sight. \"If there’s such a convenient tool, why didn’t the others use one during our missions? This is my first time seeing it.\"","\"Probably because a storage cube can only be used so many times before it needs to be repaired, which costs money. Using one on an ordinary gathering mission that only yields a few hundred ores simply isn’t worth the cost, so most soldiers just carry it.\"","This was Yuan’s first time encountering a storage treasure that could only be used a limited number of times before requiring repairs. He couldn’t help but imagine how inconvenient it would be if spatial rings and storage pouches worked the same way.","\"I’ll help you collect as many Unknown Ores as I can while I’m with you,\" said the Ironwoman.","\"Thanks...\"","Unfortunately, that also meant the ores she collected would eventually be handed over to the military for extraction, preventing Yuan from completely draining all of their Eternal Essence.","Since he was technically the one responsible for uncovering them, it would immediately draw suspicion if every single Unknown Ore he gathered turned out to be completely devoid of energy.","They continued venturing deeper into the Black Zone shortly after.","\"How vast is the Black Zone?\" Yuan asked the Ironwoman a few hours later.","\"If you continue traveling at your current pace, you’d need at least five years to reach the Purple Zone on the other side.\"","\"The Black Zone takes up far more space than I anticipated...\"","\"The Black Zone makes up the majority of this world, after all. There are even levels to Black Zones, and the one we’re currently in is considered the least dangerous—a level 1 Black Zone.\"","\"How many levels are there?\"","\"Four.\"","\"How much more dangerous is level 2 compared to level 1?\"","\"Incomparably more dangerous. Even though the Void Specters in the Green Zone can kill someone with the slightest touch, their movement speed and awareness are practically nonexistent compared to those in the Black Zone,\" the Ironwoman explained.","\"In a level 2 Black Zone, the Void Specters fight like seasoned human experts. Their durability also increases dramatically—to the point where an entire squad of captains may need several hours just to defeat a single one.\"","\"As for level 3... we’re currently incapable of defeating the Void Specters at that level. That being said, it’s not as though they’ve never been defeated before. Throughout history, there have been a handful of individuals powerful enough to accomplish such a feat.\"","\"Who are these individuals?\" Yuan inquired.","\"Have you been to Gaia’s Sanctum?\" she suddenly asked.","\"Of course.\"","\"Then you must have seen the Endless Assault rankings. Everyone who has surpassed the 40th floor was capable of defeating the Void Specters in level 3. As for level 4, only Tian Yuchen—the man who has remained at the top of the rankings for over a thousand years—was powerful enough to defeat the Void Specters there.\"","Yuan swallowed nervously at this information.","’Does this mean that the Void Specters within level 3 are on par with Eternals?!’ he cried inwardly. ’The Eternal Essence they leave behind must be tremendous! I need to train there!’","The Ironwoman narrowed her eyes at Yuan’s expression and said, \"You’re not very good at hiding your intentions, are you? If you’re thinking about going to a level 2 Black Zone—\"","\"No, I am thinking about level 3 and beyond,\" he quickly interrupted, which left her speechless and dumbfounded.","\"Then you must have a death wish, because even I wouldn’t dare to—\"","The Ironwoman abruptly stopped mid-sentence, though not because Yuan had interrupted her again.","\"I can sense other presences nearby,\" she said a moment later.","Of course, Yuan had sensed them as well. In fact, he had been aware of their presence for quite some time. He hadn’t bothered mentioning it since there was nothing unusual about encountering other people in the Black Zone.","A few moments later, the Ironwoman spoke again. \"Be careful. They’re heading straight toward us.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow. \"You sound tense. Is there really a reason to be so wary?\"","\"I wouldn’t be if they were from our city. Unfortunately, they’re not,\" she replied.","\"So they’re from another city? This will be my first time meeting people from outside our city,\" Yuan remarked, a hint of excitement in his voice.","\"Don’t get too excited. Encountering soldiers from another city isn’t always a good thing,\" she warned."]},{"number":2633,"title":"Chapter 2633: Scorpion Squad’s Interrogation","paragraphs":["Some time later, Yuan spotted six silhouettes approaching from the distance.","Once they drew close enough for him to make out their appearances, the first thing that caught his attention was their attire, which differed noticeably from the military uniforms he had grown accustomed to.","The Ironwoman moved to hover beside Yuan before addressing the approaching group in a calm yet cold tone.","\"How can we help you?\"","The group did not respond immediately. Instead, their gazes settled on the insignias worn by Yuan and the Ironwoman, silently examining them.","\"A corporal and a major? Are the two of you lost or something?\" one of them finally asked.","\"No, we’re not lost,\" the Ironwoman replied.","\"I know you’re trying to put on a brave front, but there’s no shame in asking for help, even if we’re from different cities.\"","In their eyes, there was only one reasonable explanation for why two soldiers would be wandering the Black Zone alone—the rest of their squad had perished.","\"But still... sending a mere corporal into the Black Zone? Is Gaia’s Heaven’s military really in such a dire state right now?\" another soldier remarked with a weird look on his face.","\"I won’t repeat myself. We’re not lost, so you can leave us alone.\"","\"Hey, asshole, we’re only trying to help!\" one of the soldiers snapped. \"You should watch your mouth, especially when you’re practically alone out here!\"","\"That sounds like a threat,\" the Ironwoman said calmly.","\"So what if it—\"","\"Shut up!\" another soldier suddenly interrupted, clamping a hand over his companion’s mouth. \"Look closely! A major wearing a mask—that’s the Ironwoman!\"","\"?!?!\"","\"Is it true? You’re the famous Ironwoman of Gaia’s Heaven?\"","\"And what if it’s true?\"","\"T-Then there’s no doubt that you don’t need any help. We apologize if we’d offended you.\"","Without another word, these soldiers turned around and swiftly flew away.","\"What was that about?\" Yuan asked afterward.","\"What do you mean?\"","\"Was that attitude really necessary? They were only trying to help us, weren’t they?\"","\"Perhaps,\" the Ironwoman replied. \"But nothing good ever comes from getting involved with soldiers from another city. It’s better if we simply keep our distance from one another.\"","\"Why is that? Are our cities at war with each other or something? What warrants so much caution?\" Yuan asked with a raised eyebrow.","\"We may not be at war, but we still compete over resources,\" she replied. \"In this world, nothing is more valuable than Unknown Ores and Unknown Crystals, since they serve as the primary source of energy for practically everything.\"","\"Soldiers from the same military are forbidden from harming one another, but that restriction doesn’t apply to soldiers from different cities, which is why altercations between soldiers from different cities are extremely common and borderline expected.\"","\"While it’s entirely possible that they genuinely wanted to help, there’s an even greater chance they were simply trying to confirm whether we were alone before deciding to rob—or even kill—us,\" she added after a brief moment of silence. \"There’s a reason they left the moment they recognized who I was.\"","\"I’ll keep that in mind the next time I have another encounter with soldiers from another city,\" Yuan said.","Some time later, Yuan resumed hunting Void Specters throughout the Black Zone while the Ironwoman quietly observed him and helped him pick up Unknown Ores.","A few weeks later, she finally said, \"I think I’ve seen enough. It’s obvious that you have no trouble surviving out here on your own, so I’ll leave you be and return to the city. General Mei is probably losing her mind by now, especially since you never returned with the Scorpion Squad.\"","\"I thought you’d never leave,\" Yuan joked.","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, the Ironwoman asked, \"How long do you plan on staying out here?\"","\"A few more months, probably.\"","\"Try to return within a year,\" the Ironwoman said before turning around to leave.","However, after moving a few meters, she suddenly stopped. Without looking back, she asked in a puzzled tone, \"I was expecting you to ask about my mask. Aren’t you curious why I wear it? Or what I look like underneath?\"","Yuan smiled. \"Not really.\"","Since he already knew what she looked like beneath the mask, there was no reason for him to ask. Of course, revealing that would only invite questions he’d rather not answer.","\"That feels like a rejection for some reason,\" the Ironwoman remarked in a joking tone.","Just as she was about to leave again, the Ironwoman suddenly turned her head and reached for her mask. Without saying a word, she removed it, revealing her beautiful face with a playful smile to Yuan.","Yuan raised an eyebrow at her actions and asked, \"Are you sure you want to reveal your face to me?\"","\"Since you showed me some of your secrets, I figured that I’d show you one of mine to be fair.\"","The Ironwoman quickly wore her mask again and said, \"Anyway, stay safe out here. If you die, I won’t be able to face General Mei again. Oh, right. As for your Unknown Ores, I’ll store them for you until you return.\"","Yuan silently nodded.","Once the Ironwoman left, Yuan returned to his training.","Meanwhile, back at the military base, the Scorpion Squad was taken in for interrogation the moment they returned to the city.","To ensure the interrogation was conducted fairly, General Mei wasn’t the only high-ranking officer present. Several other senior officers attended as witnesses, and even General Gu was required to be there.","\"So you admit to bringing Corporal Yuan outside the city?\" one of the interrogators asked.","\"Yes,\" Captain Chen answered truthfully.","\"Where did you take him?\"","\"To the Purple Zone.\"","\"For what purpose?\"","\"To clear a tunnel.\"","\"And why did you choose Corporal Yuan for that?\"","\"To verify the recent rumors.\"","The interrogator narrowed his eyes. \"According to those rumors, Corporal Yuan is capable of defeating a Void Guardian by himself—but only one from the Red Zone. Yet you brought him into the Purple Zone. What was your reasoning behind that decision?\"","\"We initially planned only for the Red Zone, but Corporal Yuan insisted he wanted something more challenging, so we brought him to the Purple Zone instead.\"","\"What happened in the Purple Zone? Why did you return without Corporal Yuan?\" the interrogator asked.","\"Everything went smoothly at first. We even managed to clear the tunnel in the Purple Zone. However, just as we were preparing to return, Corporal Yuan said he wanted to take a look at the Black Zone.\"","\"Of course, we were against it at first, but he insisted that he wouldn’t leave until he had seen the Black Zone for himself.\"","\"And then? What happened?\"","\"We traveled to the Black Zone—or at least to its border. However, Corporal Yuan wasn’t satisfied with merely looking at it from the outside and entered by himself. We tried to follow him, but he was too fast. The Black Zone was far too dangerous for us to pursue him any deeper, so we decided to return to the city and report what had happened.\"","Captain Chen paused briefly before continuing, \"That was when we encountered the Stellar Squad and were arrested.\"","Once they finished interrogating Captain Chen, they brought in the next member of the Scorpion Squad. Each of them was questioned separately until every member had given their testimony.","Unsurprisingly, they all gave similar answers.","\"A bunch of nonsense!\" General Mei sneered in disdain after hearing their testimony. \"Why the hell would Corporal Yuan enter the Black Zone all by himself?! That makes no sense at all!\"","\"I must agree with General Mei. Nobody would be stupid enough to enter the Black Zone alone, especially someone who’d just recently joined the military.\"","General Gu then spoke. \"Corporal Yuan is an unusual and rather arrogant individual. It wouldn’t surprise me if he entered the Black Zone purely out of overconfidence.\"","He paused briefly before adding, \"It’s unfortunate, but I highly doubt Corporal Yuan can survive in there alone.\"","Another officer then spoke. \"We can discuss Corporal Yuan later. Right now, we should focus on the Scorpion Squad. Although they didn’t break any rules by bringing Corporal Yuan outside the city, if he truly is dead, they should still be held responsible for failing to ensure his safety—regardless of the choices Corporal Yuan made while outside.\"","\"That hardly seems fair to the Scorpion Squad. They didn’t do anything wrong, and it was Corporal Yuan who insisted on entering the Purple Zone, let alone the Black Zone. I don’t think they should be blamed for his death, much less held responsible for it,\" another officer argued, one publicly known to support General Gu.","\"That’s assuming the Scorpion Squad is telling the truth,\" remarked an officer seated beside General Mei. \"For all we know, they could’ve deliberately brought Corporal Yuan, who didn’t know any better, into the Black Zone and abandoned him there to die.\"","\"That’s a serious accusation, Colonel Jing. Do you have any proof that they intended to do such a thing?\"","Colonel Jing sneered. \"I could ask you the same question. Do you have any proof that they didn’t bring Corporal Yuan outside with the intention of getting him killed?\"","\"The fact that the system hasn’t branded any of them as traitors should be more than enough proof of their innocence!\"","\"There are plenty of ways to circumvent the system, and we all know that the Scorpion Squad is notorious for bending and breaking the rules.\"","For the next several minutes, the officers on both sides continued arguing back and forth, neither willing to concede to the other."]},{"number":2634,"title":"Chapter 2634: Verdict","paragraphs":["\"Although the Scorpion Squad is infamous for causing trouble, that was a long time ago!\" one of the officers on General Gu’s side exclaimed. \"Besides, what reason would they have to want Corporal Yuan dead? It’s not as though they have any grudges against him!\"","\"We all know why they want him dead!\"","The officers on General Mei’s side immediately turned their gazes toward General Gu, who remained seated in silence with a calm, almost indifferent expression.","The reason was obvious to everyone in the room, especially after General Mei’s recent accusations against him. Even so, not a single person dared to say it aloud.","Seeing this, General Gu turned toward Mei Feng.","\"Do you see this, General Mei? Because of your baseless accusations, everyone now thinks I want Corporal Yuan dead.\"","\"...\" Mei Feng remained silent.","\"Since we’re already on the subject, let me ask you directly—have you found any evidence to support those accusations? Or do you intend to keep tarnishing my reputation with nothing but lies?\"","The room instantly fell deathly silent, with many of the officers holding their breath as they waited for Mei Feng’s response.","After what felt like an eternity, she finally spoke.","\"Whatever evidence I possess is not something I intend to reveal here. Once everything is properly prepared, I’ll hand it over to the appropriate authorities.\"","General Gu sneered in disdain at her response and said, \"So you intend to drag the Supreme General into your lies, huh? I have underestimated your recklessness!\"","\"If you’re truly innocent, you would have nothing to worry about, and I will bear all responsibility for my actions.\"","General Gu suddenly rose from his seat. \"I’m leaving. As for the Scorpion Squad, I’ll leave their fate in General Mei’s hands, even if that means innocent soldiers may end up suffering for it.\"","He turned toward the exit.","\"I want to see just how far her madness will go.\"","Without another word, he left the room shortly afterward.","A few other officers from General Gu’s side also left, but some of them remained.","\"What are you going to do about the Scorpion Squad, General?\" someone eventually asked Mei Feng.","Mei Feng closed her eyes and took a deep breath before giving her verdict, \"Release them.\"","\"What?!\"","Her own officers exclaimed in shock, as none of them expected her to let the Scorpion Squad go for killing Yuan. Even those from General Gu’s side were surprised by her verdict and stared at her with widened eyes.","Mei Feng continued, elaborating on her decision. \"Regardless of my personal opinion of the Scorpion Squad—or what I believe their true intentions were—the fact remains that we don’t have enough concrete evidence to convict them.\"","\"But—\"","\"Moreover!\" Mei Feng interrupted before the officer could continue. \"There’s still no proof that Corporal Yuan is dead. The Ironwoman is out there searching for him as we speak, so we’ll postpone the Scorpion Squad’s final verdict until we know more.\"","As much as Mei Feng wanted to find the Scorpion Squad guilty and punish them for Yuan’s presumed death, she was still a general. No matter how strongly she felt, even she couldn’t ignore military procedure and pass judgment based solely on suspicion.","\"Also, to prevent something like this from happening again, effective immediately, soldiers of any rank are forbidden from taking personnel into areas they are not qualified to enter. Furthermore, all soldiers leaving the city will be required to officially check out at the gate.\"","Before anyone could voice their thoughts on the decision, Mei Feng turned around and left the room.","Shortly afterward, the Scorpion Squad was released from custody. However, they were far from completely free. Until a final verdict was reached, every member was prohibited from leaving the military base.","It didn’t take long before word of the situation spread like wildfire throughout the military base.","\"Did you hear? The Scorpion Squad is suspected of luring Corporal Yuan outside the city to kill him!\"","\"The Scorpion Squad? Why am I not surprised it’s them? But why would they do something like that? Did Corporal Yuan somehow offend them?\"","\"Don’t tell anyone I told you this, but according to some people, the Scorpion Squad was acting on General Gu’s behalf. Apparently, he holds a grudge against Corporal Yuan for refusing to join his division.\"","\"General Gu, huh? I can believe that, especially considering how bitter he’s been ever since the Ironwoman appeared.\"","\"So what’s going to happen to the Scorpion Squad?\"","\"They’re released for now, but it’s still possible for them to be responsible for Corporal Yuan’s death.\"","\"What a pity... Corporal Yuan’s death, I mean. He was so talented and was likely to surpass the Ironwoman.\"","Meanwhile, in a private room, Sergeant Bing sighed aloud, \"It’s my fault. I should’ve kept a closer eye on him.\"","\"No, it’s my fault. It was my turn to look after him on that day...\" Sergeant Quang shook his head.","\"You’re acting like he’s already dead...\" Wu Wang said. \"Knowing that guy, he’s probably still alive.\"","\"No matter how talented he is, there’s no way he can deal with five captains by himself,\" said Sergeant Quang with a frown on his face.","\"I... wouldn’t be so sure about that,\" said Shi Fa.","At the same time, the Scorpion Squad went to report the situation to their superior. Of course, this superior wasn’t General Gu, as that would be too obvious.","\"Tell me what I want to hear.\"","\"Corporal Yuan is dead,\" said Captain Chen.","\"Did you see it with your own eyes?\"","\"...Yes.\"","\"Are you certain? Because according to your testimony, he went into the Black Zone and vanished.\"","Captain Dung sneered. \"What else were we supposed to tell them? That we made sure Corporal Yuan died before our eyes?\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Captain Chen asked, \"What’s going to happen to us now?\"","\"If you’re worried that something might happen to you, then understand this—you would’ve already been punished if they had enough evidence. The delayed verdict is most likely just a way to buy them more time to continue investigating.\"","\"Even if Corporal Yuan is ultimately presumed dead and you’re held responsible for what happened to him, the most likely punishment would be a demotion for failing to ensure his safety, which is essentially a slap on the wrist. Of course, we’ll help you regain your rank back as fast as possible.\"","\"What if Corporal Yuan returns?\" one of the members suddenly asked.","\"Is there any reason why you would even have such a thought?\"","The superior frowned.","\"N-No... I spoke without thinking just now.\"","\"...\"","The other members glared at him, but none of them dared to utter another word, fearing the truth might get out.","\"In any case, stay put and don’t leave your living quarters until the situation dies down.\"","\"Yes, Colonel Ran.\"","A few weeks later, just as General Mei was prepared to leave, she noticed a certain presence approaching her office.","\"I’m back.\"","The Ironwoman’s voice resounded as the door opened a moment later.","Seeing the Ironwoman return alone, Mei Feng sank back into her seat and let out a defeated sigh.","\"So... he really is dead, huh?\"","However, the Ironwoman ignored the remark and asked, \"What happened to the Scorpion Squad?\"","\"We don’t have enough evidence to charge them with murder or conspiracy,\" Mei Feng replied. \"At most, we can hold them responsible for negligence and failing to protect a junior soldier.\"","\"Did you already give the final verdict?\"","\"No, I was just about to leave to do that. I have delayed it for as long as I could, too.\"","\"Do as you please. It won’t matter, anyway.\"","\"What do you mean?\" Mei Feng raised her eyebrows.","\"I mean, Corporal Yuan is still alive.\"","\"WHAT?!\" Mei Feng slammed the desk as she stood up with a bewildered look on her face.","\"H-Has he returned?! Where is he now?!\"","However, the Ironwoman shook her head and said, \"I’ll tell you where he is as long as you promise me that you won’t get angry at me.\"","\"What the hell are you talking about? Why would I be angry at you?\"","The Ironwoman suddenly removed her mask and rubbed her eyes.","\"Corporal Yuan... is still outside the city. In fact, he’s currently in the Black Zone.\"","\"W-What...?\" Mei Feng muttered with a dazed expression.","\"He said it was the perfect opportunity for him to train alone, and he told me to return without him.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Mei Feng began to tremble.","\"ARE YOU INSANE?!\" she shouted, slamming her desk so hard that it smashed into countless pieces.","\"Hey, you promised not to be angry.\"","\"I made no such promise!\" Mei Feng exclaimed before falling silent again.","\"You actually left him behind? In the Black Zone? Alone?\" she muttered in disbelief some moments later.","\"Don’t make it sound like I did it on purpose. He insisted on being left alone.\"","\"I don’t care what he said! You should’ve dragged him back, even if it was against his will!\"","The Ironwoman shook her head and said, \"You can say that because you don’t know what he’s fully capable of.\"","\"What are you talking about?\"","\"You really think I didn’t consider dragging him back here?\" the Ironwoman sighed.","\"I won’t go into the details because I made a promise, but I don’t think I could’ve dragged him back here without killing him, so I’d be bringing back his corpse if I went that route.\"","Mei Feng stared at her with a baffled face, as if unable to believe her own ears.","\"In any case, there’s no need to worry about him. He’ll return in a few months once he’s done,\" the Ironwoman continued in a confident voice."]},{"number":2635,"title":"Chapter 2635: Verdict(2)","paragraphs":["\"Unbelievable...\" Mei Feng was at a loss for words after learning of Yuan’s situation through the Ironwoman.","\"And I mean both you and Corporal Yuan.\"","\"Can you really blame me? I already told you that dragging him back by force would’ve been nearly impossible without killing him.\"","\"You know, I’m having a hard time believing that someone who only recently joined the military could give you this much trouble...\" Mei Feng muttered.","She paused before adding, \"No, forget the military. If you knew what his cultivation was just a year ago, you wouldn’t believe it either.\"","\"What are you talking about?\" the Ironwoman asked, raising an eyebrow as curiosity flickered in her eyes.","Mei Feng pondered for a moment whether she should really tell her this.","\"That man... his cultivation was only at the First Ascension a year ago when I met him.\"","\"Wh-What did you just say...?\"","The Ironwoman’s eyes immediately widened, looking like she’d just seen a ghost.","Mei Feng chuckled at the Ironwoman’s reaction, as it was the first time she’d seen her look so surprised.","’I cannot even begin to imagine how she’d react if she knew that he also possessed the Perfected Heavenly Refinement physique...’ Mei Feng thought to herself, but she had no intention of revealing this secret.","\"I have so many questions...\" the Ironwoman spoke after a long moment of silence.","However, Mei Feng shook her head and said, \"Keep them to yourself because I won’t be able to answer them.\"","The Ironwoman sighed before responding, \"Anyways, what are you going to do now that he’s alive?\"","\"...\"","Mei Feng closed her eyes to ponder for several minutes before speaking again, \"I will continue to act like he’s dead until he actually returns to the city safe and sound. As for the verdict, there will be no change—at least until Corporal Yuan returns to testify against them. As for what comes after that... we can only wait and see.\"","\"Alright.\" The Ironwoman nodded before retrieving a cube-shaped object and casually tossing it into Mei Feng’s grasp.","\"Give it to him when he returns,\" said the Ironwoman as she turned around and started leaving.","\"If he doesn’t return, his blood will be on your hands,\" Mei Feng said in a low voice.","Without stopping, the Ironwoman reached for the door.","\"I know,\" she responded before leaving the room.","Mei Feng sat back in her chair and released a deep sigh.","\"That brat...\"","She looked at the storage cube in her grasp before taking a peek inside.","\"So many Unknown Ores!\"","Mei Feng’s eyes widened with surprise to see its storage filled to the brim with Unknown Ores, wondering why the Ironwoman wanted to give them to Yuan.","’Did she gather these while looking for him...? There’s no way, right?’","As far as Mei Feng knew, the Ironwoman never bothered to collect Unknown Ores herself, considering it a waste of her time and effort. She typically left such menial tasks to her squad members, so seeing her return with so many was rather unusual.","Some time later, Mei Feng left to give her final verdict on the Scorpion Squad—but not before calling someone to have her desk replaced.","Once Mei Feng gave her final verdict, every member of the Scorpion Squad was demoted by one rank, which may not seem like a lot, but going from Captain to Sergeant meant they’d lost at least two to three decades of their lives.","It didn’t take long before the news spread.","\"Doesn’t this mean that Corporal Yuan is truly dead?\"","\"A pity... a true pity...\"","The news got so big that it’d even reached the soldiers training in boot camp.","\"What?! The monster from the same recruitment as us was killed?!\"","\"???\"","Mei Xiaoyun’s entire body froze upon hearing the news, her eyes widening in shock and disbelief.","’Yuan’s dead...? There’s no way...’ she thought to herself.","Then, she approached one of the instructors and asked for more information.","\"About Corporal Yuan... is it true that he’s dead?\"","\"That’s right. It was already known a few weeks ago, but it wasn’t confirmed until recently.\"","\"Do you know what happened?\"","The instructor sighed and said, \"Do you know of the Scorpion Squad?\"","\"No.\"","\"Well, they’re a group of troublemakers, and supposedly, they lured Corporal Yuan to the Black Zone to have him killed. Of course, that’s what some people believe is the truth. Unfortunately, we may never know.\"","Mei Xiaoyun frowned. \"Why would they want him dead? Did Corporal Yuan offend them somehow?\"","\"...\"","The instructor looked at her with a hesitant expression.","\"I normally wouldn’t tell another soldier something like this, but considering you’re General Mei’s daughter, you would probably find out sooner or later anyway...\"","The instructor proceeded to explain, \"General Mei and General Gu are currently competing to become the next Supreme General. With General Mei already supported by the Ironwoman—one of the most talented and respected soldiers in the military—General Gu has been under immense pressure.\"","\"He likely saw Corporal Yuan as someone who could balance the scales in his favor. Unfortunately for him, Corporal Yuan ended up joining General Mei’s side instead. If Corporal Yuan grows into someone comparable to the Ironwoman, General Mei’s promotion would be all but guaranteed. That gives General Gu plenty of reason to want him gone.\"","\"Is that so...\" Mei Xiaoyun muttered, looking dazed.","After a moment of silence, Mei Xiaoyun spoke again. \"Instructor, I’m not feeling well today, so I won’t be participating in training.\"","\"O-Okay...\"","Normally, soldiers weren’t allowed to decide for themselves when to attend training. However, Mei Xiaoyun was General Mei’s daughter and the top performer among the new soldiers, so the instructors tended to be far more lenient with her.","Moreover, it was obvious that the news of Yuan’s presumed death had affected her deeply. Allowing her to train while she was emotionally distracted could potentially put her in danger.","Once Mei Xiaoyun returned to the barracks, the instructors began chatting among themselves.","\"I wonder what her relationship with Corporal Yuan is.\"","\"Do you really need to ask? Isn’t it already obvious enough by how she reacted to the news of his death? I’d bet an entire year’s salary that they’re lovers!\""]},{"number":2636,"title":"Chapter 2636: A Soldier Or a Bandit?","paragraphs":["Another two months passed after news of Yuan’s presumed death spread throughout the military.","Because of the incident, the Scorpion Squad had become one of the most hated squads in the entire military and was constantly harassed and bullied by other soldiers, particularly those aligned with General Mei.","At first, almost no one was willing to stand up for them. However, as time passed, more and more soldiers from General Gu’s side began stepping in to protect them.","Whenever someone confronted the Scorpion Squad, the encounter almost always devolved into a heated argument or outright brawl.","Although Yuan was still a new soldier, he had already earned a favorable reputation among his peers, largely because he frequently helped others during gathering missions—work that most soldiers considered tedious and burdensome.","However, the Scorpion Squad couldn’t care less about the situation or being targeted. They were simply relieved that Yuan had not returned to the city, as that could spell their end.","Meanwhile, in the Black Zone, Yuan had been hunting Void Specters nonstop, continuously increasing his Eternal Essence.","Though for efficiency, he did not simply wander the Black Zone killing Void Specters. Whenever he would encounter a tunnel, he would enter it and clear it alone, as the Elite Void Specters and Unknown Crystals found inside granted the most Eternal Essence.","One day, purely by coincidence, Yuan entered a tunnel that was already occupied by another group of soldiers.","The moment he sensed their presence, he concealed his own. However, rather than leaving, he decided to clear the tunnel before they did.","Fortunately, the tunnel branched into numerous paths, allowing Yuan to easily avoid the other group, slip past them unnoticed, and reach the end long before they could.","After defeating the Void Guardian at the end of the tunnel, Yuan absorbed all of the Eternal Essence contained within the Unknown Crystals before swiftly making his way out, leaving the other soldiers completely unaware that someone had beaten them to their destination.","Several days after Yuan secretly cleared the tunnel, the soldiers finally reached the end, but to their shock and puzzlement, the Void Guardian was nowhere to be seen.","\"What the heck? Where’s the Void Guardian?\"","\"Did someone already clear this tunnel?\" another soldier wondered aloud.","Although it wasn’t unheard of for two groups to enter the same tunnel without realizing it until they reached the end, the soldiers quickly dismissed that possibility. If another group had truly arrived before them, the Unknown Crystals should have been harvested as well, yet every single one remained untouched.","\"Don’t tell me that this tunnel was created without a Void Guardian?\"","\"This would be an unprecedented event if that were the case!\"","In the end, the soldiers decided to document the unusual occurrence before harvesting the Unknown Crystals and leaving the tunnel.","They then hastily returned to their city to report the discovery.","In the third month of wandering the Black Zone, Yuan had his second encounter with soldiers from another city.","Although Yuan could have easily avoided the soldiers, he decided to see for himself whether encounters with people from another city were truly as dangerous as the Ironwoman had warned.","\"What the—?\"","The soldiers froze the moment they saw Yuan. While encountering someone alone in the Black Zone was surprising enough, what shocked them even more was the insignia on his uniform.","\"Am I seeing things, or is this guy a corporal?\"","\"He’s definitely a corporal.\"","\"What is a corporal doing out here alone—\"","\"Look around him! There are Unknown Ores everywhere!\"","However, their curiosity about Yuan’s presence vanished the moment they noticed the countless Unknown Ores glistening across the ground beneath him.","The soldiers exchanged glances, greed flickering in their eyes.","A moment later, one of them turned toward Yuan and shouted, \"Kid, if you don’t want any more trouble than you’re already in, leave those Unknown Ores alone!\"","Yuan calmly responded, \"If you want the Unknown Ores, go ahead and take them.\"","Without a word, the soldiers immediately went to gather the Unknown Ores into their storage cube while Yuan quietly watched them.","Suddenly, one of them approached Yuan with a cold smile and said, \"While we’re at it, hand over all of your belongings.\"","In his eyes, the only reason Yuan would leave behind so many Unknown Ores was that his storage cube had already reached its capacity, leaving him with no way to carry the rest.","\"...\"","\"Are you a soldier, or are you a bandit?\" Yuan asked with a raised eyebrow.","\"Who the hell gave you permission to question me?\" the soldier frowned. \"I will not ask again. Hand over all of your belongings!\"","Yuan shrugged and said, \"The only thing I have is this minigun. You can have it if you want.\"","\"You dare mess with me?! Do you have a death wish?!\" the soldier shouted, believing that Yuan was deliberately mocking him.","\"So you’re not only a bandit, but a murderer as well?\" Yuan asked with an indifferent expression. \"Which city are you from? So I know when to stay away from your people the next time I encounter them.\"","The soldier trembled in anger before lunging at Yuan with killing intent.","\"There won’t be a next time!\"","Seeing this, Yuan released a disappointed sigh.","The next moment, a tremendous amount of Eternal Essence erupted from Yuan’s body.","Although the soldiers were unable to sense the energy itself, they immediately felt the atmosphere around him change. In an instant, Yuan’s entire presence became completely different—far heavier and more imposing than before.","\"What—\"","Before the soldier could even react, his head vanished from his neck.","The soldiers who had been busy collecting the Unknown Ores abruptly stopped and turned toward Yuan. However, the moment they saw their companion hovering before him without a head, they froze in stunned silence, struggling to comprehend what they were even looking at.","\"C-Captain Hong!\"","The soldiers eventually snapped out of their daze and cried out loud, their eyes wide with shock and disbelief."]},{"number":2637,"title":"Chapter 2637: A New Type of Void Specter","paragraphs":["\"Bastard! What did you do to Captain Hong?!\"","The rest of the squad swiftly acted, moving to surround Yuan.","\"Isn’t it obvious what I did to him just looking at his headless corpse?\" Yuan responded in an indifferent tone.","\"W-Why?! Why did you kill him?!\" another soldier shouted.","\"Why...? Are you asking me why I defended myself?\" Yuan shook his head before continuing, \"If you’re going to continue uttering nonsense, then save your breath.\"","\"You damn—\"","The soldiers surged with killing intent at Yuan’s words.","\"Are you sure you want to do this? You can still walk away with your life,\" Yuan said.","\"You only managed to kill Captain Hong by surprise! Do not think we will make the same mistake!\"","\"And there are five of us and one of you. Do you really think you’ll be able to kill all of us with your cultivation? Laughable!\"","\"Forget about five. Even if there were five thousand of you, I’d still be able to kill all of you.\"","\"I want to see you try!\"","The next moment, one of the soldiers used Void Control and teleported behind Yuan.","\"Die!\"","The soldier struck with the intent to kill.","However, the instant his hand touched Yuan’s body, his entire body abruptly disintegrated into nothingness, vanishing from existence before he could even let out a scream.","\"What just happened?!\"","The remaining four soldiers instinctively backed away from Yuan after witnessing such a horrifying scene.","\"W-What the fuck was that?! What did he do to Captain Dean?!\"","\"This guy is not human! He must be a Void Specter in disguise!\"","\"Run!\"","The soldiers swiftly turned and ran away, their faces twisted with fear.","Yuan watched them run away, not bothering to chase after them.","’So that’s what happens when I use my affinity on another human...’ Yuan thought, shuddering slightly.","This was his first time using his affinity on anything other than materials, and the result far exceeded his expectations. Quite frankly, even Yuan found it terrifying.","’Let’s not use it unless absolutely necessary...’ he sighed inwardly.","Yuan continued his training shortly after.","Meanwhile, the soldiers from the encounter went straight back to their city, not stopping to rest until they reached their military base. Upon their return, they reported their encounter with Yuan to their superior, describing him as a Void Specter who was indistinguishable from an ordinary human.","\"What? A Void Specter indistinguishable from a human had killed Captain Hong and Captain Dean? That almost sounds like the Void Hunter!\"","\"No! This monster was something else entirely! The moment Captain Dean came into contact with this monster, his entire body disintegrated like ash!\"","\"Hell, it can even speak like a normal human!\"","\"This is definitely a new type of Void Specter!\"","\"Where did you find this monster?\" the superior asked.","\"In the level 1 Black Zone!\"","The superior pondered for a long moment before speaking again, \"I am going to prepare a squad of eight powerful soldiers, and I want one of you to bring them to the location.\"","\"You want to fight that monster?! It’s better to avoid it! I’m telling you!\"","\"Listen here. If another monster that is on par with the Void Hunter—especially if it is indistinguishable from an ordinary human—we need to investigate it properly, regardless of the risks.\"","The superior released a deep sigh before continuing, \"I will let you guys discuss among yourselves who wants to take the job. I don’t want to force anyone, but if a decision is not reached by the time the team is assembled, I will have all of you go. If you volunteer, I will make sure you’re rewarded properly. Do I make myself clear?\"","\"Yes, Colonel...\"","A few days later, the team was assembled, and one of the soldiers who’d encountered Yuan willingly volunteered to accept the mission.","\"I’m Captain Heen, and I’ll brief you on this monster while we make our way to its location.\"","Thus, Captain Heen and eight powerful soldiers—all holding the rank of major—set out for the Black Zone to investigate the newly discovered monster.","At the same time, the other soldiers who encountered Yuan handed in the Unknown Ores they’d gathered with his approval.","A few days later, all of these soldiers were summoned by the General of their military.","\"Where did you acquire these Unknown Ores?\" the General questioned them while pointing to the pile of glistening ores before him.","\"We collected them during our previous mission,\" replied the soldiers.","\"Why? Is there something wrong with them?\" another asked.","However, the General didn’t answer this question and continued to ask, \"Did you do anything special with them?\"","\"No, not that I can think of. We immediately returned to the city after gathering them because of that monster who killed two of our members.\"","\"Tell me how you managed to gather them again?\"","The soldiers went on to reveal that the Unknown Ores originally belonged to the monster and that they’d taken them from him.","Once he was satisfied, the General spoke, revealing why he was questioning them, \"The Unknown Ores you gathered... not a single one of them contains any energy!\"","\"What?!\"","The soldiers exclaimed in disbelief.","\"H-How is that even possible? If they truly lack energy, they wouldn’t be glistening like that! At least, they shouldn’t!\"","\"I don’t know, but we can assume that this monster you encountered had something to do with it,\" said the General.","The soldiers swallowed nervously, as this monster was becoming increasingly incomprehensible.","Some time later, the special squad arrived at their destination in the Black Zone.","\"This is the place. Look on the ground. The Unknown Ores left behind by him are still here!\" Captain Heen said, pointing toward the trail of Unknown Ores Yuan had left behind.","\"This is...\"","The soldiers swallowed nervously as they stared at the scattered ores. There was something deeply unsettling about the sight, though none of them could quite put the feeling into words.","\"It feels like a trap, as though someone deliberately left these ores behind to lure us in,\" one of them finally said, voicing what everyone else was thinking."]},{"number":2638,"title":"Chapter 2638: Following the Trail","paragraphs":["\"What should we do? It’s clearly inviting—provoking us.\"","\"There’s only one thing we can do. Our mission.\"","\"Stay alert, everyone. And don’t engage without instructions.\"","The group of soldiers slowly followed the trail of Unknown Ores while keeping their presence concealed to the best of their abilities.","Meanwhile, not too far away, Yuan just finished clearing a tunnel all by himself. But before he could even exit the tunnel, he sensed several presences outside the tunnel.","’They are...’","Once he exited the tunnel, he could see several familiar-looking soldiers gathering the Unknown Ores that he’d left behind outside.","When Yuan came out of the tunnel, these soldiers stopped their movements to look at him.","\"Huh? Aren’t you that corporal with the Ironwoman? Did you just come out of that tunnel?\" one of them asked out loud.","These soldiers were the ones that Yuan had encountered while he was still with the Ironwoman.","\"Indeed, I did come out of the tunnel,\" Yuan replied.","\"...\"","The soldiers didn’t say anything else and fell silent, but they continued to stare in Yuan’s direction, almost as if they were waiting for someone else to show up.","Eventually, one of them asked, \"Where’s the Ironwoman?\"","\"She returned to the city,\" Yuan admitted.","\"Huh? The Ironwoman left you—a mere corporal—all alone in the Black Zone? There’s no way...\"","\"I don’t believe you. I bet she’s still inside that tunnel.\"","The soldiers found Yuan’s explanation difficult to believe. Given the Ironwoman’s reputation, they couldn’t imagine her deliberately leaving a low-ranking soldier behind to fend for himself in such a dangerous place.","Yuan shrugged and said, \"What do I gain from lying about this? You’re free to check the tunnels if you don’t believe me.\"","\"N-No... It’s fine...\"","\"But what were you doing inside the tunnel all by yourself? If you were looking for a place to hide, it’s actually much more dangerous inside than outside.\"","\"No, I was clearing it.\"","\"You...? Clearing a tunnel? All by yourself?\"","The soldiers fell silent again before they suddenly burst out laughing.","\"Hahaha!\"","\"Now that is definitely a lie!\"","\"There’s no way a Fifth Ascension cultivator like you could accomplish something alone that would normally require an entire squad of Sixth Ascension cultivators!\" one of them stated.","Yuan merely shrugged before turning to leave without another word.","\"Hey! Where are you going?\" one of the soldiers called out to him.","\"Why does it matter where I am going?\" Yuan asked.","\"T-That’s...\" the soldier fell silent.","\"If you have nothing else for me, I’ll be taking my leave now.\"","\"Aren’t you going to ask about these Unknown Ores?\" another soldier suddenly asked.","\"Unless you’re going to share them with me, I don’t really care.\"","The soldiers raised their eyebrows. It should be obvious that they weren’t going to share them with a soldier from another city.","\"No? Then goodbye.\"","Yuan left shortly after, with nobody stopping him this time.","\"Should we really have allowed him to leave?\" one of the soldiers asked out loud after Yuan was no longer in their field of view.","\"What else were we supposed to do? He’s none of our business.\"","\"I guess so...\"","Some time later, the soldiers finally stopped gathering once their storage cubes were filled to the brim with Unknown Ores.","\"After we clear this tunnel, let’s return to the base and grab more storage cubes for the rest.\"","Although they wanted to continue collecting the ores, they simply had no space left to store them. Thus, they decided to clear the tunnel first and harvest the Unknown Crystals within before returning for the remaining ores.","\"Just where the hell did all these Unknown Ores come from, anyways?\" one of them asked as they ventured deeper into the tunnel.","\"Why bother questioning it? Just treat it as some strange phenomenon—and a fortunate encounter for us.\"","\"What are the chances that Corporal actually cleared the tunnel all by himself?\" another wondered out loud.","\"Seriously? There’s literally no chance. If I am wrong, then I will eat my suit.\"","A few hours later—","\"Hey... we haven’t encountered a single Void Specter in hours...\"","Although no one said it aloud, the same thought gradually began creeping into their minds.","’Could that corporal have really cleared this entire place by himself...?’","The deeper they ventured, the more believable the seemingly impossible feat became. Meanwhile, the soldier who had sworn he would eat his suit if Yuan had truly cleared the tunnel by himself began sweating more and more with every passing minute.","Eventually, they reached the end of the tunnel. Without encountering a single Void Specter, of course.","\"What are the chances of a tunnel spawning without any Void Specters...?\"","\"Probably less likely than that Corporal clearing the tunnel alone...\"","After staring down into the hole for a moment, the soldiers swallowed nervously before finally jumping through the opening.","Moments later, they landed at the bottom.","\"N-No way...\"","The soldiers stared at the empty chamber, their expressions dumbfounded, their eyes wide with shock and disbelief.","\"He actually cleared the tunnel by himself?!\"","\"W-Wait! Let’s not jump to conclusions!\" said the soldier who swore he’d eat his suit. \"If that were the case, why didn’t he harvest the Unknown Crystals?!\"","\"How the hell would we know?\"","\"If he doesn’t want them, we’ll gladly take them for him!\"","The soldiers started harvesting the Unknown Crystals after snapping out of their daze, unaware that they were essentially collecting pretty crystals with no energy.","Once they were done, they made their way back up the tunnel.","However, when they emerged from the tunnel, they were taken aback to find nine unknown soldiers wearing crimson uniforms surrounding the entrance.","\"Soldiers of Ember City?!\"","\"W-We’re being ambushed!\"","The soldiers immediately armed themselves and prepared to fight.","\"Wait! We’re not here for you, soldiers of Spirit City!\" exclaimed the soldiers of Ember City.","\"What?\"","\"We’re currently investigating a certain entity, and we’ve been following the trail of Unknown Ores it left behind,\" explained one of the soldiers from Ember City. \"However, the trail abruptly ended here, so we suspected that it might have entered this tunnel.\""]},{"number":2639,"title":"Chapter 2639: Following the Trail(2)","paragraphs":["\"A trail of Unknown Ores...? In that case, it probably stopped here because we collected them,\" admitted one of the Spirit City soldiers.","\"The tunnel was also empty. Hell, it’d been cleared even before we entered it.\"","\"What sort of entity are you looking for, anyway?\" another asked.","The soldiers of Ember City exchanged glances with each other, wondering if they should reveal any information to soldiers from another city.","However, after giving it some thought, they realized that if this mysterious Void Specter was anything like the Void Hunter, keeping the information to themselves would only put everyone at greater risk. It would be wiser to share what they knew so that the cities could work together to deal with the threat.","\"As mentioned earlier, we’re currently still investigating, but from what we know so far, this is a new type of Void Specter,\" said the Ember City soldier.","\"Is that true?! A new type of Void Specter has been discovered?!\"","The soldiers of Spirit City were shocked to hear this, which wasn’t surprising, considering that it had been thousands of years since they had made such a discovery.","\"Of course it’s true. Why would we lie about something like this? This Void Specter has already killed two of our soldiers.\"","\"What does this Void Specter look like? Any special characteristics?\"","\"You’ll probably find this hard to believe, but this Void Specter looks exactly like a human. Indistinguishable, too.\"","\"A Void Specter with human features? Sounds like the Void Hunter.\"","\"No, you don’t understand. This Void Specter doesn’t just look like a human. It is literally indistinguishable from a real human, meaning if it hid in a crowd of people, we wouldn’t be able to tell it apart from the others. Hell, it can even speak the human language!\"","\"Is that even possible...? Are you sure this entity isn’t a real human?\" The soldiers of Spirit City wore doubtful expressions at this unbelievable information, wondering if this was just a big misunderstanding.","\"It’s possible, and that monster definitely wasn’t human!\" Captain Heen suddenly shouted.","\"I—my squad encountered it, and the way that monster killed my squad member... there’s no way a human is capable of vaporizing another human with a single touch!\" Captain Heen’s body trembled with fear just recalling the moment.","\"Vaporized...\"","\"With a single touch...?\"","The soldiers of Spirit City muttered with a dazed look on their faces.","\"Anyway, this Void Specter is currently disguised as a soldier from Gaia’s Heaven. He has a tall, refined build, long black hair tied into a ponytail, brown eyes, and a strikingly handsome face. If you encounter him, do not engage under any circumstances. Run away immediately.\"","The soldiers of Spirit City raised an eyebrow at this familiar-sounding description.","\"Oh, right. He’s also wearing the insignia of a corporal,\" the Ember City soldier added.","\"?!?!\"","\"That reaction... did you see this monster?\" asked Captain Chen after seeing their surprised face.","They nodded in slow motion before turning to look in the direction Yuan went.","\"H-He went that way...\"","\"Thanks! Let’s hurry up and chase after it!\" Captain Heen said to the others.","\"W-Wait!\"","\"What is it?\"","\"Are you really sure he’s a Void Specter? I still think this is some kind of misunderstanding. After all, if he really is a Void Specter, why would he clear out a tunnel by himself?\"","\"What did you just say? That monster cleared out a tunnel by himself?\" Captain Heen’s eyes widened with disbelief at this unexpected information.","\"That’s right. We said this tunnel was empty, didn’t we? Well, that wasn’t our doing. That corporal came out of this tunnel while we were collecting the Unknown Ores. In fact, he even claimed that he had cleared the entire place by himself.\"","Captain Heen fell silent upon hearing this.","\"What if this Void Specter grows stronger by consuming its own kind?\" one of the Ember City soldiers suddenly suggested.","\"Now that you mention it... we haven’t encountered a single Void Specter since we started following the trail through the Black Zone!\" another exclaimed at this realization.","\"A Void Specter that devours its own kind...?\"","The others swallowed nervously.","\"Hm? Hold on. This is actually our second encounter with this corporal.\" One of the Spirit City soldiers suddenly remarked. \"The first time we encountered him, he wasn’t alone.\"","\"Are you saying that there are actually two of these monsters wandering this land?!\" Captain Heen exclaimed in shock.","\"No...? That other individual with him is someone you should be familiar with, given her vast reputation.\"","\"Who is this person?\"","\"It’s the Ironwoman.\"","\"...\"","The place fell silent, and the soldiers of Ember City turned to look at Captain Heen, as even they were beginning to wonder if this had been a huge misunderstanding.","\"T-That must be it!\" Captain Heen suddenly exclaimed.","\"What is?\"","\"The reason this monster looks exactly like a human! It must possess some kind of ability that allows it to perfectly imitate a human’s appearance!\"","\"...\"","The others stared at him with raised eyebrows, wondering if he’d gone crazy to think of such a crazy theory.","\"Why are you all looking at me like I’m crazy?! Think about it! Would a mere corporal really be able to survive in the Black Zone for this long if he weren’t actually a Void Specter in disguise?!\" Captain Heen shouted, his voice growing louder with every word.","\"That’s...\"","As ridiculous as Captain Heen’s theory sounded, none of them could deny that it somehow seemed more plausible than a mere corporal surviving alone in the Black Zone for so long.","\"Anyway, let’s stop wasting time and continue pursuing that Void Specter. We can talk while we move.\"","\"Do you mind if we come with you?\" one of the Spirit City soldiers suddenly asked. \"We’ve interacted with him several times without any issues, and I want to see for myself whether he’s truly a Void Specter.\"","\"Well...\"","After a quick discussion, the Ember City soldiers said, \"You can follow us if you want. However, keep some distance from us. With both groups together, we’d exceed ten people, and I’d rather not risk attracting the Void Hunter while we’re already dealing with an unknown Void Specter.\""]},{"number":2640,"title":"Chapter 2640: Following the Trail(3)","paragraphs":["\"What do you guys think? What are the chances of that corporal being a Void Specter disguised as a human?\" one of the Spirit City soldiers asked his squad mates as they followed the Ember City soldiers.","\"I think it’s entirely possible and, quite frankly, very likely. He always gave me a weird vibe, but I couldn’t pinpoint it until now.\"","\"Right? Something about him just felt off.\"","\"Really? I, for one, don’t think he’s a Void Specter. I think I am just not ready to believe that a Void Specter has the capability to disguise itself as a human that perfectly... at least, not yet.\"","\"That’s reasonable. I also think he’s not a Void Specter. After all, he didn’t even try to attack us. A Void Specter that hunts its own kind and ignores humans? Hard to believe.\"","\"Didn’t he kill some of the Ember City’s soldiers?\"","\"Well, we don’t know the circumstances. They probably offended him or something. Did you see that captain’s behavior earlier? There’s definitely something very wrong with him.\"","Meanwhile, a few miles ahead of the Spirit City’s soldiers, the Ember City’s soldiers continued to follow the trail.","\"If the Void Hunter can resemble humans, it’s reasonable to believe that a special Void Specter who can perfectly copy a human’s appearance exists!\" Captain Heen spoke aloud, but he was mostly talking to himself.","\"It’s not that we don’t believe you, but we’ll reserve our judgment until we encounter—\"","\"I sense him!\"","One of the soldiers there suddenly shouted, causing everyone to tense up and slow down.","\"Hide your presence! We’re going to inspect the subject first before engaging!\"","Once everyone could see Yuan, they came to a complete halt to spectate him.","\"Can you confirm that is the entity?\" The majors turned to look at Captain Heen for confirmation.","\"I-It’s him! It’s definitely him!\" Captain Heen nodded vigorously, his body shaking nonstop.","Shortly later, the Spirit City’s soldiers also came to a halt.","\"That’s the corporal, all right.\" They confirmed.","Meanwhile, Yuan sighed inwardly after detecting the Ember City’s soldiers. ’There’s even more of them now... Are they here for revenge?\"","A moment later, he noticed the others.","’Hm? Aren’t those guys from the tunnel? Why are they also here?’","Yet, Yuan decided to pretend that he hadn’t noticed them, curious to see how the situation would unfold.","He continued to hunt Void Specters and absorb Unknown Ores, not caring if these soldiers could see everything.","\"My lord! Do you see how fast he kills the Void Specters?! He’s cleaning them up like trash!\"","\"And the way he collects Unknown Ores! I have never seen anything like that before!\"","\"Inhuman! Simply inhuman! He’s definitely a Void Specter!\"","It didn’t take long for many of the Ember City soldiers to become convinced that Yuan wasn’t human at all, but rather a Void Specter disguised as one.","\"I told you that guy isn’t human!\" Captain Heen exclaimed, feeling vindicated now that the others were finally beginning to believe him, seemingly proving that his suspicions had been right all along.","As for the soldiers from Spirit City, they weren’t as easily convinced. However, even they were beginning to understand why Captain Heen was so adamant that Yuan wasn’t human.","\"How is he using so much energy when his cultivation is only at the Fifth Ascension? Where is he getting his power from?\"","\"Isn’t it obvious?!\" Captain Heen responded. \"He’s recovering his energy from the Void Specters that he devours!\"","\"So he’s the one digging up all those Unknown Ores and leaving them behind... No wonder he didn’t seem the slightest bit interested in them before. But what could possibly be the purpose of doing that?\" one of the Spirit City soldiers muttered.","\"It’s obviously a trap to lure us in! He knows how valuable Unknown Ores are to us, so he’s using them as bait!\"","\"If that were really the case, then why didn’t he kill us when he had plenty of opportunities to do so? We were literally collecting those Unknown Ores right in front of him—even talking to him while we did it!\"","Captain Heen sneered. \"How the hell would I know what it’s thinking? Maybe you lot were simply too weak for it to even consider you prey.\"","\"...\"","The soldiers from Spirit City weren’t particularly surprised by his remark. It was common for soldiers from different cities to mock or look down on one another, so they simply ignored the insult.","These soldiers continued to watch Yuan from afar for several hours before one of them asked, \"So, what now? Are we just going to keep watching him, or are we going to do something? There’s only so much we can learn like this.\"","Captain Heen sneered and said, \"If you’re so impatient, why don’t you go ahead and approach him yourself? In fact, anyone who thinks he isn’t a Void Specter should just go ahead and approach him.\"","\"...\"","Even though some of these soldiers were still skeptical, they weren’t willing to risk their lives for it, so they all fell silent and continued watching Yuan.","Eventually, another soldier suddenly asked, \"What if the Void Hunter appears? Do you think he’ll try to fight that, too?\"","\"Who knows? But I hope they do fight.\"","\"Although we have more than ten people here, the chances of the Void Hunter appearing with our number are minuscule, so don’t expect it to show up.\"","\"It may not be likely, but it’s not impossible, right? Besides, with all the commotion he’s—\"","The soldier abruptly stopped speaking as a chill ran down his spine.","The next moment, the atmosphere around them noticeably shifted. The temperature plummeted by several dozen degrees, and the once-scorching barren landscape suddenly became bitterly cold.","\"T-This is!\"","Everyone but Yuan immediately realized the reason for the sudden change.","\"Th-This phenomenon! The Void Hunter... It’s going to appear!\"","\"Shit! Shit! Shit! Do we run away?!\"","\"No!\" Captain Heen shouted. \"Not yet! Not until we see how that monster will respond to the Void Hunter!\"","\"What if they come after us together?!\"","\"...\"","Meanwhile, Yuan came to a halt after sensing the sudden change in the atmosphere.","’The Void Hunter? Is it going to appear here? Now?’ Yuan thought to himself after overhearing the others.","He contemplated how he should react. Should he stay and fight it? Or should he run away?","’If Tian Yuchen, who has reached the 50th floor of Endless Assault, cannot defeat this Void Hunter, there’s practically zero chance I can defeat it...’ he sighed inwardly.","Yet, he didn’t want to run away just yet.","’Let’s take a look at it before I leave...’","Since opportunities to encounter the Void Hunter were exceedingly rare, with everyone actively doing their best to avoid it, Yuan decided to remain a while longer and observe it for himself.","After a few moments of silence, he noticed a lone silhouette emerging in the distance, slowly making its way toward him while exuding an ominous and menacing aura.","Sure enough, the Void Hunter looked remarkably human. If Yuan hadn’t known its identity beforehand, even he might have mistaken it for another human.","\"Fuck... what a tremendous aura!\" Yuan cursed aloud as cold sweat drenched his body.","The Void Hunter radiated a terrifying aura that surpassed that of every Eternal Yuan had encountered before, with the sole exception of Prime Eternals."]},{"number":2641,"title":"Chapter 2641: Void Hunter’s Appearance","paragraphs":["The moment the Void Hunter appeared, its overwhelming presence engulfed the entire area like an impossibly heavy blanket, bearing down with the weight of several mountains. The soldiers watching Yuan immediately felt as though their bodies were on the verge of being crushed beneath the immense pressure.","The Void Hunter—the ultimate and apex predator of this world. Even if every force in the world united against it, they would still have no chance of victory. That was precisely why everyone had long since chosen to avoid it rather than fight.","Yet, when faced with this unfathomable existence, Yuan did not think about fleeing. Rather, his blood boiled, and his bones itched with the intense desire to fight it!","Meanwhile, the Void Hunter showed no urgency as it slowly but steadily approached Yuan, almost as though it were certain that its prey had no chance of escaping its grasp.","With every step it took, the Void Hunter’s already ridiculous aura increased further, as if there was no limit to its power.","\"...\"","Yuan was beginning to question whether he should really fight the Void Hunter in his current state. As much as he wanted to test himself against it, he knew that he had virtually no chance of defeating it.","Moreover, the Void Hunter’s aura was gradually approaching the level of a Prime Eternal—or at least the level of power Deemo, the Demon God, had displayed during their battle.","\"Are you going to run away?\"","A calm voice suddenly echoed.","\"?!\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes at the Void Hunter.","\"Did it just speak?\" he mumbled to himself.","\"Did... Did the Void Hunter just speak?!\" The soldiers watching from afar were just as shocked as Yuan—if not even more so. None of them had ever heard of the Void Hunter being capable of speech.","\"What are you?\" Yuan decided to try talking to the Void Hunter.","\"I am... life.\"","\"I am... death.\"","\"I am... eternity!\"","A voice responded.","Then, without warning, the Void Hunter’s silhouette vanished into thin air.","Yuan instinctively pushed his senses to their absolute limit, but even then, he couldn’t detect the Void Hunter’s presence anywhere, as though it had truly disappeared from existence.","\"Did it... leave?\"","However, the moment those three words left Yuan’s mouth, the Void Hunter suddenly reappeared directly in front of him, standing no more than a single step away.","\"?!\"","Yuan immediately reacted, attempting to use Void Manipulation. However, before he could even activate it, a devastating punch slammed into his stomach, sending him flying into the distance.","Yuan quickly stabilized himself, coughing up a mouthful of blood afterward.","\"They’re really going to fight!\" Captain Heen exclaimed in a gleeful manner.","But the other soldiers were focused on something else entirely.","\"D-Did he just survive a punch from the Void Hunter?!\"","Of course, they weren’t referring to the sheer force behind the punch. Since the Void Hunter was classified as a Void Specter, it possessed the same terrifying ability as the rest of its kind—to kill anything it touched.","\"This confirms it! There’s no way he’s human if he can survive being touched by a Void Specter!\" Captain Heen said.","No human has ever survived a touch from Void Specters, especially not the Void Hunter, after all.","As annoying as Captain Heen was, the others had to agree with him on this matter.","\"Unless the Void Hunter allowed him to live for some reason?\" one of them suddenly muttered out loud.","\"Why would it do that?\"","\"How would I know? It also spoke with him, and we never knew it could speak before!\"","Meanwhile, Yuan unleashed his Eternal Essence to its absolute limit. After several months of relentless training, his Eternal Essence had grown tremendously, reaching an astonishing three trillion years.","Unfortunately, even that amount seemed insignificant before the Void Hunter.","The Void Hunter showed no reaction to Yuan’s Eternal Essence and simply stood there in silence.","Now that Yuan could finally observe it up close, he noticed that its body was composed of the same pitch-black substance as the other Void Specters. However, unlike them, it possessed a distinctly human figure and even appeared to be wearing a cloak, its hood concealing the shape of its face.","Suddenly, the Void Hunter moved, tapping its chest with one hand while beckoning Yuan forward with the other, clearly challenging him to attack.","\"Won’t you look at this guy...\" A cold smile tugged at Yuan’s lips.","The next moment, he struck without hesitation, pouring three trillion years’ worth of Eternal Essence into a single punch.","The Void Hunter remained perfectly still, making its intentions clear—that it intended to take the attack head-on.","When Yuan’s fist slammed into its body, a devastating ripple erupted from the point of impact, surging beyond the horizon and causing the entire world to tremble for a full second.","The soldiers watching from afar were instantly swept away by the overwhelming force of the ripple, their bodies sent tumbling through the air like trash caught in a violent storm.","As for the Void Hunter, despite taking Yuan’s punch directly, it wasn’t sent flying. In fact, it didn’t move even a single inch, as though its entire body were firmly rooted to the ground.","\"...\"","Yuan wasn’t too surprised that his attack had no effect on the Void Hunter. If anything, he had expected such an outcome from the start.","Even so, seeing his attack accomplish absolutely nothing still left a bitter taste in his mouth, especially considering how much he’d trained.","’How much more do I have to train to even harm this guy?’ he sighed inwardly.","\"You...\"","The Void Hunter suddenly spoke, \"You are not worthy.\"","Before Yuan could respond, another punch slammed into his stomach.","However, unlike before, Yuan wasn’t sent flying. His feet remained firmly planted on the ground as the force of the blow pushed him back only several meters.","\"Is it just me, or did you get weaker?\" Yuan mocked it after spitting out a mouthful of blood.","\"...\"","The Void Hunter did not react to his provocation.","\"You are not worthy,\" it repeated a moment later.","Then, its aura surged even higher.","\"This bastard can still get stronger?!\" Yuan gritted his teeth as the pressure bearing down on him became increasingly unbearable. At this point, the Void Hunter’s presence had already surpassed the power Deemo displayed during their battle in the past—the same power that defeated Tian Chenyu.","Yuan prepared for the worst when the Void Hunter started moving again.","However, Yuan was left dumbfounded when the Void Hunter simply walked past him, completely ignoring his presence.","\"Where are you going?!\" Yuan called out, feeling strangely offended by the dismissal.","But the Void Hunter offered no response. Instead, it suddenly shot into the distance at the speed of light.","\"That direction... Don’t tell me it’s going after—!\"","Yuan’s expression changed the moment he realized where the Void Hunter was headed, and he quickly chased after it.","Meanwhile, not too far away, the soldiers who had been blown away by the earlier shockwave had already decided to retreat.","\"Let’s get out of here before the Void Hunter comes after us!\"","\"What about that humanoid Void Specter?!\" Captain Heen shouted. \"I need to confirm whether it’s dead!\"","\"If you want to stay behind and wait for the Void Hunter to kill you, then be our guest!\" one of his own squad members shouted. \"We’ve already confirmed the existence of the humanoid Void Specter. For now, we will return to the city and report everything we’ve learned so far!\"","But before they could get far, an unfathomable presence suddenly descended upon them, pressing down on their bodies like a colossal mountain.","Unable to withstand the immense pressure, they plummeted from the sky and crashed heavily into the ground.","\"T-This pressure! Don’t tell me the Void Hunter already defeated that humanoid Void Specter and is coming after us now!\"","\"It’s not coming after us! It’s already here!\"","Sure enough, the Void Hunter appeared before them like a ghost, its existence seemingly materializing out of thin air.","The soldiers wanted to run, but the Void Hunter’s presence was so powerful that it distorted the very space around them, making Void Control impossible for them.","Then, with calm and unhurried movements, the Void Hunter approached one of the soldiers and lightly tapped him on the forehead.","The next instant, the soldier’s entire body disintegrated into nothingness.","Yuan arrived just in time to witness the scene, and his eyes narrowed when he saw the soldier disintegrate, as it was eerily similar to how his own affinity had killed a soldier before.","However, Yuan had no time to dwell on it, as the Void Hunter was already moving toward its next target.","\"Stop!\"","He charged at the Void Hunter and attacked with all his might, desperately trying to draw its attention away from the soldiers.","Yet, the Void Hunter completely ignored him and killed a second soldier.","Then a third... a fourth...","One after another, the soldiers vanished until only one remained.","\"N-No! I don’t want to die!\" Captain Heen cried out, tears and snot streaming down his face as terror overwhelmed him.","\"Please... save me...\"","Captain Heen stared desperately at Yuan as the Void Hunter’s finger slowly approached his forehead, resembling death’s scythe descending to claim his life.","But alas, there was nothing Yuan could do but watch as the Void Hunter claimed Captain Heen’s life.","After killing every last soldier, the Void Hunter finally turned to face Yuan.","\"You are not worthy.\"","Yuan clenched his fists in irritation. The way it kept repeating those words reminded him of the entity he had encountered on the 46th floor of Endless Assault.","\"What the hell do you want from me?\" Yuan asked a moment later when it seemed to have no intention of fighting him anymore."]},{"number":2642,"title":"Chapter 2642: Fighting the Void Hunter","paragraphs":["\"Prove... your worth!\"","The Void Hunter responded to Yuan’s question before suddenly attacking again.","Yuan gritted his teeth and fought back.","\"Fuck! You already claimed that I wasn’t worthy! How the hell am I supposed to prove myself?!\"","Yuan cursed aloud as he fought with everything he could muster, even relying on his affinity—something he had been using from the very beginning.","However, for some reason, his affinity simply didn’t work on the Void Hunter.","’Whenever I attack with ordinary Eternal Essence, I can at least feel the impact. But whenever I use my affinity, it’s different... It’s like the attack never connects at all, as though the power simply vanishes the instant it makes contact. What the hell is going on? Is the Void Hunter immune to my affinity?’ Yuan pondered inwardly as he continued his futile struggle against the Void Hunter.","The way the Void Hunter nullified his affinity felt strangely familiar to Yuan, who had achieved true immunity to several elements himself.","’Since an element can also manifest as an affinity—like Shiva’s cold affinity—it would make sense for someone with a fire-based affinity to possess a natural resistance against hers,’ Yuan continued to ponder.","With an unknown number of affinities existing in the world, it wasn’t unreasonable for some to naturally counter or even fully nullify others, and Yuan began to suspect this was exactly what was happening.","Unfortunately, since he still didn’t know the true nature of his own affinity, that only made the situation more difficult to understand.","After all, if he couldn’t even identify the nature of his own affinity, what hope did he have of figuring out his opponent’s?","’There’s also a chance that...’","Yuan swallowed nervously after realizing another possibility.","’What if it has the same affinity as me?’","After all, the way it vaporized the soldiers earlier was similar—identical to when he used his affinity on the Ember City soldiers.","Time passed quickly, and Yuan’s battle with the Void Hunter continued for several days. Although Yuan was nowhere close to defeating it, one thing had become increasingly obvious.","The Void Hunter had no intention of killing him. Instead, it seemed content to continue playing with him, like a child messing with ants because they knew there was nothing the ants could do against them.","Their battle was so intense that every Void Specter in the vicinity had been annihilated by the ripples produced whenever their Eternal Essence clashed. The tremendous energy radiating from their fight had also long since alerted every city in the world to their presence.","\"T-This energy! There’s no mistaking it! The Void Hunter has appeared!\"","\"Fucking damn it! Which fools summoned that monster?! Every time the Void Hunter appears, there’s a chance it could wipe out all of humanity!\"","The emergence of the Void Hunter immediately sent every city in the world into a state of panic.","Yet not a single city dared to send soldiers to investigate, fearing that doing so might draw the Void Hunter toward them.","As a result, all they could do was remain hidden within their safe zones and pray that the monster would disappear as soon as possible.","\"Wait... who the hell is fighting the Void Hunter? For the hunter to be releasing this much energy, its opponent must be incredibly powerful!\"","As the battle continued to drag on and the Void Hunter’s energy showed no signs of diminishing, people across the cities quickly realized that whoever was fighting it was far from ordinary.","Unfortunately, none of these people had any information or record of this second energy, so they could only guess.","However, among the nine cities, there was one that had a fairly good idea of what—or rather, who—might have caused the Void Hunter to appear.","Of course, that would be Ember City, which had sent out nearly ten soldiers to investigate a newly discovered humanoid Void Specter.","Although the Void Hunter wouldn’t appear unless a group exceeded ten people, they suspected that their soldiers might have encountered another squad during the investigation and inadvertently crossed that threshold.","After all, similar incidents had happened more than once before.","With that said, the higher-ups at Ember City couldn’t fathom how they were lasting so long against the Void Hunter.","\"What are the chances that the humanoid Void Specter is the one fighting the Void Hunter?\"","\"Extremely low... but if the alternative is that our soldiers are the ones fighting it, then it’s practically guaranteed.\"","\"A Void Specter fighting the Void Hunter? That doesn’t make any sense at all.\"","\"The existence of a humanoid Void Specter already makes no sense.\"","\"If it really is the humanoid Void Specter... wouldn’t it be a catastrophe to have two monsters of such level exist at once? We still don’t know anything about it, either.\"","\"...\"","Nobody responded, afraid of the implications.","Time continued to pass, though for everyone except Yuan, each day seemed to crawl by painfully slowly.","As the battle dragged on, the energy radiating from Yuan’s clashes with the Void Hunter continued to grow. This was because Yuan constantly absorbed the Eternal Essence left behind by the Void Specters that were inadvertently annihilated by the shockwaves of their battle.","But alas, no matter how much Yuan’s Eternal Essence continued to grow, the Void Hunter only grew stronger alongside him, gradually revealing more and more of its seemingly bottomless reserves of power.","’Damn it... are we seriously going to keep this up until I’m finally \"worthy\"?’ Yuan sighed inwardly as he coughed up another mouthful of blood.","By now, his entire body was drenched in crimson, and he had lost so much blood over the course of the battle that it could have filled a large pond.","Despite his seemingly hopeless situation, Yuan refused to give up. He was prepared to fight the Void Hunter for as long as necessary—whether that meant eventually defeating it or earning its recognition, whichever came first.","Yet, after nearly an entire month of nonstop fighting, the Void Hunter suddenly came to a halt.","\"You are not worthy...\"","Its voice seemed to carry a faint trace of disappointment, though Yuan couldn’t tell whether that was real or merely his imagination.","Then, without explanation, the Void Hunter turned around and started walking away.","\"Come back, you—\"","Yuan shouted at it, but it completely ignored him and vanished without a trace like a ghost a split second later.","\"Son of a bitch... When was the last time I was toyed around like this?\" Yuan gritted his teeth in frustration.","He continued to linger in the area even long after the Void Hunter was gone.","\"Forget it. I’ll fight it again once I train some more.\"","He turned around and began traveling in the direction of Gaia’s Heaven, deciding that it was finally time to return to the city.","Although he could have remained in the Black Zone and continued training, he felt that his progress was too slow after facing the Void Hunter. At this point, it would be more efficient to return to the city and find a way to gain access to a level two Black Zone.","Of course, Yuan would have gone there immediately if he could. Unfortunately, he had no idea where one was located.","Once the nine cities were certain that the battle had ended, each dispatched only a single soldier to investigate.","They knew the other cities would likely do the same, and sending more than one person each would risk pushing the total number of investigators past ten and summoning the Void Hunter again.","On his way back to Gaia’s Heaven, Yuan suddenly sensed a familiar presence approaching from the opposite direction.","’This presence... the Ironwoman?’","Sure enough, it was indeed the Ironwoman. However, rather than stopping to speak with her, Yuan concealed his presence and quietly allowed her to pass by without noticing him.","’The direction she’s heading... she must be going to investigate my battle with the Void Hunter...’","Yuan easily guessed the purpose of her mission, which was precisely why he had chosen to avoid encountering her.","By the time Yuan returned to the city, the Ironwoman had just arrived at the scene, where some soldiers from the other cities had already gathered.","\"W-What the hell happened here...?\" the Ironwoman muttered, a dazed expression hidden beneath her mask as she surveyed the aftermath of the battle.","Thousands of massive craters stretched as far as the eye could see, some so deep that they resembled bottomless pits leading straight into hell.","The land in this world possessed a unique regenerative property, gradually repairing any damage until the terrain returned to its original state.","However, the destruction caused by this battle was so severe that even weeks after it had ended, the landscape remained utterly devastated.","Once the Ironwoman snapped out of her daze, she was startled by the powerful energies still lingering throughout the battlefield.","Although she had never fought the Void Hunter herself, she had experienced its presence firsthand before and immediately recognized its energy.","However, what truly shocked her was the second energy lingering alongside it, as she also found it familiar.","’This energy...’","The face of a certain arrogant and handsome man suddenly appeared in her mind.","’No, it can’t be him...’","She quickly dismissed the thought, finding it far too ridiculous to even entertain.","\"I figured they would’ve sent you out here, Ironwoman.\"","One of the soldiers there suddenly approached her and remarked.","The Ironwoman turned to face this soldier, who wore an azure-colored uniform, and responded, \"I am the most capable, after all.\"","\"Then you must have some information about what happened here... or more specifically, who was fighting the Void Hunter.\" The soldier said, staring at her with slightly narrowed eyes."]},{"number":2643,"title":"Chapter 2643: Returning to Military Base","paragraphs":["\"What makes you think I have such information? I literally just got here, you know?\"","\"I was just hoping you were capable enough to know something before coming here, that’s all.\"","\"Sorry to disappoint you, but I am not capable enough to know everything.\"","The soldier in the azure-colored suit shrugged, \"What a pity.\"","The two of them grouped up with the other soldiers shortly after.","\"Have you guys learned anything so far?\" asked the Ironwoman.","\"Not really,\" one of them responded, a soldier wearing a green uniform.","He then retrieved a glass vial that contained what appeared to be a chunk of dried blood and continued, \"Besides the craters, this blood was left behind. And there are a lot of them.\"","\"A little too much,\" said another soldier. \"It’s like thousands of people have been slaughtered here.\"","\"Blood?\" The Ironwoman muttered in a puzzled tone before inquiring, \"How could there be blood if the Void Hunter leaves no traces of its victims behind? A single touch from that entity will turn one into dust before they could even bleed a single drop of blood.\"","\"True, so the blood must’ve been the result of a fight between whoever was present when the Void Hunter was summoned. I am guessing that a large group of soldiers fought here for some reason and ended up dying to the Void Hunter.\"","\"But that doesn’t explain why the Void Hunter had fought for so long before disappearing,\" said another soldier.","\"And we would know about it if such a large-scale battle had really occurred.\"","\"Because the Void Hunter wasn’t fighting a human,\" a new voice suddenly resounded.","The Ironwoman and the others turned their heads to see a soldier in crimson uniform approaching them.","\"What do you know?\" the Ironwoman asked him.","The soldier from Ember City sighed and said, \"We were going to withhold this information until we had more, but considering the situation and implications, we have decided to share it, so listen carefully.\"","\"Not long ago, we discovered a new kind of Void Specter—one that has the ability to perfectly disguise itself as a human, and we believe it was the Void Hunter’s opponent.\"","\"What?!\"","Nearly everyone there exclaimed in shock at this revelation.","\"A Void Specter that can disguise itself as a human...?\" the Ironwoman mumbled.","\"A few of our soldiers discovered this Void Specter during their mission. They mistook him for a human lost in the Black Zone at first and approached him to help, but it became clear that the entity was not human when it killed two of them without warning.\"","\"That doesn’t really mean anything...\" said the soldier in the azure-colored uniform.","\"Let me continue,\" said the Ember City soldier.","\"After learning of its existence, we sent out a group of powerful soldiers to investigate. Nine soldiers in total.\"","\"Almost enough to summon the Void Hunter, huh?\"","\"Yes, and their life signals disconnected shortly after the Void Hunter’s appearance.\"","\"Even if those nine soldiers died here, that doesn’t explain the amount of blood present here.\"","\"The blood is likely from the humanoid Void Specter. If it has the ability to disguise itself as a human, we can assume it bleeds like one, too. And since it’s not a real human, it doesn’t know that humans don’t have an unlimited supply of blood.\"","\"That’s a whole lot of assumptions...\" the Ironwoman remarked. \"Nothing you’ve said can really be taken seriously without evidence.\"","The Ember City soldier turned to look at her and said, \"Then you’ll likely not believe me when I say that this humanoid Void Specter has taken the appearance of a soldier from your city.\"","\"What?\"","The Ironwoman frowned behind her mask.","\"You heard me. The humanoid Void Specter was wearing Gaia’s Heaven’s uniform, and according to the survivors, he was also a corporal.\"","\"...\"","A look of bewilderment appeared on the Ironwoman’s face after hearing this information.","\"A corporal... from my city?\" she muttered in a dazed voice as a certain face surfaced in her mind.","If the soldiers from Ember City had truly encountered a corporal wandering alone in the Black Zone, then there was only one person who fit that description—Corporal Yuan.","’Are they mistaking Corporal Yuan for a Void Specter...?’ she wondered inwardly.","Even with that possibility in mind, the Ironwoman decided not to say anything until she had more information. After all, there was still a chance that the mysterious corporal wasn’t Yuan at all.","\"Well, that’s all the information I have on the humanoid Void Specter for now, so do with it what you will,\" said the soldier from Ember City.","Shortly afterward, the soldiers resumed their investigation, collecting blood samples from various locations throughout the devastated area.","Meanwhile, Yuan arrived at the military gates.","When Yuan approached the gates, the soldier on duty stared at him with wide eyes, as if he were before a ghost.","\"C-Corporal Yuan...?\" the soldier, who recognized him, muttered in a dazed voice.","\"Yeah?\" Yuan casually responded, acting as if he hadn’t been presumed dead for more than half a year.","The soldier rubbed his eyes and looked at Yuan again.","\"I-I thought you were dead!\"","\"Well, as you can see, I am well and alive.\"","\"How is that possible?! The Scorpion Squad said you entered the Black Zone and died there!\"","\"I was in the Black Zone, but I didn’t die. I was lost, hence why it took me so long to return,\" Yuan said, giving a convenient excuse.","\"Anyway, let me in. I have to speak with General Mei.\"","\"R-Right away!\"","The soldier immediately opened the gates.","After entering the military base, Yuan made his way toward General Mei’s office, deliberately taking his time as he walked through the open areas, almost as though he wanted as many people as possible to notice his return.","\"Hey... am I seeing things, or is that Corporal Yuan?\"","\"Huh? What are you—Holy shit! It’s Corporal Yuan! He’s alive?!\"","\"What’s going on?! I thought he died a few months ago!\"","The soldiers exclaimed in disbelief when they saw Yuan casually walking through the base, staring at him as though they had just seen a ghost."]},{"number":2644,"title":"Chapter 2644: Yuan’s Testimony","paragraphs":["\"C-Corporal Yuan?! Is that really you?!\"","While most were frozen in a daze, one soldier suddenly called out to Yuan.","Yuan turned to that soldier and responded without stopping, \"Yes, it’s me.\"","\"How are you still alive?! I heard you entered the Black Zone alone!\"","\"I don’t want to explain the entire thing every time someone asks, so I’ll let the higher-ups explain it later,\" he said.","\"A-Alright...\"","News of Yuan’s return spread like wildfire in the military, reaching General Gu’s ears even before Yuan made it to General Mei’s office.","\"WHAT DID YOU JUST SAY?!\" General Gu stood from his chair after hearing the news and screamed at the top of his lungs.","\"C-Corporal Yuan is still alive, and he’d just returned to base!\"","\"That’s impossible! The Scorpion Squad has confirmed his death in the Black Zone!\"","\"The Scorpion Squad must have lied.\"","\"Where the hell are they?! Demand answers from them!\"","\"Yes, General.\"","Meanwhile, inside General Mei’s office, she also received news of Yuan’s return.","\"General! You won’t believe this, but Corporal Yuan—the one everyone thought had died a few months ago—has returned to the city alive!\"","\"Really? When did he return?\" Mei Feng asked in a surprised tone, though her reaction was far more subdued than the officer had expected.","\"About fifteen minutes ago, and from what I heard, he seems to be approaching the direction of your—\"","*Knock* *Knock*","The door was suddenly knocked on, followed by a familiar voice.","\"It’s me.\"","\"Speaking of the devil...\" Mei Feng muttered. \"I’ll speak to you later.\"","After disconnecting the call, Mei Feng answered Yuan, \"Enter.\"","The door opened, and Yuan calmly stepped into the office a moment later.","Mei Feng drew a sharp breath upon seeing his face. Although she already knew he was alive, there had always been a chance that something could happen to him while he continued training alone in the Black Zone. Now that he was standing before her in person, whatever lingering unease she still harbored vanished like smoke.","\"I’m back,\" Yuan spoke first, acting as if he’d only just gone out for a short adventure.","Mei Feng’s chest rose and fell heavily, as though she were preparing to unleash a torrent of anger. However, after taking another deep breath, she let out a long sigh instead.","\"Is that all you have to say?\" she asked.","\"Sorry for making you worried,\" Yuan immediately added.","Mei Feng rubbed her eyes for a moment before speaking again, \"Did you really spend the entire time in the Black Zone?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Well? What do you think of the Black Zone?\"","\"It wasn’t as dangerous as I thought,\" he replied without hesitation.","\"What exactly are you trying to achieve?\" she then questioned.","\"I already told you. I am training.\"","Mei Feng frowned at his response and quickly replied, \"If you’re going to lie, at least make it believable. Your cultivation hasn’t improved in the slightest since I last saw you.\"","\"I never said I was training my cultivation,\" Yuan said while shaking his head. \"I am training another power.\"","\"What—\"","\"Don’t bother asking. It’s not something you can comprehend, and it’s a power that only I can wield,\" Yuan quickly interrupted.","\"A little conceited, don’t you think?\"","\"No, not at all.\"","\"Is it related to your physique?\"","\"You can say that.\"","\"Then was it fruitful? Your training.\"","\"It went smoothly, but it’s not progressing as fast as I want. Therefore, I intend to visit level 2 Black Zone next.\"","\"Level 2 Black Zone...? Did the Ironwoman teach you that?\"","He nodded.","\"What are the requirements to go there?\" he then asked.","\"Ask me that once you qualify for the Black Zone—officially.\"","\"I’ll do that after this.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan asked, \"What happened to the Scorpion Squad?\"","\"I was wondering when you’d ask,\" Mei Feng replied. \"Since we didn’t have enough evidence to charge them with murder or conspiracy, the most we could do was hold them responsible for negligence. In other words, they essentially got away with it.\"","She paused briefly before continuing, \"However, now that you’re back, things are different. You can testify against them yourself.\"","\"That sounds fun, but I have a feeling that General Gu might get rid of them before we can serve real justice.\"","\"That would save us a lot of time and trouble,\" Mei Feng sneered.","\"...Not that I am saying it should happen,\" she added after a brief pause.","Yuan chuckled. \"So, when and where do I give my testimony?\"","\"We’ll do it right now,\" Mei Feng replied. \"There’s a chance General Gu might try something if we wait too long, so I want to get this over with as soon as possible.\"","\"Alright.\"","Mei Feng immediately contacted several officers and informed them of the situation.","Then, she brought Yuan to another location, where they waited for about half an hour before a group of officers finally arrived.","\"Wow... he’s really alive...\"","Even though they already knew Yuan was alive, it was still surprising to see him in person.","Of course, General Gu was among these officers.","’Those useless fucks!’ General Gu gritted his teeth and cursed the Scorpion Squad inwardly after confirming that Yuan was alive with his own eyes.","Although Mei Feng would have preferred to keep General Gu out of the proceedings for obvious reasons, this was an official testimony, and as a general, he had every right to be present.","In fact, the number of officers present for Yuan’s testimony was more than four times the number that had attended the Scorpion Squad’s interrogation a few months earlier.","\"I can’t wait to find out how he survived alone out there for so long.\"","While many were curious about what had truly happened between Yuan and the Scorpion Squad, they were even more curious about how a corporal who had only recently joined the military had managed to survive alone in the Black Zone for several months.","\"Are you ready to begin?\"","Some time later, the interviewer asked Yuan.","\"I am.\"","\"Then we will begin.\"","After starting a voice recorder, the interviewer spoke again, \"Please state your identity for us.\""]},{"number":2645,"title":"Chapter 2645: Yuan’s Testimony(2)","paragraphs":["\"Please state your identity for us.\"","\"Yuan. Corporal Yuan.\"","\"We’ll start from the very beginning of your encounter with the Scorpion Squad. Tell us when you first encountered them and how it happened.\"","\"I was waiting to accept a mission in the mission hall when they approached me. That was also the first time I’ve met them.\"","\"What did you talk about?\"","\"They said they had an offer for me that I wouldn’t be able to refuse and wished to speak with me in private.\"","\"Then what happened?\"","\"I went with them, and that’s when they said they wanted to verify the rumors of me being able to clear tunnels and defeat Void Guardians by myself, asking me if I wanted to go on a gathering mission with them.\"","\"Did they specify which danger zone they planned on going?\"","\"They did say that we’d be doing the mission in the Purple Zone.\"","\"And you agreed to it?\"","\"I did.\"","The interviewer paused for a bit before asking, \"Why did you agree to going to a place you don’t qualify to enter? Aren’t you aware of the risks?\"","A smile tugged at Yuan’s lips, and he glared at the interviewer in the eyes as he responded, \"I don’t qualify? Says who? Just because I didn’t have time to take some test doesn’t mean I am not qualified.\"","\"Also, the Scorpion Squad said I don’t need any permits to enter the Purple Zone if there were at least three captains with me. I was curious about the Purple Zone, so I went. It’s as simple as that.\"","\"...\"","The interviewer was stunned by Yuan’s arrogance, but he quickly snapped out of his daze and asked, \"Did you have any worries at that time?\"","\"No, I did not.\"","\"So what happened after you agreed to go on a mission with the Scorpion Squad?\"","\"We left the city immediately.\"","\"How did you leave?\"","\"Through the front entrance.\"","\"Did you have any interactions with the guards on duty on that day?\"","\"None at all. They let us leave without even speaking to us, which I found weird at the time but didn’t think much of since I thought officers were treated differently. After that, we left the city and went straight to the Purple Zone.\"","Everything Yuan said so far wasn’t new; it only confirmed what everyone already knew.","\"Tell us what happened outside the city.\"","\"Nothing eventful happened until we reached the Purple Zone, where the Scorpion Squad brought me to a tunnel they had discovered beforehand. We went inside, and I cleared the tunnel by myself.\"","\"Y-You cleared a tunnel in the Purple Zone by yourself...?\" The interviewer’s eyes widened at Yuan’s seemingly outrageous claim.","\"Is it really that surprising? I survived alone in the Black Zone for several months, you know?\" Yuan remarked.","\"Anyway, nothing particularly noteworthy happened while I was clearing the tunnel. It was only at the end—when I defeated the Void Guardian—that things started to get interesting, as that was when the Scorpion Squad admitted that their true reason for bringing me outside the city was to kill me.\"","The interviewer narrowed his eyes and inquired, \"Did they admit that to you of their own accord? Why would they expose themselves?\"","\"Because I revealed to them that I already know their intentions.\"","\"That doesn’t make sense. How would you know in the first place? We can assume that you followed them because you had no reason to suspect them.\"","\"Well, it’s not the first time my life has been targeted by the person behind them. And what can I say? Their killing intent was too obvious.\"","\"Who is this person you speak of?\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"Do I really need to spell it out for you? However, since I don’t have evidence, I won’t say anything more on this matter.\"","\"Then do you have any evidence that the Scorpion Squad admitted they intended to kill you?\"","\"No, I don’t,\" Yuan replied calmly.","Even before returning to the city, Yuan had already considered the possibility that his testimony might actually end up helping the Scorpion Squad rather than condemning them. After all, the opposing side could simply demand proof.","They had never possessed any evidence that the Scorpion Squad had killed him, and now that Yuan had returned alive, proving that they had intended to kill him would be even more difficult.","Meanwhile, the officers on Mei Feng’s side turned to look at her with worried expressions. None of them said anything, but the implications were obvious.","If things continued this way, not just the Scorpion Squad, but even General Gu could get away scot-free from this incident.","Mei Feng didn’t say anything and continued to watch in silence. As for General Gu, he had a hand over his mouth, hiding the wide smile behind it.","\"You can continue with your testimony,\" said the interviewer.","\"Is this really a testimony? It feels more like an interrogation,\" Yuan remarked with a cold smile.","\"You—\"","\"Not that I care.\" Yuan interrupted the interviewer and continued speaking, \"Anyway, after I confronted them and they revealed their intentions, I decided to run away.\"","\"Fortunately for me, my Void Control was superior, allowing me to barely escape them. However, I knew that I wouldn’t have enough energy to completely get away and return to the city safely, so I took a gamble and entered the Black Zone, hoping they wouldn’t chase after me.\"","\"And sure enough, they gave up chasing me shortly after I entered the Black Zone. But alas, I was not familiar with the Black Zone and quickly became lost after trying to avoid getting killed by the Void Specters there.\"","\"It was quite terrifying at first, but I eventually stopped running away and fought them, and to my surprise, they were easier to deal with than I expected, so I spent the next several months trying to find my way home and defeating every Void Specter in my path.\"","Yuan’s story left pretty much everyone present speechless."]},{"number":2646,"title":"Chapter 2646: Yuan’s Testimony(3)","paragraphs":["The room remained silent long after Yuan finished recounting his side of the story. The interrogator stared at him with wide eyes, disbelief clear across his face.","\"Since this is a testimony and not an interrogation, I should be done here, right?\" Yuan spoke after a moment of silence.","\"O-Of course...\" The interviewer nodded in a dazed manner.","Yuan left the room shortly after, but before he could go anywhere, Mei Feng came out of the spectators’ room and asked him, \"What are you going to do now? Don’t tell me you’re going to the mission hall.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"How did you know?\"","\"You can’t be seriously thinking about going on another mission right after everything that has happened!\" one of the officers behind Mei Feng exclaimed in disbelief.","\"Hm? Who said anything about accepting a mission?\" Yuan replied before elaborating, \"I am going to take the exam for the Black Zone—or the Purple Zone if I have to get the permit for that first.\"","\"Nobody would blame you for taking a rest, you know?\"","\"I know, but I am not the type who likes to sit around doing nothing all day.\"","Mei Feng sighed and said, \"Do as you please.\"","\"Thanks.\"","\"Before you go...\"","Just as Yuan started turning around, Mei Feng retrieved something from her pocket and tossed it to him.","\"This is... a storage cube?\" Yuan muttered after catching the item.","\"The Ironwoman asked me to give it to you wh—if you ever returned,\" Mei Feng said, almost revealing that she already knew Yuan was alive before his return.","Yuan didn’t say anything, merely offering a silent nod before leaving with the storage cube.","After leaving, Yuan made his way to the mission hall to see when the next exam was.","Unsurprisingly, his presence attracted the attention of everyone in the mission hall.","\"H-Hey... am I seeing things, or is that Corporal Yuan?\"","\"You haven’t heard yet? Apparently he managed to make it back alive.\"","\"No, I haven’t! When did he return?\"","\"Literally today.\"","\"That’s crazy... To survive outside the city for months alone? He’s really a different breed.\"","\"Not just outside the city. If the rumors are true, he went to the Black Zone.\"","It didn’t take long before someone approached Yuan and asked him directly, \"Can you tell us what happened out there?\"","Yuan replied with a smile, \"I just gave my testimony, so you will learn of it soon.\"","\"Can’t you just tell us now?\"","\"I was advised by General Mei not to say anything about it until then,\" he said, using Mei Feng as a scapegoat.","\"Oh...\"","Sure enough, when the soldier heard Mei Feng’s name, he immediately backed down.","And for the rest of Yuan’s time in the mission hall, nobody approached him again.","Once he was inside the machine, Yuan tried to join the next Black Zone exam.","However, as he’d anticipated, he needed to first pass the exam for the Purple Zone.","After signing up for the exam, Yuan headed directly to the training area. Of course, he wanted to see how much closer he’d gotten to defeating the entity on the 46th floor.","’I have about three and a half trillion years’ worth of Eternal Essence right now. Surely, I should be able to last more than a few minutes against it...’","<Your restriction on Eternal Essence has been temporarily lifted>","\"Foolish mortal...\"","A familiar voice resounded before the entity attacked, sending a massive wave of Eternal Essence at Yuan.","\"After fighting the Void Hunter, you don’t seem nearly as powerful as before,\" Yuan remarked with a faint smile.","He immediately unleashed his Eternal Essence—three trillion years’ worth—to meet the incoming attack head-on.","A moment later, their Eternal Essences collided. However, instead of Yuan’s being overwhelmed as it had been in the past, the two forces canceled each other out.","Seeing this, Yuan knew he had a good chance of defeating it.","After realizing its attack had failed, the entity immediately prepared another.","\"Using the same attack after the last one failed? Who’s the fool now?!\"","Yuan unleashed as much Eternal Essence as he could muster, condensing it into a massive spear before launching it forward.","The spear tore straight through the incoming wave with ease and continued onward, rapidly closing in on the entity.","However, just as the spear was about to reach its target, the entity suddenly vanished from its spot like a ghost.","’Void Manipulation!’","Yuan immediately shifted his focus toward locating the entity. Unfortunately, his mastery of Void Manipulation was still inferior, making it difficult for him to track its movements through the void.","A second later, a sharp pain suddenly pierced Yuan’s chest.","When he looked down, his eyes widened slightly at the sight of a massive hole torn straight through his chest.","<You have died>","After returning to the lobby, Yuan sat on the ground and sighed, \"My Eternal Essence has gotten strong enough to overcome that thing’s power, but I am still lacking in terms of Void Manipulation...\"","Thus, he decided to focus on training his Void Manipulation for the time being.","Yuan left the training room shortly after, but instead of returning home, he went to turn in the Unknown Ores in the storage cube that the Ironwoman had collected for him.","\"I’d like to turn this in.\"","Yuan placed the storage cube on the desk in front of the worker.","The worker accepted the storage cube and placed it on a machine that counted its contents.","\"T-Ten thousand Unknown Ores?!\" the worker muttered in a surprised voice after seeing the result.","\"By the way, is it possible to only accept merits?\" Yuan suddenly asked. \"I don’t need the money.\"","\"Yes, it’s possible. Would you like to turn in these Unknown Ores for merits only?\"","Yuan confirmed with a nod.","\"I understand.\"","After turning in his Unknown Ores, Yuan finally decided to return to his living quarters.","Some time later, just as Yuan reached the door to his home and was about to enter, a stunned voice suddenly sounded from behind him.","\"Y-Yuan?\"","Yuan turned around and saw Mei Xiaoyun standing several meters away, staring at him with a bewildered expression as though she had just seen a ghost."]},{"number":2647,"title":"Chapter 2647: Confirmation","paragraphs":["\"Y-Yuan?\" Mei Xiaoyun muttered with a dazed look on her face as she glared at the figure standing in front of Yuan’s living quarters.","She blinked a few times and even rubbed her eyes to make sure she wasn’t hallucinating.","A few more moments of silence passed, and Mei Xiaoyun still had trouble believing her eyes.","It wasn’t until Yuan spoke aloud that she confirmed he wasn’t an illusion but real.","\"Mei Xiaoyun? Oh, it’s been a whole year since the recruitment, hasn’t it? How was boot camp?\" Yuan steadily approached her with a calm smile on his handsome face, acting like everything was normal—as if he wasn’t supposed to be dead.","\"What’s with that look on your face? You look like you’re seeing a ghost,\" he remarked with a chuckle.","\"Am I not?\" she responded with a slight frown. \"You’re supposed to be dead, after all.\"","\"More like they assumed I was dead. As you can see for yourself, I am very much alive.\"","Mei Xiaoyun sighed. \"Give me a moment.\"","She then spent the next two minutes repeatedly rubbing her temples and letting out several deep sighs, as though trying to convince herself that Yuan was really standing before her.","\"When did you return?\" Mei Xiaoyun asked once she was done.","\"Today.\"","\"What happened?\"","Yuan explained the whole situation to her without hesitation.","\"I see... and what are your plans now?\"","\"I am going to get my permit for the Black Zone and then try to get one for level 2 Black Zone.\"","\"Unbelievable...\" Mei Xiaoyun muttered with wide eyes. \"I’ve just finished boot camp, and you’re already thinking about going into level 2 Black Zone? Did we really join at the same time?\"","\"The exam is scheduled in two weeks. You can come watch if you’d like.\"","\"I’ll think about it.\"","\"By the way, which division did you join?\" Yuan then asked.","\"The First Division.\"","\"The same as me, huh? Good to know. Anyway, I’m going to rest now. If you need anything, don’t hesitate to knock on my door.\"","Yuan entered his building the next moment, but Mei Xiaoyun lingered outside for some time, silently staring at his building.","’I can’t believe how much his death bothered me...’ she sighed inwardly, feeling a little puzzled by her own feelings.","After lingering for a few more moments, Mei Xiaoyun left.","Meanwhile, after returning home, the first thing Yuan did was train his Void Manipulation.","’There’s only one method of training that I can think of in this environment...’","After taking a deep breath, Yuan activated Void Manipulation, entering the void.","However, instead of coming out, he remained inside, training directly within the void. Although it was incredibly dangerous, it was also the most effective.","’T-This feeling! It’s much more painful than before!’","The pain was so much worse than when he last used this training method, forcing him to emerge from the void mere minutes later.","\"What is going on? I could stay in the void for days before, but I can’t last even ten minutes right now!\"","After resting for a bit, Yuan returned to the void. But instead of enduring the pain, he studied it.","’No wonder it hurts so much more!’ Yuan exclaimed inwardly as he quickly realized what was happening.","The pain he felt within the void pierced directly into his soul—a sensation he was all too familiar with, considering he had once shattered his own soul.","\"As I thought...\" Yuan muttered in a low voice after exiting the void again.","He lowered his head to look at his body.","\"This body... is an avatar, composed entirely of my soul.\"","Yuan had already figured this was the case when his storage rings did not transport to this world with him, but he wasn’t a hundred percent certain until this moment.","After all, if he were inhabiting an avatar created from his soul—similar to a player’s avatar in Cultivation Online—he should have been able to summon his Soul Weapons. Yet, that wasn’t the case here.","Once Yuan realized this, he sat down to ponder what to do with the information.","\"Even if I am in an avatar created from my own soul, it doesn’t change anything, as I still have no way out of this world.\"","In the end, his goal to find Gaia hadn’t changed in the slightest with this new information.","Thus, he resumed training his Void Manipulation.","Although practicing Void Manipulation with nothing but his soul was far more painful, his progress was also incomparably faster than when he trained it normally.","<Your Void Manipulation mastery has reached a new level>","By the time Yuan was scheduled to take the Purple Zone examination two weeks later, his mastery of Void Manipulation had already advanced by a full level.","When Yuan exited his living quarters, his gaze shifted to look at the four soldiers who had been waiting outside for over a week.","\"You know you could’ve knocked on the door if you wanted to speak with me,\" Yuan said.","\"I told you he was fine,\" said Shi Fa.","Sergeant Bing and Sergeant Quang approached Yuan together and stopped a few steps away.","Then, without hesitation, they both lowered their heads.","\"We’re sorry for failing to protect you properly.\"","\"There’s no need for either of you to apologize,\" Yuan said, shaking his head. \"Quite frankly, I never needed your protection in the first place. I only went along with it because it gave General Mei some peace of mind.\"","\"As arrogant as ever, huh?\" Wu Wang remarked with a smile.","\"Where are you heading to now?\"","\"I’m going to take the exam for the Purple Zone.\"","\"Do you plan on taking the one for the Black Zone?\"","\"Of course. Right after I pass this one.\"","\"Then I won’t bother watching this one since you’ll obviously ace it,\" said Wu Wang.","\"I’ll go,\" said Sergeant Bing.","\"Me too,\" said Sergeant Quang.","\"I got nothing else to do, anyway,\" Shi Fa shrugged.","Thus, Yuan made his way to the examination site, which was being held at the same location as his previous examination.","At the same time, the Ironwoman returned to the military base to report the details of her investigation to Mei Feng."]},{"number":2648,"title":"Chapter 2648: Ironwoman’s Report","paragraphs":["\"W-What did you just say?\" Mei Feng muttered, staring at the Ironwoman with a dumbfounded expression after hearing the results of her investigation, looking as though she had just been told a horrifying story.","The Ironwoman cleared her throat before repeating, \"Apparently, the Ember City has discovered a new Void Specter—one that rivals the Void Hunter in prowess. They also believe that Void Specter was the one fighting the Void Hunter for weeks.\"","\"A Void Specter fighting with the Void Hunter...? That sounds ridiculous,\" remarked Mei Feng.","\"I haven’t even told you the best part. According to Ember City, this Void Specter can perfectly disguise itself as a human.\"","\"What sort of nonsense is that?!\"","\"Moreover...\"","\"There’s more?\"","\"This humanoid Void Specter currently has the appearance of a soldier from our city.\"","Mei Feng frowned upon hearing this. \"A soldier from our city?\"","The implications of a new Void Specter with prowess on par with the Void Hunter were already troubling enough, but the fact that it supposedly bore the appearance of a soldier from Gaia’s Heaven made the situation even worse. Once word spreads, it could easily lead to unnecessary suspicion and discrimination against their soldiers.","\"What do you think?\" Mei Feng asked the Ironwoman a moment later. \"Is this information from Ember City trustworthy, or are they using this opportunity to damage our reputation? We’ve been at odds with each other for generations, after all.\"","\"Personally, I think it’s a misunderstanding.\"","\"What makes you think that?\"","\"Because they said this Void Specter took the appearance of a corporal.\"","\"A corporal?\" Mei Feng raised an eyebrow, looking puzzled.","\"Think about it. A lone soldier with the rank of corporal in the Black Zone...\"","\"Corporal Yuan?!\" Mei Feng exclaimed in disbelief after realizing this.","The Ironwoman nodded.","\"Of course, it could just be a coincidence. We’ll know for sure once we speak with him,\" she said.","After a brief pause, she added, \"Speaking of him, any news on his return?\"","Mei Feng sat back in her chair and sighed, \"He returned to the city two weeks ago.\"","\"Oh? What happened?\"","\"He gave his testimony and hasn’t left his living quarters since then. I’ll let you hear the recording of it later.\"","\"And the Scorpion Squad?\"","\"We were going to interrogate them again with the new information from Corporal Yuan’s testimony, but...\" Mei Feng paused to rub her temples before continuing, \"We could not find them. They’ve completely vanished into thin air.\"","The Ironwoman raised an eyebrow at this news.","\"That’s a funny way to say General Gu got rid of them.\"","\"Even if that’s the case, we have no evidence. And quite frankly, I hope that’s what happened since it saves us the trouble.\"","\"With the Scorpion Squad gone, wouldn’t it be harder to make General Gu pay for his crimes?\"","\"It’s not like he won’t have other ways to weasel his way out of trouble. Unless we catch him in the act with irrefutable evidence, there’s nothing we can do to him,\" Mei Feng sighed.","\"Well, what are we going to do now? You think he’ll continue targeting Corporal Yuan?\"","\"I don’t know, but we’ll make it harder for him to target him.\"","\"How?\"","\"I’m going to promote him. I checked his records last week, and he has more than enough to be promoted to Sergeant. However, he’ll need to pass the examination for the Purple Zone before he fully qualifies.\"","\"When’s the next examination?\"","\"Today. In fact, he should be—\"","Mei Feng abruptly stopped speaking when she received a call.","\"What is it?\"","\"T-This is about Corporal Yuan!\" A frantic voice responded.","\"Did something happen to him?\" Mei Feng frowned.","\"Yes! He just finished the examination for the Purple Zone, and you won’t believe the results! A perfect score! He completely aced it!\"","\"That’s hardly surprisingly for someone like—\"","\"That’s not all!\" the voice interrupted Mei Feng before continuing, \"He asked to take the examination for the Black Zone since he was already there, and the examiners agreed. In the end, he passed with perfect results, too! This is the first time anyone has aced the Black Zone exam!\"","Mei Feng became speechless.","After a moment of silence, Mei Feng asked, \"Are you at the examination right now?\"","\"Yes, I am.\"","\"Is Corporal Yuan still there?\"","\"He left just a few seconds ago.\"","\"Go catch him and tell him to come to my office immediately.\"","\"Right away.\"","Time passed swiftly, and half an hour later, Yuan showed up at Mei Feng’s office.","\"You called?\" Yuan said aloud as he walked into the room.","\"Hm? You’re here, too?\" he looked at the Ironwoman with a raised eyebrow.","\"...\"","Neither Mei Feng nor the Ironwoman spoke, merely gazing at him in silence.","\"What is it?\" Yuan asked again.","\"First and foremost, congratulations on passing your exams with perfect scores,\" Mei Feng said a moment later.","\"Second, I have a few questions for you regarding your time in the Black Zone.\"","\"What sort of questions?\"","\"Have you encountered soldiers from the Ember City?\"","\"Ember City? Never heard of them.\"","\"They wear a red uniform,\" the Ironwoman said, giving details of their uniform to him.","\"Oh, them? In that case, yes, I have,\" Yuan calmly admitted.","He wasn’t sure how they found out, but he had no reason to hide it.","\"Is that so...\" Mei Feng mumbled, leaning her head back as she rubbed her temples with a weary expression.","\"Is this about me killing two of their soldiers?\" Yuan asked. \"In that case, it was self-defense.\"","\"This is way beyond that,\" said the Ironwoman, shaking her head.","\"For some reason, they seem to think you’re a Void Specter.\"","\"Huh?\" Yuan’s eyes widened slightly at the unexpected accusation.","He had considered many possibilities regarding the situation, but being mistaken for a Void Specter was certainly not one of them.","Then he had a sudden realization.","’It was probably because of my affinity...’ he sighed inwardly.","\"Well? Are you actually human, or are you a Void Specter disguised as one?\" the Ironwoman asked a moment later, a hint of amusement in her voice."]},{"number":2649,"title":"Chapter 2649: Promotion","paragraphs":["Yuan smiled at the Ironwoman’s question and responded with a question of his own, \"What do you think?\"","The Ironwoman narrowed her eyes at him and replied, \"I don’t think you’re human, but I doubt you’re a Void Specter, either.\"","Yuan chuckled at her response before turning to Mei Feng and asking her, \"What about you?\"","\"Something that doesn’t belong in this world,\" she calmly responded.","The Ironwoman was slightly surprised by Mei Feng’s response.","\"Anyway, I have an idea why they think I am a Void Specter. It’s just a misunderstanding,\" Yuan said a moment later. \"Are they making a big deal out of this or something?\"","\"No... not yet.\" Mei Feng shook her head. \"But it will become an issue once news spreads in the other cities—if it hasn’t already.\"","\"Can’t you just tell them it was a misunderstanding?\" Yuan asked.","\"Of course I can. The real question is whether they’ll believe us,\" Mei Feng replied.","After a brief pause, she continued, \"That being said, the existence of a humanoid Void Specter is simply too outrageous. Without concrete evidence, I doubt most people will accept that such an entity exists. In fact, they’ll probably find it much easier to believe the whole thing was a misunderstanding than to accept that a humanoid Void Specter is real.\"","\"So what you’re saying is... to just ignore it?\" Yuan asked.","\"For now, yes.\"","\"...\"","The room quickly fell silent afterward.","\"Is that all?\" Yuan asked a moment later.","\"No, we’re about to go into the main topic,\" Mei Feng responded before her expression turned dead serious.","\"You... Did you fight the Void Hunter before coming back to the city?\" Mei Feng asked with narrowed eyes.","\"I did.\"","Yuan answered immediately and without the slightest hesitation, catching them off guard. They hadn’t expected him to admit it so readily.","\"What’s with the surprised look?\" Yuan remarked after seeing their faces.","\"Well... I was expecting you to keep it a secret...\"","\"Why?\" Yuan calmly replied. \"It wouldn’t benefit me to keep it a secret.\"","In his eyes, the more people who knew about his achievement, the better his reputation would be, which would allow him to progress faster in this world.","However, Mei Feng thought differently.","\"Are you thinking that letting the world know you fought—and survived—the Void Hunter would help with your recognition?\"","Yuan quietly nodded.","\"While I will admit that you will definitely become the most famous individual in the world, it’s not necessarily a good thing.\"","The Ironwoman then said, \"Throughout history, only two people have ever fought the Void Hunter and survived. The first was Tian Yuchen, and now, you’re the second.\"","\"Tian Yuchen was already a renowned figure before his battle with the Void Hunter, but surviving that encounter propelled his reputation to the very peak of the world. And because he was affiliated with our city, the other eight cities immediately became wary of us and began working together to suppress Gaia’s Heaven, fearing that we had grown too powerful.\"","\"In order to prevent a war from breaking out, Tian Yuchen ultimately had no choice but to sever his ties with our city and become an independent figure, unaffiliated with any city, power, or individual.\"","\"You, on the other hand, are practically unknown outside our military. If word gets out that we have someone capable of fighting the Void Hunter and surviving, the other cities will undoubtedly see us as a threat.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow at such words and spoke, \"Isn’t this world supposed to be working together to deal with the threat prophesied by Gaia?\"","\"If only things were that simple...\" Mei Feng sighed. \"Unfortunately, not every city believes in Gaia’s prophecy. Some even outright reject it, such as Ember City.\"","\"And while we’re on the topic, the next drill is scheduled to happen in two months.\"","\"You mean the one where the civilians must go underground?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"About time,\" Yuan said. \"Anything I should know before that happens?\"","\"No, you’ll be briefed a week before it happens.\"","\"Alright.\"","\"In any case, the fact that you fought and survived the Void Hunter will not leave this room, understand?\" Mei Feng said a moment later.","\"I do.\"","\"What do you think? About the Void Hunter,\" the Ironwoman suddenly inquired.","\"It’s immensely powerful. So much so that I couldn’t do anything to it,\" he admitted.","\"Huh? But didn’t you fight with it for weeks?\"","\"I did, but it was toying with me, and it left once it was satisfied. What? Did you think I was secretly as powerful as the Void Hunter? You’re giving me too much credit.\"","\"...\"","The Ironwoman and Mei Feng fell silent with dumbfounded looks on their faces, but it wasn’t that they realized Yuan wasn’t as powerful as they expected.","\"The Void Hunter... toyed with you and left you alive? I have never heard of such a thing before! When the Void Hunter appears, it always tries to kill everyone who summoned it without exception!\" said the Ironwoman.","Mei Feng added, \"The only time it failed was when Tian Yuchen held it back long enough for everyone to escape safely.\"","\"What about all that blood?\" the Ironwoman then asked. \"There was so much of it that the place looked like the aftermath of a bloody battle between two massive armies!\"","\"Oh, that’s my blood.\"","\"There’s no way!\"","\"It’s a unique trait of my physique.\"","\"And what kind of physique is that?\" The Ironwoman narrowed her eyes at him.","\"You don’t have to answer that,\" Mei Feng suddenly said, dumbfounded the Ironwoman.","\"Huh?\"","The Ironwoman stared at Mei Feng with a suspicious gaze, falling silent.","\"One more thing before I send you away,\" Mei Feng said, pretending the previous interaction didn’t happen.","She reached into her drawer and retrieved an insignia, then handed it to Yuan.","\"Congratulations on your promotion. You’re now a Sergeant.\"","\"Oh?\" Yuan gladly accepted his new rank.","\"Usually, there would be a ceremony for a promotion of your rank, but alas, I don’t want you to draw any unnecessary attention.\"","\"That’s fine,\" Yuan said. \"In fact, I’d rather not have one if I could choose.\""]},{"number":2650,"title":"Chapter 2650: Creating His Own Squad","paragraphs":["\"That’s all I have for you for now,\" Mei Feng said to Yuan shortly after giving him his new insignia.","Once Yuan left the room, the Ironwoman turned to stare at Mei Feng in silence.","\"I’m not going to tell you, so don’t bother asking,\" Mei Feng said after a moment of silence, almost as though she could read the Ironwoman’s thoughts.","\"You don’t need to,\" the Ironwoman replied. \"I’ve already seen his status—his physique, the Inexhaustible Heavenly Refinement.\"","She paused briefly before continuing, \"However, the fact that you don’t want him answering my question suggests there’s more to it than that. If I had to guess, you altered the information displayed on his status.\"","\"...\" Mei Feng remained silent, refusing to confirm or deny it.","\"Do you not trust me?\" the Ironwoman suddenly asked.","\"This is not a trust issue,\" Mei Feng swiftly responded. \"The fewer people know, the better. Just like how I keep my mouth shut about your background, regardless of who asks.\"","The Ironwoman smiled at her response before replying, \"Fair enough.\"","She turned around and walked to the door, stopping once her hand reached the handle.","\"By the way, regarding that thing we talked about before.\"","\"What thing?\"","\"About having him join my squad.\"","\"Have you decided to let him join, after all?\"","\"No, it’s the opposite,\" said the Ironwoman as she shook her head.","\"Huh?\" Mei Feng uttered in a puzzled voice.","The Ironwoman removed her mask to show Mei Feng a stiff smile.","\"He’s too much for my squad. I think it’d be much better if he made one to lead himself.\"","\"I see...\" Mei Feng mumbled, understanding the Ironwoman’s reasoning and finding herself in agreement.","\"And since he’s a Sergeant now, he can form his own squad.\"","\"I have a feeling he’ll definitely go that route once he realizes the benefits...\" Mei Feng said with a nervous smile.","Meanwhile, Yuan made his way back to his living quarters after leaving Mei Feng’s office.","\"Huh? Your rank... you’ve been promoted?\" Sergeant Quang, who waited for him outside, remarked with a surprised face after seeing his new insignia.","\"Yes, it was a sudden promotion, but I’m not complaining.\"","\"How long has it been since you joined the military? A year?\"","\"Just about.\"","\"And to think it took me fifteen years to reach this rank...\" Sergeant Quang sighed aloud.","\"What are the benefits of becoming a sergeant?\" Yuan then asked. \"Even as a corporal, I already had access to missions that were normally restricted to sergeants, so I don’t really see what’s changed.\"","\"Well... as a sergeant, you can create a squad of your own.\"","\"Hm?\" Yuan stopped walking and turned to look at him with one eyebrow raised.","\"My own... squad?\"","Yuan immediately realized the benefit of having his own squad. With a team of trusted soldiers under his command, he would always have people ready to accompany him on missions outside the city whenever he wanted.","Of course, he’d still rather go out on his own since that was the most convenient for him, but that wasn’t possible right now.","\"How many members do I need to have a squad of my own?\" Yuan then asked.","\"Well, you can create your squad at any time, but you won’t be officially recognized as one until you have at least four members, so you’ll need three other people.\"","\"For the members, is there a rank requirement?\"","\"No, anyone who finishes boot camp can join a squad.\"","\"I see. Then are you already in a squad? Want to join mine?\"","\"Unfortunately, I am already in a squad. In fact, you were with us during your first mission,\" said Sergeant Quang, referring to Sergeant Bing, Wu Wang, and Shi Fa.","\"Is that so? Well, if you ever feel like changing squads, you can find me. Let the others know, too.\"","\"Alright.\"","Once Yuan reached his living quarters, he said to Sergeant Quang, \"By the way, there’s no need for you to guard me any longer. Tell Sergeant Bing this, too.\"","\"Huh? But General Mei didn’t—\"","\"Because this is my decision. Don’t worry, she won’t make things difficult for you.\"","\"Alright...\"","After Yuan entered his living quarters, Sergeant Quang contacted General Mei to tell her the situation.","\"Corp—Sergeant Yuan said he no longer needs us to guard him. What should we do?\"","\"Do as he says. In fact, I was going to relieve you of your guard duties even if he didn’t ask.\"","\"I understand.\"","Sergeant Quang notified Sergeant Bing of the situation afterward.","Time passed swiftly, and in the blink of an eye, another month went by.","During this time, Yuan spent all of his time inside his room training his Void Manipulation.","’I was only able to stay inside the void for a few seconds at first, but after nearly two months of training, I can stay in the void for three days at a time.’","Even though he was still a far cry from his peak, his rate of progress had improved tremendously compared to before.","With a month left before the drill, Yuan decided to challenge the entity on the 46th floor again.","On his way to the training hall, Yuan encountered Mei Xiaoyun, who appeared to be coming out of the building.","\"Are you on your way to train?\" Mei Xiaoyun asked him.","\"Yes.\"","\"Have fun.\"","Mei Xiaoyun said before continuing to walk away, but she was quickly stopped.","\"Wait a second.\"","Once she stopped, Yuan asked, \"Are you in a squad right now?\"","\"No, but I have had hundreds of requests,\" she revealed.","\"Hundreds of requests...?\" Yuan muttered with a somewhat dumbfounded expression.","Now that he thought about it, Yuan realized that he hadn’t received a single invitation to join a squad since entering the military despite all of his achievements.","Considering his talent and reputation, it wouldn’t have been strange for squads to constantly try recruiting him. Yet, for some reason, not a single one had approached him.","Despite the oddity, Yuan decided not to ponder too much about it and asked Mei Xiaoyun, \"Anyway, I plan on creating my own squad and was wondering if you’d like to join it.\""]},{"number":2651,"title":"Chapter 2651: Clearing the 46th Floor","paragraphs":["\"You want me to join your squad...?\" Mei Xiaoyun muttered in a somewhat dazed voice.","\"Is it really that surprising?\" Yuan smiled at her reaction. \"In this entire world, I trust you and your mother the most, after all.\"","\"With that being said... since you’ve refused hundreds of invites, you’re probably not ready to join any squad yet.\"","\"Then why did you even ask?\" Mei Xiaoyun frowned slightly.","\"I wanted to let you know that option was on the table,\" Yuan replied.","\"Anyways, I’ll see you later.\"","Yuan turned around and continued walking.","However, after taking just a few steps, Mei Xiaoyun’s voice resounded from behind, \"I’ll join your squad.\"","Yuan’s movements froze at her words.","He turned around with a smile and asked, \"Can I ask why?\"","\"I just feel like it,\" she said with a casual shrug, seemingly unwilling to answer.","\"Good enough,\" Yuan said, not going to question further.","\"What’s the name of our squad? And how many members do we have?\"","\"Right now, you’re the only member besides me. As for the name... I haven’t thought of one yet.\"","\"So... you haven’t even created the squad yet?\"","\"Nope.\"","\"...\"","Mei Xiaoyun was speechless.","\"I’ll let you know once I create it. See ya.\"","Yuan disappeared into the training hall the next moment.","\"Why did I join...?\" Mei Xiaoyun mumbled in a low voice, looking like she was puzzled by her own decision.","\"Forget it. It’s not like I have plans to join another squad.\"","Mei Xiaoyun shook her head and returned to her living quarters shortly after.","Meanwhile, Yuan entered Simulated Combat and began his fight against the entity on the 46th floor.","Just like before, Yuan’s Eternal Essence was just enough to overwhelm the entity’s.","\"I can see it! I can see its movements properly now!\" Yuan clenched his fists in excitement when the entity escaped into the void.","\"Not this time, you bastard!\"","Now that Yuan could follow the entity’s movements through the void, he was finally able to react in time and block its attacks.","After having its attack stopped, the entity immediately tried to retreat back into the void. Unfortunately for it, Yuan could do more than merely track its movements now, as he could also strike it while it was still inside the void.","An immense amount of Eternal Essence surged through Yuan’s arm as he swung it through the air like a blade.","The next moment, the entity was violently forced out of the void after being struck by his attack, screaming in pain.","\"Hahaha! That’s more like it!\"","Although the attack wasn’t powerful enough to defeat the entity in a single strike, Yuan actually preferred it that way. After being killed by it hundreds of times, he had accumulated plenty of frustration, and now he finally had the opportunity to vent it.","After several minutes and hundreds of exchanges, Yuan finally defeated the entity, clearing the 46th floor.","However, a single victory wasn’t enough to satisfy him, and he immediately challenged the 46th floor again, defeating the entity over and over—hundreds of times—until he had finally vented all of his pent-up frustration.","\"Now I just need to clear it at Gaia’s Sanctum,\" Yuan mumbled to himself as he left the training hall.","Although Simulated Combat functioned identically to Endless Assault, the two were completely separate systems. As a result, clearing the 46th floor here had no effect on his progress in Gaia’s Sanctum.","In other words, Yuan would still need to defeat the 46th floor in Gaia’s Sanctum before he could advance to the 47th floor and beyond.","As much as he wanted to visit Gaia’s Sanctum immediately, there were only two weeks left before the drill, so he decided to wait until afterward.","Shortly after Yuan left, a commotion broke out in the training hall when the soldiers noticed something different.","\"S-Someone just cleared the 46th floor for Simulated Combat!\"","\"What?! Who?! Who was it?!\"","Soldiers swiftly gathered at the ranking board.","[Simulated Combat Rankings]","[1. ???: 46th floor(21seconds)]","[2. ???: 45th floor(84 hours, 42 minutes, 11 seconds)]","\"A hidden name? What a pity.\"","\"A-Am I seeing things, or does that say 21 seconds?\"","\"It definitely says 21 seconds, but there’s no way anyone could clear the 46th floor in such a short time, especially when the second rank took several days to clear the 45th floor...\"","\"So you’re saying that it’s a bug? But the system has never bugged out before.\"","\"When did the ranking change?\"","\"I noticed it a few minutes ago, and it wasn’t there half an hour ago.\"","\"Then that person must still be inside, right? Let’s wait and see who comes out.\"","Thus, the soldiers began waiting for someone who had already left.","Since the rankings don’t update until the participant exits the waiting room, Yuan’s name did not appear after his first clear, as he had remained inside to challenge the same stage repeatedly.","\"By the way, who’s in second place? Their name is also hidden.\"","\"This is just a rumor, but I heard it’s the Supreme General—the current one.\"","\"Speaking of the Supreme General, he’s retiring soon, right?\"","\"That’s what I heard, too.\"","\"There’s a reason the two Generals are going at each other’s necks right now.\"","It didn’t take long for news of the updated ranking to spread throughout the military, with countless soldiers speculating about the identity of this mysterious individual. Of course, nobody guessed it correctly.","\"It can’t be him, right...?\" Mei Feng muttered to herself after hearing this news.","Even with Yuan’s recent achievement, for him to clear the 46th floor in 21 seconds was too far-fetched for her to believe.","Meanwhile, after leaving the training hall, Yuan made his way to create his own squad.","\"Hello, is this where I create a squad?\"","\"Yes. Do you already have four members?\"","\"No, not yet.\"","\"Then for now, you can only register the squad’s name. To officially establish the squad, you’ll need at least four members in total. Have you decided on a name yet?\"","Yuan nodded and said with a smile, \"My squad will be named Nine Heavens.\""]},{"number":2652,"title":"Chapter 2652: Squad Name","paragraphs":["\"Nine Heavens, correct? I have registered it in the system, Sergeant Yuan. Once you acquire three other members, you’ll officially be recognized as a squad.\"","\"Do I have to bring them here with me?\" Yuan then asked.","\"No, they just need to join the squad. Although it’s not an official squad, soldiers can still apply to join it.\"","\"I understand.\"","Yuan left the place shortly after and went to notify Mei Xiaoyun that he’d created the squad.","\"The name of the squad is Nine Heavens.\"","Mei Xiaoyun raised an eyebrow at the name and inquired, \"Is there a specific reason why there are nine heavens? Do you intend to have nine members?\"","\"No, it’s just the name of my world,\" he said with a smile.","\"Now that you mention it...\" Mei Xiaoyun recalled hearing such a name before. \"Anyways, I’ll put in my request whenever I have time, unless you really need me to do it right now.\"","\"You can take your time, since I still need to find two other members,\" he said. \"Speaking of time... what do you usually do these days?\"","\"Training. Although I can already use Void Control, I want to improve my mastery and confidence before doing missions outside the city.\"","\"I’d love to help you, but Void Control isn’t something that can really be taught—\" Yuan suddenly paused, a pondering expression appearing on his face.","\"Hey, you wanna try something? It could help speed up your training.\"","Mei Xiaoyun looked at him with a suspicious gaze.","\"What is it?\"","\"It’s hard to explain, so just follow me.\"","Yuan proceeded to lead Mei Xiaoyun to his living quarters.","\"Are we going to train here...? At your home?\"","Yuan nodded, \"It’s not something I want people to see, after all.\"","The suspicious look on Mei Xiaoyung’s face became even more evident, but she didn’t say anything and entered his home shortly after.","Once inside, Yuan extended his hand and said, \"I am going to bring you into the void with me. See if being surrounded by the void helps with your training.\"","\"Huh? What do you mean—\"","Before Mei Xiaoyun could even finish her sentence, Yuan grabbed her hand and used Void Manipulation, dragging her into the void with him.","Once they were inside the void, Yuan manipulated the void around both of them, keeping Mei Xiaoyun safe. However, doing this consumed Yuan’s stamina at several times the rate it normally would.","\"T-This is...?!\" Mei Xiaoyun stared into the pitch-black void with widened eyes and a dazed expression.","Although this wasn’t her first time entering the void, as she could also use Void Manipulation, she had never remained inside for more than a split second—unlike Yuan, who seemed perfectly capable of lingering there.","However, it wasn’t that Mei Xiaoyun was incapable of remaining inside the void. Rather, when she had been taught Void Manipulation during boot camp, there was one warning the instructors had repeatedly drilled into everyone’s minds.","\"Go in and get out. Never linger in the void, or it could destroy both your body and soul.\"","That warning had been emphasized so often that it had practically become instinct.","Mei Xiaoyun turned to look at Yuan, who looked unfathomably tranquil.","\"Don’t look at me,\" Yuan suddenly said to her. \"You won’t learn anything by staring at my face. Look at the void and study it.\"","Mei Xiaoyun nodded in a dazed manner before focusing on the void. But because her situation was so bizarre, she had a hard time focusing.","A few short minutes later, Yuan brought Mei Xiaoyun out of the void.","\"Well? What do you think?\" he asked her in a somewhat exhausted voice.","\"...\"","Mei Xiaoyun did not respond, merely staring at him in silence.","Yuan didn’t rush her and patiently waited.","After a long moment of silence, Mei Xiaoyun rubbed her eyes and sighed aloud, \"I can’t believe you just dragged me into the void with you. Do you have any idea how dangerous that is?\"","\"Don’t worry, it’s not my first time taking people with me into the void. Your safety is guaranteed.\"","\"That’s not the point! You should’ve warned me first!\"","\"It’s much quicker to show you.\"","Mei Xiaoyun released another sigh before speaking, \"I... didn’t really get to study the void too much because I wasn’t mentally prepared for it.\"","\"No worries. We’ll do it as many times as you need. This is great training for me, too.\"","\"I’ve heard about your unfathomably perfect Void Control and how abnormally fast your progress has been. Is this the secret behind it?\" she asked.","She paused for a moment before adding, \"Are you sure you want to share something like this with me? What if I share it with others?\"","\"I don’t mind.\" Yuan casually shrugged. \"Besides, I doubt anyone other than me could use this training method efficiently, given how dangerous it is.\"","The main reason Yuan’s understanding of Void Manipulation improved so drastically was that he didn’t protect his body while training, instead allowing the void to ravage him freely.","Such a training method would normally be impossible, as it required regenerative abilities powerful enough to constantly repair the damage inflicted on both his body.","\"The Perfected Heavenly Refinement physique sure is convenient,\" she sighed.","\"Give me a moment to mentally prepare myself before we try again.\"","Yuan nodded and said, \"I will need some time to recover every time we do it, too.\"","Some time later, Yuan brought Mei Xiaoyun into the void once again.","This time, having mentally prepared herself beforehand, Mei Xiaoyun quickly entered a training mindset and began studying the void with intense concentration.","A few minutes later, they left the void.","\"It’s still too early to say how effective this method will be in the long run, but I can definitely feel my understanding of Void Control improving much faster than when I train normally,\" Mei Xiaoyun revealed afterward.","\"That’s good to hear. Want to continue training?\" Yuan then asked.","She nodded.","\"At least until the briefing in a few days.\"","Thus, they continued training in this manner for the next several days."]},{"number":2653,"title":"Chapter 2653: A Quick Briefing","paragraphs":["*Knock* *Knock*","Someone knocked on Yuan’s door as he rested from his training.","\"I’ll get it.\" Mei Xiaoyun said, not thinking too much about her actions before going to answer the door.","\"Hey, Sergeant Yu—?!\"","The voice abruptly halted when they noticed Yuan wasn’t the one who answered the door.","\"Y-You are... Private First Class Mei?! What are you doing inside Sergeant Yuan’s living quarters?\" Sergeant Bing asked with a bewildered expression.","Even as she voiced the question, however, a single conclusion had already taken root in her mind.","\"We’re training,\" Mei Xiaoyun said.","\"Training... What sort of training can one even do in such an environment? If you’re sparring, there are much better places...\" Sergeant Bing continued to ask.","\"Sorry, but it’s not something I can reveal,\" Mei Xiaoyun shook her head.","\"I-Is that so...\" Sergeant Bing muttered in a dazed voice.","\"You looking for me?\"","A moment later, Yuan appeared at the door.","\"Y-Yes...\" Sergeant Bing snapped out of her daze and quickly explained the reason for her visit. \"General Mei sent me to inform you that the briefing for the upcoming drill will take place tomorrow at ten in the morning. It’ll take place at the Parade Deck, so make sure you don’t miss it.\"","\"I understand. Thanks for letting me know,\" said Yuan. \"By the way, now that we’re at the same rank, you can just call me by my name. Let the others know, too.\"","\"Sure. You can call me by my name, too. I’m Bing Bing.\"","After Sergeant Bing left, Mei Xiaoyun said, \"I’ll also take my leave then. Thank you for the training.\"","\"You can come back whenever you want to continue.\"","\"I will.\"","The following day, Yuan, Mei Xiaoyun, Sergeant Bing, and Sergeant Quang made their way to the Parade Deck for their briefing.","By the time they arrived, nearly half of the military was already present.","\"How many soldiers do we have, anyway?\" Yuan suddenly asked.","\"Approximately 70,000 soldiers.\"","\"That’s... a lot less than I expected.\"","\"Well, it’s not exactly easy to join the military.\"","About ten minutes later, the rest of the soldiers appeared.","At this moment, practically all 70,000 soldiers were present, with a few exceptions.","General Mei and General Gu were also present, both standing on an elevated platform.","Eventually, General Gu began speaking. \"I know it hasn’t been long since our last drill, but with Gaia’s prophecy looming over us, we’ve decided to increase the frequency of these drills.\"","\"Since we have new soldiers with us, we’ll explain the purpose of the drill and the exercise to them.\"","Mei Feng then spoke, \"The purpose of these drills is simple—to prepare us for what lies in the near future. Gaia, the protector of this world and Messenger of the Universe, received a prophecy from the universe itself. According to that prophecy, this world and every living being within it will one day face an unfathomable ordeal—a tribulation unlike anything we have ever experienced.\"","The soldiers who were already aware of the prophecy showed little reaction, aside from the firm determination visible on their faces.","However, those who had only recently joined the military and were hearing about it for the first time reacted with shock and disbelief, as though the peaceful future they had taken for granted had suddenly been ripped away.","\"I won’t go too deeply into the details of the prophecy, but there exist beings in this universe whose power is beyond anything we can currently comprehend. They dwell beyond the skies above us, and according to Gaia’s prophecy, there will come a day when they descend upon this world with the intent to destroy mankind.\"","Mei Feng paused briefly before continuing, \"During the drill, everyone here will be assigned a position somewhere within the city. Your objective is simple. Defend the city from the invading forces.\"","\"In simpler words, it’s an all-out war.\"","General Gu then spoke, \"There are two things you must keep in mind. First, although you won’t actually die during your clashes with the invaders, you can still be ’killed’, which will result in you being ’removed’ from the drill. In addition, a pain-enhancing formation will amplify the pain you experience. Its effect will begin at the maximum level and gradually weaken as the drill progresses, so do your best not to die too early.\"","\"Second, every invader you defeat will earn you merit points, which can contribute toward your future promotions. If you defeat a certain number of invaders, you will receive additional rewards, such as Gaia’s Gifts and powerful techniques.\"","Mei Feng spoke next. \"The drill is scheduled to begin sometime next week, but we will not reveal the exact time. The moment the sirens sound, every soldier will be automatically teleported to their assigned position, regardless of whether they’re ready.\"","She then swept her cold gaze across the area.","\"That concludes the briefing. And for the newer soldiers, I shouldn’t need to say this, but everything discussed here is strictly classified. Revealing any of this information to civilians carries the death penalty, so you are forbidden from sharing it with anyone—including your own family.\"","Once the generals left, the soldiers lingered to chat with each other.","\"Man... we gotta do this drill even more frequently now? What a pain in the ass!\"","\"What are you talking about? This means there will be more opportunities to earn rewards and merits! This is a great change!\"","\"Please tell me it’s a joke... That Gaia’s prophecy is not real...\"","\"Sorry to break it to you, but it’s real.\"","\"W-Why...? Why can’t we tell the civilians? I feel like something this important should be known by everyone...\"","\"Who knows?\"","\"You nervous?\" Sergeant Quang asked Yuan.","He shook his head with a smile before asking, \"How many invaders do we need to defeat for the rewards?\"","\"The minimum for a reward is 10. The most anyone has defeated is 979 invaders.\"","\"How long is this drill?\" Yuan continued asking. \"Surely, it won’t last for years...\"","Sergeant Bing shrugged as she responded, \"Who knows? It varies on our performance, and it has lasted for years in the past, so it’s definitely possible.\""]},{"number":2654,"title":"Chapter 2654: Drill","paragraphs":["When Sergeant Bing saw the frown on Yuan’s face, she chuckled and said, \"Are you worried about fighting for years without rest? Don’t worry, there will be breaks here and there.\"","Yuan shook his head and said, \"It’s not the fighting that worries me. I don’t want the drill to be that long, period.\"","Since he wouldn’t be able to train during the drill, his progress would essentially come to a standstill until it ended, which was far from ideal.","\"I wouldn’t worry about that too much,\" Sergeant Quang suddenly said. \"Although there were instances where a drill lasted for years, that only happened in the early days, when the system was still new, and nobody really knew what they were doing. Nowadays, drills usually last only a few weeks at most.\"","Yuan recalled the last drill and said, \"Now that I think about it, the last drill ended quite fast.\"","\"Oh, that was a special occasion. The drill had to be canceled for some reason,\" revealed Sergeant Bing.","\"Is that so?\"","\"Anyway, I am going to prepare for the drill,\" said Sergeant Quang.","\"How does one prepare for the drill?\" Mei Xiaoyun asked.","\"By doing nothing,\" replied Sergeant Bing. \"Everyone who isn’t out on a mission is prohibited from accepting new missions until it ends, and since the drill could happen at any moment, I also wouldn’t waste my energy training, so just rest until then.\"","\"Speaking of those who are still out on missions... what happens to them? Do they just get to skip the drill?\" Yuan asked curiously.","\"That rarely happens. Drills are announced months in advance, so everyone knows when to stop accepting missions and return to the city before it begins. But yes, if there is an emergency mission that cannot be delayed, those soldiers get to skip drill.\"","Some time later, Yuan and the others left the Parade Deck and returned to their living quarters.","Since there was no telling exactly when the drill would begin—or when they might suddenly be teleported to their assigned positions—most soldiers spent the next several days resting in their rooms. Others passed the time chatting, eating in the cafeteria, or spending time with friends.","As for Yuan, he spent his time studying the Limitless Cultivation Technique.","Six days later, the moment the clock struck three in the afternoon, sirens began blaring throughout the city.","The instant the civilians heard them, they rushed toward the teleporters, evacuating to the underground city.","Meanwhile, every soldier immediately stopped whatever they were doing and prepared to be teleported to their assigned positions.","Yuan opened his eyes to see a notification before him.","<You will be teleported to Sector 7 in 60 seconds>","Sixty seconds later, Yuan was teleported directly from his room to Sector 7.","Once the teleportation was complete, he looked around and found himself standing atop a rooftop somewhere within the sector. Other soldiers were stationed throughout the surrounding area, though none were close enough for a conversation, as they were about three miles away from each other.","He couldn’t see Mei Xiaoyun or the others nearby, so he assumed they were assigned to a different sector.","\"So this won’t be a team-based event, huh?\" Yuan mumbled as he looked toward the sky.","The once-clear blue sky was rapidly darkening, as though a massive storm were closing in from all directions.","A few minutes later, cracks suddenly began appearing across the pitch-black sky, as though countless spears had pierced through it from the other side.","Then, silhouettes emerged from the openings, slowly descending toward the world below.","The moment they appeared, the atmosphere throughout the entire city shifted. An indescribable pressure descended with them, blanketing everything beneath the darkened sky.","Yuan narrowed his eyes at the descending silhouettes. They had humanoid figures and ghostly pale skin, with a pair of large, bat-like wings flapping behind their backs. Their faces also resembled humans, yet their expressions remained eerily blank, making them seem like soulless beings devoid of emotion.","As for their cultivation levels, they varied greatly, ranging from the Third Ascension all the way to the Seventh Ascension.","Ding!","<Military Drill: Stop the Celestial Beings’ invasion on Earth!>","Shortly after their appearance, the Celestial Beings made the first move, unleashing a barrage of Limitless that rained down upon the soldiers like a violent storm.","The soldiers responded by shielding themselves with Limitless. Some avoided them entirely with Void Control.","\"This is... quite boring,\" Yuan muttered as he counterattacked with his own Limitless, firing at the Celestial Beings still descending from the sky.","The moment his Limitless collided with theirs, the enemy attacks shattered with no resistance. Yuan’s attack then continued forward and struck one of the Celestial Beings, killing it instantly.","<Celestial Being defeated>","<Total Points: 1>","After defeating the Celestial Being that had been targeting him, Yuan turned his attention toward the others.","At a glance, it seemed that each soldier had been assigned a single Celestial Being to deal with.","A few minutes later, Yuan lifted his head toward the sky when he noticed more Celestial Beings were appearing.","\"Two of them this time, huh?\" Yuan mumbled to himself as he gazed at the two Celestial Beings that appeared side by side.","A burst of Limitless surged from Yuan’s body before he unleashed a barrage of Limitless bullets at the Celestial Beings, destroying them before they could even attack.","<Celestial Being defeated>","<Total Points: 3>","Meanwhile, the others were still on their first Celestial Being.","As boring as the drill seemed at first, Yuan didn’t complain, as he could tell that the difficulty would gradually increase.","’Hm? Wait a second. Am I only allowed to attack the Celestial Beings targeting me, or can I help the others?’ Yuan suddenly wondered.","After pondering for a moment, he decided to test it himself. Without leaving his assigned position, Yuan launched an attack at a Celestial Being already engaged in combat with another soldier.","<Celestial Being defeated>","<Total Points: 4>","Upon confirming that he could assist the others, Yuan felt a strong urge to defeat every Celestial Being in the area by himself. However, he ultimately restrained himself.","’This is a drill, after all. I should let the others get some experience. I’ll only step in if things start getting out of hand,’ he thought before he waited for more Celestial Beings to show up."]},{"number":2655,"title":"Chapter 2655: Drill(2)","paragraphs":["<Celestial Being defeated>","<Total Points: 50>","A few hours had passed since the drill began, and Yuan had just slain his 50th Celestial Being. Meanwhile, the soldiers around him were still struggling with their third or fourth opponent.","A few more hours passed, but Yuan’s points remained the same, as Celestial Beings had stopped spawning for him.","With nothing else to do, he decided to study the Limitless Cultivation Technique instead.","Meanwhile, somewhere within Gaia’s Heaven, two individuals watched the ongoing drill through a massive screen.","One of these individuals possessed a tall, slender figure and long, pitch-black hair that cascaded down their back like a curtain, clearly a woman.","\"Who is that man with fifty points already?\" asked the black-haired woman.","The other individual, an old man with long white hair and a neatly trimmed white beard, responded, \"That’s Sergeant Yuan, a new soldier who joined the military a little over a year ago. However, very little is known about him. There is essentially no record of him prior to joining the military, as if he’d appeared out of thin air.\"","The black-haired woman then made a graceful gesture with their hand, summoning a system screen before them. It displayed Yuan’s information, including details that weren’t accessible to the public.","\"T-That’s...!\" The old man exclaimed in surprise. \"Perfected Heavenly Refinement?! But when I looked at it before, it showed Inexhaustible Heavenly Refinement!\"","\"His information was altered.\"","\"That explains it...\" the old man muttered. \"If I had suspected that his information had been altered, I would’ve dug deeper. This was my mistake.\"","After a moment of silence, he continued, \"This is the first time someone has achieved the Perfected Heavenly Refinement physique. However, it doesn’t match his cultivation.\"","The black-haired woman did not respond, only continuing to read through Yuan’s information in silence.","\"Truly a peculiar individual... I would like to meet him.\"","\"Y-You?\" The old man wore a shocked expression after hearing those words.","\"Not right now. There is still so much I need to learn about him before I decide if it’s safe to meet him. For all we know, he could be a Celestial Being.\"","\"A Celestial Being?!\" the old man exclaimed in disbelief.","\"It’s just speculation right now. His existence is clearly otherworldly, but whether he is a Celestial Being or not is a different matter.\"","\"Is it possible to ask... you know...\" asked the old man.","\"If only it were that simple...\" sighed the black-haired woman.","She continued a moment later, \"With all that said, I’m not too worried. After all, General Mei seems to trust him, and I trust her judgment.\"","\"General Mei, huh?\" the old man sighed bitterly. \"If I could, I would hand my position over to her rather than that poisonous bastard surnamed Gu. Unfortunately, there are rules within the military that even I cannot ignore.\"","\"Maybe you should—\"","\"No, I won’t intervene,\" the woman interrupted. \"I have faith in General Mei. I believe she is destined to overcome this challenge on her own, without my assistance.\"","She turned to look at the screen spectating the drill and continued, \"Especially if she has someone like that on her side.\"","Time passed swiftly, and before anyone realized it, an entire week had already passed since the drill began.","Yuan, who had been cultivating for the majority of the drill, suddenly opened his eyes as a notification had appeared before him.","<Warm-up will be ending soon>","<The real drill will begin in three days>","When the new soldiers, who had never participated in a drill before, saw the notification and realized the entire past week had only been a warm-up, many of them began to despair.","If what they’d experienced had only been the warm-up, they could hardly imagine how outrageous the real drill would be.","After another day, once all of the Celestial Beings had been defeated, the 3-day countdown began.","<Resting period has begun>","<71:59:59>","The moment the break began, many soldiers collapsed to the ground, breathing heavily as they tried to recover from their exhaustion.","\"Hey, newbie. If you’re already this exhausted after the warm-up, you won’t last ten minutes once the real thing begins,\" an experienced soldier remarked.","\"W-What is the real thing like...?\" the new soldier asked nervously, almost afraid to hear the answer.","\"You’ll find out in three days.\"","Meanwhile, the soldiers stationed near Yuan silently stared at him while they rested.","Although they had spent the entire warm-up fighting almost nonstop, they had all noticed that the Celestial Beings had stopped spawning for Yuan at some point.","\"There have been fewer than ten people who have managed to clear the warm-up...\" one of them suddenly remarked.","\"And he’d done it without his weapon.\"","\"Now that you mentioned it, where is his weapon? I heard that he uses a minigun, too.\"","\"Who knows?\"","\"Does a monster like him even need one?\"","Weapons primarily served to assist their wielder’s control over Limitless, allowing them to use it more efficiently and unleash greater power while consuming less energy. However, Yuan had little to no need for such assistance, so his weapon was mostly for show.","Time continued to pass, and in what felt like the blink of an eye, their 3-day rest period came to an end.","<Resting period has ended>","<Work together with your fellow soldiers to protect this world from destruction!>","Shortly after the notification appeared, the sky once again turned pitch-black.","This time, however, instead of countless smaller openings, a single massive slit resembling an eye slowly opened across the darkened sky. From beyond it, an ominous black fog began pouring into the world.","Of course, this wasn’t ordinary black fog. It was actually countless Celestial Beings packed so densely together that, from a distance, they resembled a massive cloud of black fog.","\"Holy shit...\"","The new soldiers stared at the scene in bewilderment, their eyes wide and mouths agape.","Even the seasoned soldiers who had witnessed and endured it multiple times before couldn’t help but swallow nervously.","\"Now this is more like it...\" Yuan mumbled with a calm smile on his face."]},{"number":2656,"title":"Chapter 2656: Drill(3)","paragraphs":["Shortly after the real drill began and the Celestial Beings started pouring down from the sky, Yuan made the first move, unleashing a barrage of Limitless at the massive horde still descending.","Since this was now a group effort, he no longer had any reason to hold back.","<Defeated a Celestial Being>","<Defeated a Celestial Being>","<Defeated a Celestial Being>","<Total Points: 154>","In the blink of an eye, Yuan tripled his points by defeating all of the weaker Celestial Beings first.","\"This guy is truly outrageous!\"","The other soldiers stared at Yuan with wide eyes, their expressions filled with shock.","Yuan ignored them completely and shot into the sky, charging straight toward the sea of Celestial Beings as though he intended to take on the entire army by himself.","\"What the hell is he doing?!\"","\"Does he intend to fight them all by himself?! That’s ridiculous!\"","\"He’s clearly just trying to show off, but at this rate, he’ll only get himself killed and removed from the drill early,\" one of the soldiers said.","\"Yeah. Let’s stop paying attention to him and focus on ourselves. This may only be a drill, but our performance here can have a huge impact on our chances of promotion, especially if you’re aiming to become an officer!\"","However, Yuan wasn’t the only soldier charging toward the Celestial Beings. Several others were doing the same, most of them being experienced soldiers and officers. Meanwhile, the newer soldiers and those less confident in their abilities remained behind. Of course, these soldiers made up the majority of the military.","\"That guy...\"","Not too far away, in Sector 1, Ironwoman spotted Yuan ahead of her, immediately igniting her competitive spirit.","Ever since discovering Yuan and his overwhelming talent, she had wanted to compete with him. However, the difference in their ranks and cultivation had never given her a proper opportunity to do so—until now.","Meanwhile, the Celestial Beings did not simply wait for the soldiers to attack. They immediately bombarded everyone approaching with a massive wave of Limitless that spread outward like an enormous wall, leaving no room to evade normally.","Although Yuan could have avoided the attack using Void Manipulation, he chose to confront it head-on. With a slash of his arm, he unleashed a wave of Limitless infused with Supreme Sword Aura and a small trace of Eternal Essence.","A sword light flickered into existence and collided with the massive wall of Limitless. The two forces remained locked against each other for a good moment before Yuan’s attack finally broke through, slicing the wall cleanly in half and splitting the torrent of energy in two.","The scene shocked all of the soldiers watching, their jaws dropping wide open.","After breaking through the Celestial Beings’ attack, Yuan immediately used Void Manipulation to close the distance in an instant.","However, instead of confronting the army from the front, he teleported directly into the heart of their formation, deliberately allowing himself to be surrounded.","Despite Yuan’s unexpected actions, the Celestial Beings showed no visible reaction and calmly attacked him.","Not wanting to go overboard with his performance, Yuan kept his use of Eternal Essence to a bare minimum, relying on it only to defend against particularly dangerous attacks and never using it offensively.","Instead, he used Supreme Sword Aura and Limitless, which was already more than enough to deal with many of the Celestial Beings there.","<Defeated a Celestial Being>","<Defeated a Celestial Being>","<Defeated a Celestial Being>","<Total Points: 284>","Yuan’s points skyrocketed thanks to his bold and aggressive strategy, nearly doubling within mere moments.","Seeing this, Ironwoman unleashed her full cultivation. The power of her ninth-level Seventh Ascension cultivation instantly swept across the area, causing even the air itself to tremble.","Once she reached the Celestial Beings and began fighting them, her points also rose rapidly. However, her pace was nowhere near Yuan’s. Despite having a much lower cultivation, Yuan was defeating the Celestial Beings far faster than she was.","Of course, the Ironwoman didn’t know this, as she was too focused on the Celestial Beings to pay attention to Yuan, much less count his kills.","Time passed, and although Yuan was constantly defeating and holding off hundreds of Celestial Beings on his own, they continued pouring endlessly from the eye-shaped slit in the sky.","Eventually, their sheer numbers overwhelmed the soldiers fighting in the air, allowing the Celestial Beings to reach the city and clash with the soldiers below.","It didn’t take long for the drill to erupt into a full-blown war, with over a hundred thousand beings locked in fierce combat at once. The once-peaceful city had transformed into a massive battlefield, with unimaginable destruction unfolding in every corner.","However, the Celestial Beings vastly outnumbered the soldiers, forcing nearly everyone to fight at least two enemies at once, while some had to contend with three or more.","Faced with such overwhelming numbers, it didn’t take long for the newer soldiers to realize the battle was unwinnable and defeat inevitable.","As for the veteran soldiers who had experienced the drill before, they were already well aware of this. In fact, throughout the history of the drills, the soldiers had never once succeeded in repelling the invasion.","It didn’t take long for the soldiers to start dying to the Celestial Beings, and within minutes, their numbers began dropping like flies.","Within an hour, nearly a quarter of the soldiers had already died and been removed from the drill. Whenever a soldier ’died’ in battle, they were automatically teleported to a separate area, where they would remain until the drill concluded.","By the end of the first day, only half of the 70,000 soldiers remained.","As for the Celestial Beings, their numbers only continued to grow, seemingly without end. Moreover, every newly spawned Celestial Being possessed a cultivation of at least the Fifth Ascension, meaning their forces were only growing stronger as the battle progressed, as the weaker ones no longer spawned.","The third day came and passed, and by the end, less than ten thousand soldiers remained."]},{"number":2657,"title":"Chapter 2657: The Last Three Survivors","paragraphs":["As more and more soldiers were killed and removed from the drill, the burden on those remaining only grew heavier, forcing them to take on an increasing number of Celestial Beings at once.","Since this was a group effort, practically every soldier fought alongside a squad, including Ironwoman. The only ones still fighting alone were those whose teammates had already been eliminated or who were too surrounded by enemies to receive any assistance.","Of course, there was Yuan, who was fighting alone by choice.","Not only had he been fighting alone this entire time, but he wasn’t even fighting seriously.","’What was the record again? 979 Celestial Beings?’","Yuan looked at his own score as he avoided the Celestial Beings’ attacks left and right.","<Total Points: 4,162>","\"...\"","Before he realized it, he’d already surpassed the record more than four times.","’Well, there’s nothing I can do now that I’ve passed the record. But I should still hold back a little...’ Yuan thought to himself.","Time continued to pass, and at the end of the fourth day, the number of soldiers halved.","By the end of the fifth day, the number fell even more, and less than a thousand soldiers remained on the battlefield.","In less than a week, the entire city had been reduced to ruins, without a single building left standing.","At the start of the seventh day, exactly a week after the real drill began, the number of soldiers had fallen to below a hundred. Meanwhile, there were still thousands... tens of thousands of Celestial Beings.","However, even though the Celestial Beings vastly outnumbered the soldiers, it wasn’t as though the soldiers had to fight all of them at once, as there was clearly a limit to how many could engage each soldier at any given time.","Even so, most of the soldiers were utterly exhausted and barely holding on. By the end of the seventh day, their numbers had dwindled by eighty percent, leaving fewer than twenty soldiers left in the drill.","\"I don’t get it. How is someone at the Fifth Ascension able to last this long?\" a soldier suddenly asked aloud.","Soldiers who had been removed from the drill were allowed to spectate the remaining participants, and at that moment, most of them were watching Yuan.","\"Well, he’s famous for having a tremendous and abnormal amount of energy. I heard he could wield the minigun nonstop for days.\"","\"He must have a powerful technique that allows him to recover his Limitless. Otherwise, it doesn’t make any sense.\"","\"To possess such a powerful technique... I wonder where he’s from.\"","\"I heard a rumor saying that he’s actually from another city.\"","\"How much longer do you think he’ll last? He’s slowed down tremendously compared to yesterday.\"","Five more soldiers fell within the next six hours.","\"It’s really hard to believe that he’s a new soldier. His combat experience is on another level...\"","\"For a combat instructor like you to praise him so highly...\"","After another six hours, the number of soldiers remaining fell below ten.","\"To think he’d reach the top 10 on his first drill!\"","\"Do you think he’s broken the previous record of the most Celestial Beings defeated?\"","\"Definitely, but he won’t be the only one to break a record. Seeing how the Ironwoman is taking this drill seriously, she’ll likely break it, too.\"","\"I guess she’s heard the rumor of Sergeant Yuan being seen as her rival.\"","By the end of the eighth day, only three soldiers were left in the drill.","The Ironwoman, Yuan, and another soldier bearing the insignia of a Colonel.","\"Congratulations, General Mei! With two of our soldiers, Ironwoman and Sergeant Yuan, dominating the drill, General Gu must be shaking with worry!\" one of her officers remarked.","Mei Feng nodded and said, \"Although the drill is important, it won’t be enough to secure my promotion.\"","The drill continued for another three days without anyone else being eliminated. However, two days later, the Colonel finally fell, leaving only Ironwoman and Yuan left in the drill.","’So it’s just the two of us now...’","Yuan briefly considered whether he should continue or simply give up and let Ironwoman take the victory—even though this wasn’t a competition.","After some thought, however, he decided against giving up so easily. It would undoubtedly draw even more unnecessary attention to himself, but at this point, he felt it was already too late to worry about that.","’Let’s see how long you can last!’","One day... two days... three days passed with only Ironwoman and Yuan remaining on the battlefield, yet neither of them showed any signs of nearing defeat.","Five days... six days... seven...","The drill entered its second week, yet Ironwoman and Yuan still remained on the battlefield.","Yuan had long since given up on defeating the Celestial Beings and shifted his focus entirely to survival, using Void Manipulation nonstop to evade their attacks. His main reason for not fighting them was simply because he didn’t want to increase his points too much, but another reason was that the Celestial Beings being spawned are all at least the Seventh Ascension.","\"That guy is trying to outlast the Ironwoman!\"","\"Isn’t it technically cheating if he’s not even fighting anymore?\" one of the spectators remarked.","\"Not really... Just look at the difference in their cultivation. It’d be unreasonable to expect him to keep fighting them at this point. Hell, I’d even argue that using Void Control nonstop is more exhausting than fighting.\"","\"What’s the point of continuing if he’s not going to fight? The purpose of this drill isn’t to survive for as long as possible, but to defeat as many Celestial Beings as you can. If you can’t do that anymore, you might as well give up.\"","Yuan’s actions quickly divided the spectators into two camps. One side supported his actions, while the other questioned the point of continuing.","\"Knowing him, he’s probably using this opportunity to train his Void Control,\" said Shi Fa.","\"Not probably. Definitely,\" said Wu Wang."]},{"number":2658,"title":"Chapter 2658: End of the Drill","paragraphs":["Another week has passed since Yuan and Ironwoman became the last two survivors of the drill, meaning they’d spent three weeks fight nonstop at this point.","’Looks like she’s on her last leg.’ Yuan thought to himself after seeing the Ironwoman’s condition.","’I guess it’s about time for me to give up...’","However, Yuan suddenly realized something.","’Will I even be able to lose?’ he wondered inwardly.","After all, with his regeneration, it might be impossible for him to die normally. Moreover, he was worried about revealing his healing capabilities to the military.","’I am already suspected of being a Void Specter... If I reveal my regeneration ability, that might give them more ammunition against me.’","After some consideration, Yuan decided against giving up. In fact, he decided that if he had already made it this far, he might as well survive until the end.","A few hours later, Ironwoman finally exhausted all of her energy and fell to the Celestial Beings.","\"H-He actually outlasted the Ironwoman!\"","The spectators were left in awe by the unexpected outcome, as everyone was certain that the Ironwoman would be the last survivor.","\"How much longer do you think he’ll last?\"","\"What’s the point of trying to stay alive now that he’s the last one standing? He’s already proved his point.\"","\"Right? It’s not like he can defeat the Celestial Beings, either.\"","Shortly after Ironwoman was removed from the drill, Yuan decided to give up as well. Since he was already the last survivor, there was no point in continuing, especially when even he couldn’t defeat the Celestial Beings without relying on Eternal Essence.","To avoid making his surrender too obvious, Yuan continued dodging their attacks for several more minutes before deliberately allowing one of the Celestial Beings to land a direct hit, its Limitless striking him squarely in the heart.","\"...\"","\"...\"","\"Damn it...\"","Yuan let out a deep sigh when he realized he hadn’t died or been removed from the drill.","His greatest concern had come true. Because of his regeneration, he was literally incapable of dying through normal means.","’Let’s try this again...’","After pretending like the first strike wasn’t fatal, Yuan continued evading the Celestial Beings’ attack for another minute before letting them strike him again. This time, however, he struck himself with his own Eternal Essence, ensuring that he died from it.","<You have died>","<You have been teleported>","Yuan found himself back in the military base at the Parade Deck after being teleported.","Moments later, Mei Feng and General Gu appeared before them and said, \"With the last soldier out of the battlefield, we will end the drill here.\"","General Gu continued, \"Although the drill ends here, it will not be the last one, and we intend to have another one in three years. Those of you who performed poorly during this drill will be required to participate in supplementary training. That is all.\"","Mei Feng then said, \"Besides Ironwoman and Sergeant Yuan, you’re all now dismissed.\"","The soldiers scattered the next moment.","\"Come with me to my office,\" Mei Feng said to Yuan and Ironwoman afterward.","Some time later, once they were inside her office, Mei Feng said, \"First and foremost, I want to say good work. You’ve both managed to perform beyond expectations and even broken the record.\"","She turned to look at Yuan and asked, \"What did you think of the drill?\"","\"Quite frankly, I’m a little disappointed,\" he shrugged.","\"Can you elaborate?\" Mei Feng asked, raising an eyebrow at his response.","\"There’s not much to it. Do we simply fight until we can’t fight anymore? What’s the purpose of that?\" Yuan asked.","Mei Feng remained silent for a moment before responding, \"Because we don’t know the full extent of the threat we’ll face in the future, we can only prepare in a way that gives our soldiers the greatest chance of survival. If the drill is too easy, they won’t learn anything from it and will be woefully unprepared when the real threat arrives.\"","\"With that being said, it’s not impossible to win the drill. It just hasn’t happened yet.\"","\"Is there a reward for beating it?\" Yuan then asked.","\"I knew you’d ask that,\" Mei Feng sighed before responding, \"But to answer your question... no, not really, but the better your performance, the faster you’ll be promoted, which is your goal, right?\"","Yuan nodded.","\"Well, considering your performance this time... I won’t be surprised if you’ve already earned enough merits to be promoted again, even though you’ve just received your promotion.\"","Yuan then said, \"Speaking of promotions... when does my credential rank increase? It’s been a while since it happened.\"","Mei Feng fell silent for a moment before a look of realization appeared on her face.","\"I forgot to tell you, but your credential rank doesn’t automatically increase after rank 3. You’ll need to manually apply for an upgrade.\"","\"Seriously?\" Yuan sighed out loud.","\"Sorry.\" Mei Feng apologized.","\"Well, that’s fine. Where do I go to increase it?\"","\"I can show you after this,\" said Ironwoman.","\"Okay.\"","The Ironwoman then asked, \"Anyway, why’d you call us?\"","Mei Feng’s expression turned serious as she responded, \"An assembly has been initiated. I believe you know what’ll be discussed even without needing me to say it.\"","The Ironwoman quietly turned her head to look at Yuan.","\"I think I have an idea,\" she said a moment later.","\"The highest-ranking authority from each military will be attending this assembly, so our Supreme General will have to travel to the meeting location. I want the two of you to escort him there,\" Mei Feng said.","\"Wait...\" Ironwoman quickly interjected. \"I understand why you’d want to send me, but why send him as well when he’s the main subject of the discussion?\"","\"I have two reasons. First, I hope to clear up the misunderstanding before it spreads any further. Second... I want him to become acquainted with the Supreme General. Although the Supreme General will likely seek him out sooner or later after his performance at the drill, I’d rather it be sooner than later.\""]},{"number":2659,"title":"Chapter 2659: Assembly","paragraphs":["\"I understand that you want him to form a connection with the Supreme General, but I still don’t think it’s a good idea to send a new soldier like him on a mission like this, especially when we’ll be meeting some of the highest-ranking individuals from the other militaries. Surely, there are other ways to introduce the two of them.\"","Ironwoman shook her head, worried that the other cities would look down on them for sending a mere Sergeant to such an important assembly.","Although Ironwoman herself wasn’t particularly high-ranking within the military, her prowess and reputation far surpassed those of even some of the highest-ranking soldiers in Gaia’s Heaven, so it made sense for her to participate in the assembly.","Yuan, however, was essentially an unknown soldier outside of their city. Even worse, he was currently suspected of being a Void Specter by another city, even being the reason the assembly was happening in the first place.","Rather than making the decision on her own, Mei Feng turned to look at Yuan and asked him, \"What do you think? Do you want to go? I won’t force you if you refuse.\"","\"Just to clarify, you want me to escort the Supreme General to this assembly, where they’ll likely talk about me being a Void Specter, and try to convince them that I am actually a human?\" Yuan asked for clarification.","\"Indeed.\" Mei Feng nodded.","\"What if I fail to convince them and do the opposite?\" Yuan then asked.","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Mei Feng responded, \"If you fail to convince them that you’re human—or somehow make the situation even worse—you could end up becoming an enemy of every other city. Hell, there’s even a chance you might be exiled from this city.\"","\"Exile, huh? That sounds fun,\" Yuan calmly remarked with a smile on his face.","\"Anyway, I want to go to this assembly. It sounds too fun to miss,\" he then said.","\"Then I’ll put your name on the list. Also, it won’t just be the two of you, as General Gu will also send two of his own soldiers. Of course, there’s also the Ninth Division, who answers only to the Supreme General.\"","After a brief pause, Mei Feng continued, \"The assembly will happen next month, but since it won’t take place in any city, you won’t be able to teleport there.\"","\"One last thing... Although it’s unlikely General Gu’s soldiers will try to do anything funny in the Supreme General’s presence, it’s not guaranteed, so stay alert,\" Mei Feng said, warning Yuan.","\"I will keep that in mind.\"","\"You’ll start your journey in three days, so do whatever you need until then. That’s all.\"","Yuan left the office shortly after, leaving Ironwoman behind.","\"I don’t really have much to say to you. Just keep an eye out for him,\" Mei Feng said to Ironwoman after Yuan left.","The Ironwoman nodded before asking, \"What did you think of the drill? About his performance? I didn’t have the luxury to pay attention during, but I’ll definitely watch the recording later.\"","\"Hard to say. I don’t know if I should be happy or disappointed.\"","\"Huh? Why would you be disappointed?\" Ironwoman inquired, raising an eyebrow.","\"Because it didn’t seem like he was giving it his all during the drill.\" Mei Feng sighed.","\"On one hand, I’m glad he managed to become the last survivor. On the other hand, I was hoping to see him do much more.\"","\"He probably didn’t want to attract any more attention than he already had, especially with the entire military watching.\"","\"I know, but I really want to see him go all out—to see what he’s truly capable of.\"","\"Give him a little more time. Knowing his character and arrogance, he’ll definitely show it to us in the near future.\"","The Ironwoman left shortly after, but when she went outside, she noticed that Yuan hadn’t completely left.","\"You said you’d show me where I can increase my credential rank, so I waited for you,\" said Yuan when he saw her coming out.","Ironwoman nodded and said, \"Follow me.\"","Some time later, they entered a building Yuan had never been to before.","\"Just tell them you’re here to see if you qualify for a credential upgrade.\"","\"Okay.\"","Yuan approached the front desk and asked, \"I’m here to see if I qualify for a credential upgrade.\"","The worker then gestured toward the usual machine before Yuan.","Yuan placed his hand in the machine and allowed it to consume a drop of his blood.","A moment later, the worker’s expression changed drastically, causing Yuan to raise an eyebrow.","\"P-Please wait a moment...\"","Without any explanation, the worker stood up and rushed into the room in the back.","\"What happened?\"","The Ironwoman approached Yuan and asked after seeing this unusual response.","\"I don’t know.\"","Several minutes passed without any sign of the worker.","Suddenly, Yuan noticed a group of soldiers wearing uniforms different from those he was accustomed to entering the building.","These soldiers walked straight to Yuan and said to him, \"Sergeant Yuan, you’re currently under arrest. Please do not resist and come with us peacefully.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow at this unexpected situation, but before he could even say anything, the Ironwoman stepped forward and asked, \"What the hell is going on? Why is he being arrested?\"","The soldiers looked at her and responded, \"Sorry, but even we don’t know the details.\"","Ironwoman frowned upon hearing this. Whatever was happening must be incredibly serious if even the military police didn’t know the details.","She turned to Yuan and said, \"Just go with them for now and find out what this is about. I’ll speak with General Mei first, then come find you.\"","\"Okay.\" Yuan nodded, then calmly followed the military police away.","Meanwhile, Ironwoman rushed back to General Mei’s office and informed her of the situation.","Mei Feng immediately rose from her seat upon hearing the news, disbelief written across her face.","\"There’s no way an arrest order could’ve been issued for him without me knowing about it!\" she exclaimed."]},{"number":2660,"title":"Chapter 2660: Arrested Again","paragraphs":["\"Did the military police reveal the reason for his arrest?\" Mei Feng asked.","\"No, I asked them, but they claim to not know the details, either.\"","The frown on Mei Feng’s face deepened.","\"Only Generals are able to issue arrest orders to the military police without giving a proper reason, so it’s likely that General Gu had something to do with this. For such a thing to happen right before the assembly, what shitty timing!\" Mei Feng cursed aloud.","She then said to the Ironwoman, \"Go to Sergeant Yuan and ensure nothing happens to him while I go speak with General Gu.\"","\"I understand.\"","While the Ironwoman went to the military prison, Mei Feng made her way to General Gu’s office. Although Mei Feng could contact General Gu much faster on the phone, she felt it would be more effective to show up in person.","Some time later—","\"What did you just say?\"","The Ironwoman questioned with a deep frown on her face.","\"Sergeant Yuan is no longer with us... He was escorted away literally the moment we took him here,\" said the military police who arrested Yuan.","\"Who took him away? Was it General Gu?\"","\"General Gu?\" The military soldier repeated in a puzzled tone before responding, \"No, the one who escorted him away was...\"","\"What?!\" Ironwoman exclaimed in disbelief.","Meanwhile, Mei Feng arrived at General Gu’s office.","\"General Mei? You’ve been visiting my office an awful lot recently. What is it this time?\" General Gu glared at her with an unwelcoming expression.","\"Why did you put an arrest order for Sergeant Yuan?\" Mei Feng went straight to the point.","\"An arrest order? What are you talking about?\" General Gu replied with a genuinely puzzled face.","\"Don’t play dumb. Only you and I can arrest someone without giving a reason.\"","General Gu rubbed his eyes and sighed, \"I don’t know what to tell you except that I had nothing to do with it. If Sergeant Yuan was arrested, then it was because of his own doing.\"","\"You—!\"","Just as Mei Feng opened her mouth to speak, she noticed the Ironwoman was calling her.","\"What happened?\"","\"It’s Sergeant Yuan. He was escorted away by the time I reached the prison, and you won’t believe this, but I don’t think General Gu had anything to do with his arrest.\"","\"What...?\" Mei Feng wore a dumbfounded look on her face after hearing this.","Her eyes glanced at General Gu, and sure enough, he looked genuinely confused by the whole situation.","\"Who arrested him?\" she then asked.","\"That would be...\"","\"What?!\" Mei Feng exclaimed in disbelief after hearing the response. \"Why would they arrest him?!\"","\"I don’t know, but this is the first time anything like this has happened before.\"","\"Alright... I’ll be with you in a moment.\"","After hanging up, Mei Feng returned her attention to General Gu but said nothing.","\"Sounds like you made a mistake, General Mei,\" General Gu spoke first, breaking the silence.","\"If I really made a mistake, I’ll apologize for it. However, since I don’t have all of the information, I’ll wait until I do.\"","After saying that, Mei Feng turned around and left.","Once Mei Feng left, General Gu made his own call.","\"I just received news that Sergeant Yuan was arrested. I want every piece of information you can find on it!\"","Meanwhile, somewhere within the military base, Yuan sat inside an empty white room that resembled a seclusion room in a psychiatric ward.","Seated across from him was a group of individuals dressed in white uniforms resembling those worn by scientists.","\"So, what is this all about?\" Yuan finally asked after several minutes had passed without anyone saying a word.","One of them responded, \"Do you really have no idea why you’re here?\"","Yuan calmly shook his head.","\"Do you even know where you are right now?\" another asked.","\"Should I?\"","After another moment of silence, one of the individuals in white retrieved an Unknown Ore and placed it on the desk before them.","\"Do you know what this is?\"","\"An Unknown Ore?\"","\"Anything special about it?\"","\"...\"","Yuan fell silent as he stared at the Unknown Ore.","’I see... so this is what it’s about...’ Yuan sighed inwardly as he realized what was happening.","The Unknown Ore sitting before him was obviously one he had personally collected—and completely drained of its energy.","\"Well?\"","One of the individuals spoke again when Yuan didn’t respond.","Yuan shook his head and said, \"It looks like an ordinary Unknown Ore to me.\"","\"It is indeed an Unknown Ore, but there is nothing ordinary about it.\"","They retrieved another piece of Unknown Ore and placed it beside the first, but there was a clear difference between the two.","Unlike the first, which glistened like a first-rate jewel, the second lacked its usual shimmering appearance and looked like nothing more than an ordinary piece of colorless crystal.","\"It may be hard to believe, but these two are actually the same,\" one of them explained. \"Normally, when an Unknown Ore loses all of its energy, it also loses its glistening appearance and ends up looking like this. However, for some reason, this one retained its original appearance despite having no energy left.\"","\"Okay...?\" Yuan muttered.","\"Why are you telling me this?\" he asked.","\"Because we’re hoping you can help us solve this phenomenon.\"","\"And what makes you think I have the answer to your question?\"","\"For starters, this Unknown Ore was collected by you. In fact...\"","One of the individuals stood up, walked to the side of the room, retrieved a spatial cube, and emptied its contents onto the floor. In the blink of an eye, thousands of glistening Unknown Ores formed a massive pile.","\"All of these were gathered by you. More importantly, out of everyone in the military, you’re the only person who has ever brought back Unknown Ores like these.\"","\"And whatever you say next, please don’t tell us it’s a coincidence, because none of us will believe you.\"","After those words, the room fell silent once again as Yuan stared quietly at the massive pile of Unknown Ores before him."]},{"number":2661,"title":"Chapter 2661: Arrested Again(2)","paragraphs":["While it wasn’t technically true that all the Unknown Ores came from Yuan, since many were collected as a squad, there was no denying that Yuan was involved in all of them.","He silently stared at the Unknown Ores, wondering how he should tackle this situation.","However, before Yuan could say anything, another individual retrieved a second spatial cube and emptied its contents onto the floor, revealing another pile of glistening crystals.","This time, however, they were Unknown Crystals.","\"These Unknown Crystals are affected by the same phenomenon, and they were also collected by you, Sergeant Yuan.\"","\"Well? What do you have to say for yourself?\"","\"Let’s stop wasting time and reveal how you extracted their energy without the use of specialized equipment!\" one of them shouted as he slammed the desk.","\"...\"","\"Why are you staying silent? We can take that as an admission of guilt.\"","Yuan closed his eyes and took a deep breathe, looking as though he was prepared to reveal the truth.","Then, he spoke, \"I’m staying silent because I didn’t want to waste my breath.\"","\"What?\"","They frowned at his words.","\"You already said that you wouldn’t believe me, so why even bother?\"","\"So you’re telling us that this is all just a huge coincidence and that you’re not responsible for it?\"","Yuan quietly nodded his head, leaving them speechless, as they really expected him to give in after showing him so much evidence.","\"Listen carefully. I don’t know how you managed to do it, but this is a national-level security issue that goes far beyond this city! If the other cities discover that there’s a way to extract Limitless from Unknown Ores and Crystals without using any machinery, they’ll do everything in their power to obtain that method!\"","\"Then I don’t see the issue, since I can’t extract Limitless from them,\" Yuan calmly said.","Although his words might have sounded like a lie, he was actually telling the truth. What he extracted from the Unknown Ores and Crystals wasn’t Limitless, but Eternal Essence.","\"You—!\"","Just as one of the white-suited individuals opened their mouth to speak, another voice resounded from outside.","\"W-Wait! You can’t go inside, General—!\"","Bang!","The door suddenly swung open, and two individuals walked into the room.","\"General Mei? Ironwoman? What are the two of you doing here?\"","\"I think you know very well why I am here,\" Mei Feng responded with a slight frown on her face.","\"Even if you’re a General, you cannot just barge into this facility as if you own it, General Mei. Also, we have full authority to arrest someone.\"","\"This isn’t his first time being targeted, so I am just doing my due diligence,\" Mei Feng said. \"If you have a valid reason for arresting him, I will not intervene.\"","She scanned the room, trying to understand the situation, but it only left her more puzzled.","\"They think I can extract Limitless from Unknown Ores and Crystals,\" Yuan suddenly spoke, revealing the reason they arrested him.","\"What?\" Mei Feng frowned after hearing these words, turning to look at the group of individuals with a questioning gaze.","\"Despite their flawless appearance, all of the Unknown Ores and Unknown Crystals you see in this room lack energy, and it started happening ever since his appearance. Moreover, they were all collected by him—or rather, he was involved in all of them,\" elaborated one of the individuals.","\"When did this start happening? And how come this is my first time hearing about this?\" Mei Feng then asked.","\"We started noticing it shortly after Sergeant Yuan went on his first gathering mission, so about a year ago. As for why we’ve kept this a secret until now... We were simply gathering more evidence.\"","After a moment of silence, Mei Feng turned to look at Yuan and asked, \"What do you have to say for yourself?\"","\"...\"","Although Yuan could simply continue denying it, there was one issue. The Ironwoman had watched him collect Unknown Ores in the Black Zone and likely already knew the truth.","Eventually, Yuan let out a defeated sigh and said, \"This might require me to reveal my... You know what. Should I still tell them?\"","Mei Feng fell silent for another moment before nodding. \"It’s not like we can keep it hidden forever. We’re bound to reveal it sooner or later anyway. Moreover, this situation is much more serious than you think.\"","Yuan nodded and revealed, \"This is just a hypothesis, but because of my physique, my body automatically absorbs the energy within Unknown Ores and Unknown Crystals whenever I touch them. Unfortunately, it’s not something I can control.\"","\"What sort of nonsense is that?\"","The people in white swiftly remarked with doubtful expressions.","\"He has the Perfected Heavenly Refinement physique,\" Mei Feng revealed.","\"What?!\"","Not just the people in white, but even the Ironwoman exclaimed in shock after hearing this.","\"B-But we saw his information!\"","\"I had it concealed for obvious reasons.\"","\"...\"","The room fell silent as everyone there turned to look at Yuan with dumbfounded faces.","\"H-How is that even possible? He’s only at the Fifth Ascension!\"","\"I was born with it,\" Yuan calmly lied.","After a long minute of silence, one of them spoke, \"We will need to confirm two things. One, that you really have the Perfected Heavenly Refinement physique, and two, that you can absorb the energy of Unknown Ores that you touch.\"","\"Fine by me.\" Yuan easily agreed.","Some time later, they brought a capsule-shaped machine into the room and instructed Yuan to enter it.","However, this was no ordinary machine. Only individuals with the highest Credential Ranks could operate it, and it revealed virtually everything.","[Physique: Perfected Heavenly Refinement]","\"I-It’s true! He really has the Perfected Heavenly Refinement physique!\"","\"This is the first confirmed Perfected Heavenly Refinement physique in history!\"","\"Perfected Heavenly Refinement, huh?\" Ironwoman mumbled in a low voice as she begun to understand the reason behind Yuan’s unfathomable talents and capabilities.","A few minutes later, they moved on to the second test and handed Yuan an Unknown Ore and Unknown Crystal that still had all of its energy."]},{"number":2662,"title":"Chapter 2662: Extractors","paragraphs":["\"Go ahead. Absorb the energy in this Unknown Ore and Unknown Crystal.\"","Yuan accepted them and held one in each hand before absorbing their Eternal Essence.","\"Done.\"","A moment later, he handed them back to the individual in white.","\"That fast?!\"","They didn’t dare to believe it, but after examining the Unknown Ore and Unknown Crystal, they had no choice but to believe it.","\"I don’t get it. If you absorbed so much Limitless, why hasn’t your cultivation shown any results?\" one of them questioned out loud.","Yuan shrugged and said, \"I don’t know. As a matter of fact, I didn’t even realize my physique had this power until you dragged me here.\"","\"What now, Senior Zhang?\" asked another individual in white.","\"...\"","\"We will need some time to decide what to do with this information,\" said Senior Zhang.","\"Until then, we’ll have to keep you here,\" she added while looking at Yuan.","Mei Feng then said, \"Sorry, but that won’t do. He’ll be heading to the assembly with the Supreme General in three days.\"","\"You can just find someone else to go.\"","\"That won’t be possible, either.\"","\"Why is that?\" Senior Zhang asked.","\"That isn’t something I can disclose to you,\" Mei Feng replied.","\"Even though we have the same Credential Rank?\"","\"We may have the same Credential Rank, but our clearances are still different. While there is information within this facility that I’m not authorized to access, there is also military-related information that you’re not authorized to know, since you’re not a soldier.\"","\"...\"","\"Three days, right? He’ll remain here until then. I doubt we’ll need any longer than that,\" Senior Zhang said.","\"I can accept that, but what is there even to consider? He possesses a never-before-seen physique, and while it’s true that he’s been turning in defective Unknown Ores and Crystals, he claims he wasn’t aware of it. I believe him, too. After all, how could he have possibly known when the Unknown Ores remain completely unchanged in appearance even after their energy has been drained?\"","\"I’m not going to argue with you here. Three days. You’ll have your answer in three days.\"","As much as Mei Feng wanted to free Yuan, there was truly nothing she could do in this situation.","\"Don’t worry, I’ll be fine,\" Yuan said.","Mei Feng nodded and left shortly after with Ironwoman.","Meanwhile, Yuan was taken to another room, already furnished like a bedroom.","\"You are prohibited from leaving until we say so,\" Senior Zhang said to him.","After locking Yuan inside the room, Senior Zhang and the others left to discuss the situation.","Inside Mei Feng’s office, she and the Ironwoman also had their own discussion.","\"What do you think?\" Mei Feng asked. \"Is Sergeant Yuan telling the truth?\"","The Ironwoman closed her eyes to recall everything she’d seen in the Black Zone.","\"Hard to say, since we don’t know much, if anything, about the Perfected Heavenly Refinement physique. However, I do believe he was lying when he said he didn’t know until today,\" Ironwoman said.","\"Is that so?\"","Despite declaring she believed Yuan, Mei Feng also doubted it.","\"It’s obvious that he’s hiding a lot from us, but who doesn’t have secrets? I’m sure he has his reasons,\" said the Ironwoman. \"Most importantly, I don’t feel worried even knowing that.\"","\"The biggest question right now is what they—the Extractors—will do about it.\"","The Extractors were the individuals dressed in white. Although they weren’t soldiers, their Credential Ranks were higher than those of most military personnel due to the importance of their work, which involved extracting Limitless from Unknown Ores and Unknown Crystals.","Of course, this wasn’t a job that just anyone could apply for. One could become an Extractor only through a personal invitation from the Supreme General, after undergoing a lengthy and rigorous vetting process.","Three days passed in the blink of an eye.","\"Damn it... I thought this would be a simple decision...\" Senior Zhang sighed as she sank back into her chair, looking defeated after they failed to reach a decision on how to deal with Yuan.","\"Quite frankly, I think this is beyond us. Let’s just speak with the Supreme General and have him decide,\" one of the Extractors suggested.","\"I agree.\"","\"Fine. I’ll speak with the Supreme General,\" Senior Zhang sighed aloud.","Some time later, she called the Supreme General and revealed the entire situation to him.","The Supreme General did not speak for several minutes as he pondered.","Eventually, he responded, \"Let him go. I’ll deal with him myself.\"","\"Understood.\"","Senior Zhang did not question the Supreme General’s decision and immediately released Yuan.","\"Am I free to go?\" Yuan asked.","\"I guess so,\" said Senior Zhang, not revealing everything.","Yuan had expected them to at least warn him against touching any more Unknown Ores or Unknown Crystals, but to his surprise, they said nothing and simply let him leave without another word.","After leaving, Yuan went straight to Mei Feng, who was just as surprised by the outcome as he was.","\"What? They simply let you leave without saying anything? There’s no way they’d let this matter go so easily. Something is definitely going on, so don’t let your guard down,\" she warned.","\"What now?\" Yuan asked a moment later.","\"Until we have a clearer understanding of the situation, all you can do is carry on as usual. In any case, your escort mission has already been approved, so you’ll be accompanying the Supreme General to the assembly.\"","\"Alright.\"","\"Also, I shouldn’t have to say this, but refrain from touching any more Unknown Ores and Unknown Crystals from now on,\" Mei Feng added.","\"Of course.\" Yuan calmly nodded.","Even without Mei Feng’s warning, he had already decided to stop absorbing their energy—or at the very least, stop turning in the ones he had drained. After all, he could obtain far more Eternal Essence by defeating Void Specters in the level 2 Black Zone.","\"Head to the Parade Deck within the next hour,\" Mei Feng said shortly later.","\"Alright. See you later.\"","Yuan bid her farewell and left the office."]},{"number":2663,"title":"Chapter 2663: Supreme General","paragraphs":["After leaving Mei Feng’s office, Yuan immediately made his way to the Parade Deck since he had no need to prepare.","On his way to the Parade Deck, Yuan bumped into a familiar face.","\"Did you just meet with my mother?\" Mei Xiaoyun asked after noticing the direction he was coming from.","\"Yes, she sent me on a new mission.\"","\"A mission directly from a General, huh? It must be fairly important.\"","\"Well, I will be escorting the Supreme General.\"","\"The Supreme General?!\" Mei Xiaoyun’s eyes widened with surprise after hearing this.","\"I hear that despite being the highest-ranking in the military, he’s rarely seen,\" she said a moment later.","\"Do you want to see him? He’ll be at the Parade Deck in an hour.\"","Mei Xiaoyun pondered for a moment before nodding her head, as she was too curious about the Supreme General to pass such an opportunity.","Thus, the two of them made their way to the Parade Deck together.","As they walked, Mei Xiaoyun asked, \"Any progress with the squad? Or am I still the only member?\"","\"Uh... I haven’t really had the time to recruit anyone, but I will definitely prioritize it once I return from this mission,\" said Yuan.","\"Is that so? Quite frankly, it’s better to take things slow since it’s more important to find people that we can trust.\"","\"Don’t worry, I don’t intend on inviting just anyone to the squad.\"","\"Good to know.\"","Eventually, they arrived at the Parade Deck—or at least, they were about to enter the area when they encountered a line of soldiers blocking the path.","\"The Parade Deck is closed today,\" one of the soldiers informed them.","\"I’m Sergeant Yuan, and I am supposed to show up at the Parade Deck for a mission.\"","\"Please give me a moment to verify.\"","The soldier retrieved a list of names, and after he verified Yuan’s name was on it, he nodded and said, \"You may enter.\"","He then turned to look at Mei Xiaoyun, seemingly waiting for her to identify herself.","\"I’m not on the mission,\" she admitted.","\"Then you won’t be able to enter.\"","Mei Xiaoyun calmly nodded.","\"Looks like I’ll have to wait for another chance to see the Supreme General,\" she turned to Yuan and said.","\"Sorry.\"","\"It’s fine. Whatever you’re doing, stay safe.\"","\"I will.\"","Yuan continued making his way to the Parade Deck while Mei Xiaoyun turned around and walked in the opposite direction.","A few minutes later, Yuan arrived at the Parade Deck.","The Parade Deck was usually crowded with soldiers who’d go there to socialize or train, but today, it was basically completely empty.","\"I was beginning to worry that you might not be able to participate in the mission,\" said the Ironwoman when she noticed him.","\"So, what happened? Are you good?\" she then asked.","Yuan shook his head and explained, \"I don’t know. They allowed me to go without saying anything. General Mei said it’s too suspicious and that they might be up to something.\"","\"That definitely does sound suspicious,\" she muttered.","While Ironwoman fell silent in thought, Yuan shifted his attention to the other two individuals standing not far away on the Parade Deck.","He recognized one of them as the Colonel who had lasted the third longest during the drill.","The other, however, he didn’t recognize in the slightest, and he was a Major just like the Ironwoman.","\"Who are they?\" Yuan asked.","\"Colonel Gu and Major Gu.\"","\"...Are you serious?\" Yuan looked at her with a dumbfounded face.","\"Yes, I am serious.\"","Yuan shook his head and sighed, \"Just how big is their family?\"","\"Big enough to have at least one ’Gu’ in every single rank,\" she said.","\"Honestly, I’m impressed.\"","Suddenly, the two of them began walking in Yuan’s direction.","\"Are you sure you’re in the right place, Sergeant Yuan?\" Major Gu asked once they stopped a few meters away.","Before Yuan could respond, Colonel Gu spoke, \"I heard you got arrested recently. By the Extractors, no less.\"","\"Indeed, I was arrested. But as you can see, I am free, so it was just a misunderstanding.\"","\"That’s not what I heard,\" remarked Colonel Gu.","\"Oh? Then what did you hear?\"","\"Don’t worry about it,\" Colonel Gu said, his lips curling into a cold grin.","\"...\"","Yuan and Colonel Gu silently stared at each other, neither willing to look away as the atmosphere between them gradually grew cold and heavy.","\"You...\" Colonel Gu opened his mouth to speak, but stopped when several powerful presences suddenly appeared on the Parade Deck.","Yuan and the others immediately turned toward the source and saw a group of seven soldiers, six in black outfits that looked more like armor than suits, their faces completely concealed behind full helmets.","As for the seventh individual, he was a healthy-looking old man with long white hair and a neatly trimmed beard. Unlike the others, he wore a white outfit that was adorned with medals and three distinct crimson stars.","\"We greet the Supreme General.\"","The Ironwoman and the two from the Gu Family saluted.","When Yuan saw this, he quickly followed and saluted him.","\"At ease,\" said the Supreme General.","\"It’s been a while, Ironwoman. How’s General Mei doing these days?\" he said a moment later.","\"The same as usual,\" she calmly replied.","\"That’s good to hear. I’ve been wanting to visit her, but my schedule was too full, and just as I was about to go on a break, I had this assembly shoved down my throat. I really cannot wait until my retirement,\" he sighed aloud.","The Supreme General glanced at Colonel Gu and Major Gu, but his gaze lingered on them for barely half a second before shifting to Yuan, not even bothering to acknowledge their presence.","\"Sergeant Yuan... I’ve heard quite a lot about you. Despite being a relatively new soldier, your achievements have been nothing short of astonishing. In fact, some of your achievements are so unbelievable that even now, I find them difficult to believe.\"","The Supreme General openly praised Yuan, which irritated Colonel Gu and Major Gu even more than being ignored."]},{"number":2664,"title":"Chapter 2664: Supreme General(2)","paragraphs":["\"Anyway, although I would like to talk more, we need to set out for the assembly immediately, as we’re already running behind schedule. We’ll talk more during the journey,\" said the Supreme General before he turned to look at one of his soldiers and gave a silent nod.","The next moment, the soldier retrieved a palm-sized object and tossed it into the air.","Just as it reached the peak of its ascent, the object rapidly expanded, transforming into a full-sized ship roughly as large as two buses placed side by side.","The ship also did not descend and remained in the air, hovering in place.","’A flying treasure, huh?’ Yuan thought to himself.","This was his first time seeing one in this world, not including the flying hoverboards he’d seen before, since they were essentially flying swords in his eyes.","Without a word, the Supreme General and the others jumped aboard the flying treasure.","\"You don’t look surprised at all, as if you’d seen it before,\" the Ironwoman remarked as she gazed at his face.","Flying treasures were exceedingly rare in this world and couldn’t be purchased with money, as they were considered property of the city itself.","Naturally, this meant that the flying treasure before them didn’t belong to the Supreme General personally; he had merely been granted permission to use it for the mission.","\"Perhaps I have,\" Yuan responded with a smile before jumping onto it.","Once everyone was aboard the flying treasure, the controller activated it. However, instead of flying forward like an ordinary vessel, it tore open the void and entered directly into it, traveling through the void itself.","Yet, the flying treasure remained within the void for only a few seconds before returning to the surface. By the time it emerged, they were already several hundred miles beyond the city walls.","Yuan initially assumed the flying treasure needed some time to recover before it could enter the void again. However, it continued flying normally afterward without doing so.","\"Is this flying treasure incapable of traveling through the void continuously? It would make traveling much faster if it could,\" he asked Ironwoman.","\"Do you have any idea how much energy that consumes? We only use that function when entering or leaving the city, or in a life-or-death situation,\" Ironwoman replied.","\"That sounds... a little strange. Why can’t it just fly in and out of the city normally?\"","\"Because this flying treasure has built-in functions that block all forms of surveillance. Unfortunately, those same functions also interfere with nearby signals, so flying it through the city normally would cause too much disruption. Also, it doesn’t use much energy to leave the city. Using it to travel to the assembly is an entirely different story.\"","Yuan looked around and then said, \"Are we not worried about the Void Hunter? We have eleven people here, so there’s a chance for it to appear.\"","\"Another special feature of this flying treasure is that it completely conceals our presence, so as far as the outside world is concerned, we essentially don’t exist. In other words, the Void Hunter won’t appear,\" she quickly explained.","\"And how certain are you that it actually works that way, rather than simply having been lucky so far?\"","\"...\"","The Ironwoman fell silent, as she was unable to answer his question with certainty.","\"Don’t worry. The Void Hunter won’t appear. We’ve conducted extensive research on this, including tests with over a hundred people aboard for months at a time. If we combined the duration of every test we’ve conducted, it would amount to decades,\" the Supreme General suddenly said.","Yuan turned his head to see the Supreme General approaching them.","\"Let’s continue our conversation, shall we?\" he added.","\"I wouldn’t consider that a conversation,\" Yuan remarked with a smile.","\"Well, you’re not wrong. In any case, follow me. I have a few questions for you.\"","Without waiting for a response, the Supreme General turned around and walked toward the rear of the ship, where a single private room was located.","Yuan quietly followed him into the room.","Once inside, the Supreme General sat behind a small desk and gestured toward the seat across from him, where Yuan sat down.","However, even after several moments had passed, the Supreme General remained silent, merely staring at Yuan with an intense, unreadable gaze.","\"So, what did you want to talk to me about?\" Yuan asked, breaking the silence.","\"I’ll get straight to the point...\"","The Supreme General spoke in a cold, serious tone, his demeanor so different from before that he seemed like an entirely different person.","\"Who are you? Where did you come from? And why are you in our city?\"","Despite the sudden and drastic shift in the Supreme General, Yuan remained calm as he responded, \"I don’t understand.\"","\"Did you really think I wouldn’t look into your profile? Not only is your history completely blank until just a few months before you joined the military, but you even possess the Perfected Heavenly Refinement physique—something General Mei deliberately concealed from the military!\"","The Supreme General continued, \"I am also aware of your recent arrest and the reason behind it.\"","\"Is it a crime to possess the Perfected Heavenly Refinement physique?\" Yuan asked.","\"No, but your existence is far too suspicious not to raise any alarms. I’ve lived for many, many years and seen countless things, yet none of them compare to the anomaly that is you.\"","\"...\"","Yuan fell silent as he contemplated how he should respond to the Supreme General.","The Supreme General realized this and did not rush him to answer.","After some consideration, Yuan responded, \"To answer your questions... I am Yuan, and I am from another world. As for my purpose in this city... I wish to meet Gaia.\"","The Supreme General’s eyes widened, looking dazed by his response.","\"You are from another world? Are you admitting to being a Celestial Being?\" he then asked.","Yuan chuckled, \"Me? A Celestial Being? Of course not. I am human.\""]}]);
